window.COURSE = {"title":"B1 revised scripts — six lessons (English)","version":"3.6.0-b1-reviewed-2026-10-07","documents":{"DOC-REQ":{"title":"NDT request (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Request / job reference (fictional: TS-V2)","Planned examination (day only, no calendar date)","Site / contact role (client's maintenance manager — Bram)","Component / drawing and weld IDs (vessel V-2; welds W-07, W-08; drawing V2-GA rev C)","Material (carbon steel)","Thickness / dimensions (12 mm / 1 200 mm — fictional sample values)","Examination extent (100 % of both welds)","NDT method (RT)","Examination technique standard (ISO 17636-2:2022, digital detectors)","Acceptance criteria (ISO 10675-1:2021; level per fictional project specification PS-V2 §6.5)","Attachments","Responsibility / confirmation (role only, no signature)"],"rules":"No default-standard fallback; method standard, acceptance criteria and legal justification are separate fields."},"DOC-TECH-JUST":{"title":"Justification of the technique (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Job / type of assignment (vessel V-2 shell welds, repair)","3a — Standard issued by a recognised standardisation organisation requiring radiography for this type of assignment: 'none identified'","3b — Contractual / project requirement: fictional PS-V2 rev C §6.3 'All circumferential butt welds in pressure-retaining shell plates shall be examined by radiographic testing over 100 % of their length.' (fictional teaching document — not a standard)","3c — Risk analysis of undetected fabrication defects: attached; RT selected for these welds (summary only, no values)","Prepared by (role: client's welding/NDT engineer — competent in NDT techniques)","Attachments"],"rules":"The selected legal route is 3c (KB IR art 3 §2); 3b alone never suffices; nothing is quoted from a real standard."},"DOC-LOC-JUST":{"title":"Justification of the irradiation location (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Workpiece / context (installed vessel on saddles; not movable)","Bunker — assessed: dismantling and transport for two repair welds assessed and rejected (reasons recorded) → not reasonably feasible","Irradiation infrastructure — none present; arranging fixed shielding around the vessel for these welds assessed (access on three sides only, crane traffic, duration) → not reasonably feasible","Conclusion for this type of assignment: another place (the hall), after risk analyses by client and company","Client's risk-analysis information for the company (hall occupancy, walkways, store behind the hall, crane use)","Associated evidence / attachments"],"rules":"Immobility, absence of infrastructure or ownership alone are never the stated reason; no transitional flowchart branch."},"DOC-LICENCE":{"title":"Establishment and operating licence — teaching excerpt","pages":2,"fields":["Authorised establishment / practice (industrial radiography in the company bunker and on clients' sites)","Installations covered","Equipment scope / inventory (placeholders, no numeric inventory)","Sources (placeholders)","Conditions","Evidence fields (acceptance, security acceptance where applicable)"],"rules":"Placeholders instead of real reference numbers; not blanket evidence that a job, site or person is ready."},"DOC-CERT-BUNKER":{"title":"Bunker conformity certificate — teaching excerpt","pages":1,"fields":["Description of the bunker and its location on the site","Permitted isotopes / maximum activity; maximum X-ray voltage and current (placeholders)","Permitted working configurations","Safety-logic reference (document with electrical diagram — referenced, not shown)","Validity (maximum 10 years)","Drawn up by: recognised expert in physical control (role only)"],"rules":"No stamp, signature, number or shielding dimension; this example has a roof; no universal roof rule."},"DOC-EXT-WORKER-FILE":{"title":"Pre-assignment information — external worker (teaching sample)","pages":2,"fields":["Page 1 — Sending employer: name / establishment unit / enterprise number (placeholders)","Page 1 — Worker: first name Clara; other identity fields as placeholders","Page 2 — Doses, last five calendar years, per year: 'provided' ×5","Page 2 — Doses, last twelve rolling months with monitoring period: 'NOT PROVIDED'","Page 2 — Non-uniform exposure / internal contamination: none declared","Page 2 — Assignment abroad: not applicable","Instruction / assignment scope (added by the operator): bunker and bunker X-ray set"],"rules":"'provided' / 'not provided' / placeholders only; a missing section is an evidence gap, not zero dose."},"DOC-AGREEMENT":{"title":"Signed agreement — external undertaking and operator (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Parties (roles only)","Clause A — Individual dosimetric monitoring and transfer of results to the exposure register: external undertaking","Clause B — Personal protective equipment: external undertaking","Clause C — Specific training on the controlled area and task: operator (not allocated)","Signature area: illustrative placeholders, no names"],"rules":"Allocates only what it names."},"DOC-CHECK-SHEET":{"title":"Pre-use check sheet — current version (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Instrument / device","Function check result","Date","Checked by (role)","Ambiguous sentence: 'Check the meter's response before/after positioning the device' (the sentence Daniel proposes to clarify)"],"rules":"The proposed revision sits beside it marked PROPOSED — not approved."},"DOC-CERT-AGENT":{"title":"Agent-course certificate (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Holder: Daniel","Theoretical training — knowledge test passed","Training body (placeholder)","Date (placeholder)"],"rules":"Proves the passed knowledge test only."},"DOC-PLANNING":{"title":"Worksite planning sheet (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Worksite / day","Team","Designated radiation protection agent (line)","Equipment","Client contact person"],"rules":"Designation is a recorded company decision."},"DOC-CONTROL-TEST-PROGRAMME":{"title":"Control and test programme — bunker safety devices (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Device: door interlock","Columns: Result · Date · Tested by","Previous month: satisfactory · date · name (placeholders)","This month: — · — · — (empty)"],"rules":"Result, date and operator name as KB IR art 15 §4 requires."},"DOC-HOLD-CARD":{"title":"Hold card (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["BUNKER USE ON HOLD","Reason: this month's interlock test result not established","Placed by (role) / informed (roles)"],"rules":"The visible held-work state; not tiny status text."},"DOC-CHANGE-REGISTER":{"title":"Change register of the physical control service (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Change description (additional X-ray set, type not in licence inventory)","Approvals given / still needed (expert countersignature; Agency decision)","Implementation status (proposal)"],"rules":"Per TR 6 Dec 2021 art 10; not every change shares one signature route."},"DOC-EVENT-RECORD":{"title":"Event account / handover record (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Observation (time, place, equipment, what happened)","Work / protective status","Contacted — and whether contact succeeded","Unknowns (cause; dose)"],"rules":"Unknowns are never converted into a cause, a dose or a permission."},"DOC-NOTIFICATION":{"title":"Written notification to the Agency — teaching sample (initial)","pages":1,"fields":["What / where / when; when discovered","Equipment and sources involved","Actual consequences incl. doses where known — 'dose under assessment'","Suspected causes (labelled suspected)","Urgent measures taken","Who manages the event","Physician follow-up / proposed INES level where applicable","Notifier (role)"],"rules":"Facts known at that moment; no zero for an unknown."},"DOC-CRITERION-EXTRACT":{"title":"Criterion extract — significant events (teaching card)","pages":1,"fields":["Criterion 1.5 — loss or failure of equipment fulfilling a safety function: direct contact by the next working day; INES evaluation yes","Criterion 1.4 — non-compliance with / unsuitable safety logic leading or possibly leading to unforeseen behaviour: direct contact immediately; INES evaluation yes","Written notification within 48 h for every event meeting a criterion","Source and date of the extract"],"rules":"Learning card; the procedure holds the complete current table."},"DOC-ASSIGNMENT-SLIP":{"title":"Changed assignment slip (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Worker: Clara","Requested: assist with gamma exposures, hall two, this afternoon","Requested by (role)"],"rules":"Shown beside the instruction record."},"DOC-INSTRUCTION-RECORD":{"title":"Specific instruction record — Clara (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Area: company bunker","Equipment: bunker X-ray set","Task: X-ray radiography of castings","Given by (role) / date (placeholder)"],"rules":"Scope is the evidence; a different area/equipment/task is outside it."},"DOC-PLANNER":{"title":"Job planner — week view (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Tuesday: client request received; written justifications received","Wednesday: company risk analysis completed; planning","Thursday (current day): worksite — vessel V-2, welds W-07/W-08"],"rules":"Current day clearly marked; plays automatically, not an exercise."},"DOC-SITE-PLAN":{"title":"Site drawing — client's hall (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Vessel V-2 position","Protection perimeter line (conceptual; no distances)","Walkway route (agreed) and changed route","Store behind the hall","Gate","Supervision positions"],"rules":"Conceptual planning drawing; no exclusion distances or dose values."},"DOC-FINAL-REPORT":{"title":"Final report — teaching sample (structure only)","pages":1,"fields":["Established causes","Doses","Detailed description","Preventive measures / lessons learned / action plan","Approvals where applicable (recognised expert; class 7 safety adviser)"],"rules":"Structure only; no content invented for the case."},"DOC-REG-EXTRACT":{"title":"Regulation extract page (teaching reader)","pages":1,"fields":["Article reference and short verbatim extract (Dutch) with English gloss"],"rules":"Used in the B1.1 exploration and reference readers."},"DOC-PROCEDURE-RECORD":{"title":"Approved procedure page with its approval line, and a record line (teaching sample)","pages":1,"fields":["Procedure title and version","Approved by: recognised expert (role)","Record line: what was checked · result · date · by whom"],"rules":"Procedure = method; record = evidence of a check on a day."}},"lessons":[{"id":"B1.1","title":"Getting started: radiation protection in Belgian industry","scenes":[{"id":"S01","title":"Welcome to the course","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S01-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Welcome to your radiation protection training. I'm Emilia, and I'll be your guide. Your own health, and the safety of the people around you, are at the heart of this course. By the end of it you will recognise where radiation risks arise in industrial work, know which responsibilities and checks apply before a job starts, and know when to stop and ask for help. We build that step by step, with examples from Belgian industry, and three principles will return in every example: justification, optimisation and dose limitation.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Approved Emilia beside the original cream, teal and gold illustration: trefoil connected to a balance, exposure-reduction shield and bounded dial. All visible from the start; no workplace photo.","beats":[{"at":"Welcome to your radiation protection training.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"I'm Emilia, and I'll be your guide.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"By the end of it you will recognise where radiation risks ar","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"We build that step by step, with examples from Belgian indus","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"equipment":[],"characters":["Emilia"],"clip":"B1.1-S01-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S01-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"I work for an industrial radiography company, and that is the company we'll follow in this course. There, I lead the physical control service: the organised radiation-protection function of the company, the people, the checks and the procedures that keep exposure under control. You will meet my colleagues as they work: Daniel preparing an inspection, Clara arriving with her file, and Bram arranging a job at his site. Through their decisions we connect the Belgian rules with the information and the equipment in front of us.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Emilia introduces herself beside the principles illustration, with her name and role. No other participant is shown until named.","beats":[{"at":"I work for an industrial radiography company, and that is th","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"There, I lead the physical control service: the organised ra","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"You will meet my colleagues as they work: Daniel preparing a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Through their decisions we connect the Belgian rules with th","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"documents":["DOC-REQ"],"characters":["Emilia","Daniel","Clara","Bram"],"clip":"B1.1-S01-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S01-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"We start with the framework and the people: who is responsible for what, and why protection has to be settled before work begins. Later lessons build the physics and apply it to more detailed situations. Take the course at your own pace: pause, replay an explanation, and keep your own notes. The practice questions along the way help you understand the decisions; they are not scored, and the final assessment is separate.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"A clean three-stop course route appears beside Emilia; stop 1 active.","beats":[{"at":"We start with the framework and the people: who is responsib","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Later lessons build the physics and apply it to more detaile","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Take the course at your own pace: pause, replay an explanati","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The practice questions along the way help you understand the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S01-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S01-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Before we begin, let me be clear about what this course is and what it is not. It gives you the theory: the knowledge you need if you work with radioactive sources or X-ray generators in Belgian class II industry. What it cannot give you is the rest: hands-on experience, instruction on the actual installation you'll use, and the responsibilities your employer assigns to you. Those come from your workplace. So when you finish these lessons, you'll understand the decisions; being appointed to a function, or allowed to use a particular piece of equipment, is a separate step that your company takes.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Emilia to camera; route fades to the two labels.","beats":[{"at":"Before we begin, let me be clear about what this course is a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"It gives you the theory: the knowledge you need if you work ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Those come from your workplace.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"So when you finish these lessons, you'll understand the deci","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S01-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S01-P1","B1.1-S01-P2","B1.1-S01-P3","B1.1-S01-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S02","title":"Where the course will take you","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S02-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Here is the road ahead, so you know where each lesson fits. The foundations come in three stages. The first stage is the one we're in now: the Belgian framework and the people who make it work. We start here, and not with the physics, for a simple reason: every protective measure you'll ever meet is a decision taken by someone with a responsibility, and you need to know who those people are before the rules make sense.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"One continuous three-part course route, with Framework and people active and the Belgian-framework illustration and summary visible.","beats":[{"at":"Here is the road ahead, so you know where each lesson fits.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The foundations come in three stages.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The first stage is the one we're in now: the Belgian framewo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"We start here, and not with the physics, for a simple reason","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S02-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S02-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The second stage is radiation itself: where it comes from, how it behaves, and what the different quantities actually measure. That is where words you already hear at work, dose, dose rate, activity, get their precise meaning. With those ideas in place, shielding, exposure, biological effects and personal dosimetry stop being separate topics and become one story: how radiation reaches a person, what it does, and how we keep it low.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Continue in part 2 without restarting the route. Show Instruments and safety checks.","beats":[{"at":"The second stage is radiation itself: where it comes from, h","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"That is where words you already hear at work, dose, dose rat","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"With those ideas in place, shielding, exposure, biological e","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.1-S02-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S02-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The third stage brings you to the equipment and the routines: the instruments you measure with, the safety checks you perform, and the way sources and contamination are handled day to day. From there, the class II modules take the foundations into more demanding situations: the authorised activity, equipment and safety systems, radioactive sources, more precise measurements, worksite arrangements and transport, and the response when something unusual happens. We won't ask you to solve all of that today; each module gives you something the next one can use.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Part 3 active from the first word; show the additional class II modules as applied knowledge.","beats":[{"at":"The third stage brings you to the equipment and the routines","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"From there, the class II modules take the foundations into m","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"We won't ask you to solve all of that today; each module giv","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.1-S02-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S02-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Each part of the course is taught by a colleague whose own work fits the subject, so you hear the physics from someone who measures, and the routines from someone who performs them. For this first module I stay with you from start to finish, so that we can build on our conversation from one lesson to the next, and so that the people you meet today, Daniel, Clara and Bram, are still the same people when the situations become harder.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"A distinct four-part learning flow, not the course route again. Explanation, workplace example, decision and feedback stay visible.","beats":[{"at":"Each part of the course is taught by a colleague whose own w","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"For this first module I stay with you from start to finish, ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.1-S02-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S02-P1","B1.1-S02-P2","B1.1-S02-P3","B1.1-S02-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S03","title":"Who protects whom? The Belgian system","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Let's begin with the people and organisations responsible for radiation protection in Belgium, starting from the outside. FANC is the Federal Agency for Nuclear Control: the public authority that regulates and supervises nuclear safety and radiation protection, with one purpose: to protect workers, the public and the environment from ionising radiation. For an industrial radiography company, FANC is the regulator. It grants the authorisations we need, it sets the rules, and through its inspections it checks that we comply. The protection itself is organised inside the company, by the people you'll meet next.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"FANC name and official logo","beats":[{"at":"Let's begin with the people and organisations responsible fo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"FANC is the Federal Agency for Nuclear Control: the public a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"It grants the authorisations we need, it sets the rules, and","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The protection itself is organised inside the company, by th","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"equipment":["EQ-FANC-LOGO"],"characters":["Emilia"],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P1","documents":[]},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now step inside the company. Ours is an NDT company. NDT stands for non-destructive testing: we check whether a weld, a casting or a pipe is sound without cutting it open or damaging it. One way to do that is industrial radiography: we send X-rays or gamma rays through the part onto a detector, and the image shows cracks, voids or inclusions hidden inside the metal. That is why we work with X-ray generators and sealed radioactive sources, and why radiation protection is part of our daily work. A company that does this needs a licence for it. In the regulation the licence holder is called the operator, and the law places the responsibility for radiation protection squarely on the operator. To carry that responsibility, every operator must organise a physical control service, the service I introduced at the start. \"Physical\" here refers to the physics of radiation: the service controls exposure, from the equipment to the worksite. The health of the workers themselves is followed separately, through medical surveillance by a recognised physician.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Company frame highlighted; the word 'operator' appears on the frame.","beats":[{"at":"Now step inside the company.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"One way to do that is industrial radiography: we send X-rays","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"In the regulation the licence holder is called the operator,","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The health of the workers themselves is followed separately,","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"This is where I fit in. I am the head of that service. I coordinate and organise its work, and I have direct access to the head of the company: if a responsibility is unclear, or an issue needs to reach management, the organisation has to let me take it there. Beside my function stands another one, the recognised expert in physical control, and in a moment you'll see why I keep the two apart.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Emilia steps into the service area of the scene (supplied pose: standing, open hand).","beats":[{"at":"This is where I fit in.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"I am the head of that service.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"I coordinate and organise its work, and I have direct access","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Beside my function stands another one, the recognised expert","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The regulation reserves certain tasks for a recognised expert in physical control: a person who holds an individual recognition from FANC for a defined scope of work. Why an expert with a formal recognition? Because some judgements, whether a risk analysis is sound, whether a procedure gives enough protection, whether an installation may be put into service, must rest on expertise that the regulator has verified. A company may employ such an expert; ours does not. So, as the regulation requires, we have a contract with a recognised physical-control organisation: a specialist service provider, itself recognised by FANC, which carries out those expert tasks for us.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Company-to-organisation contract","beats":[{"at":"The regulation reserves certain tasks for a recognised exper","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Why an expert with a formal recognition?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"A company may employ such an expert; ours does not.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"So, as the regulation requires, we have a contract with a re","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P4","characters":["Emilia"],"documents":[]},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P5","speaker":"Emilia","clip":"B1.1-S03-P5","text":"Two things are easy to blend, so let me name them separately. The organisation is the service provider: it holds a recognition and keeps meeting its conditions. The expert is a person employed by it, with her own individual recognition. In our arrangement, that expert performs the reserved tasks for our company: she examines and approves our radiation-protection risk analysis and our working procedures, for example. I coordinate our service; she brings the formally recognised expertise; and both of us work under FANC's supervision.","start_visual":"Individual expert inside the recognised organisation","beats":[{"at":"Two things are easy to blend, so let me name them separately","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The organisation is the service provider: it holds a recogni","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"In our arrangement, that expert performs the reserved tasks ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"I coordinate our service; she brings the formally recognised","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"screen_text":[],"characters":["Emilia"],"documents":[]},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P6","speaker":"Emilia","clip":"B1.1-S03-P6","text":"What does that look like in practice? The expert comes to our company for periodic evaluation visits, to see how radiation protection and safety actually work, and not only how they are written down. Depending on the visit, she examines equipment and safety devices, reviews dosimetry results and staff training, and checks our procedures and working arrangements. In industrial radiography that can include our own premises and observations at a customer's worksite; the exact scope follows from our activities and from the visit itself. Her job, in one sentence, is to connect what our records say with what happens where people work.","start_visual":"Why visit: evaluate radiation protection in practice","beats":[{"at":"What does that look like in practice?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The expert comes to our company for periodic evaluation visi","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"In industrial radiography that can include our own premises ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Her job, in one sentence, is to connect what our records say","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"screen_text":[],"characters":["Emilia"],"documents":[]},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P7","speaker":"Emilia","clip":"B1.1-S03-P7","text":"After the visit, the company receives a written evaluation report. It records the findings and identifies the actions we have to take, each with a deadline. A report can grade how serious an issue is and show which actions are still open and which have been closed. The follow-up is mine to coordinate: we read the findings, carry out the required actions, and report back to the expert on what we have done. The organisation, in turn, has its own duties towards FANC. That is what gives the visit its weight: the expert's findings carry through into our records and, where needed, to the regulator.","start_visual":"Teaching report: findings, actions, deadlines and status","beats":[{"at":"After the visit, the company receives a written evaluation r","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"A report can grade how serious an issue is and show which ac","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The follow-up is mine to coordinate: we read the findings, c","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"That is what gives the visit its weight: the expert's findin","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"screen_text":[],"characters":["Emilia"],"documents":[]},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P8","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now the people in the field: the industrial radiographers, sometimes called RT technicians, who actually carry out the radiography. In industrial radiography their training is built in. Every radiographer follows the training for radiation protection agents early in their employment, and only a radiographer who has followed it may operate gamma or X-ray equipment. So every radiographer is trained as an agent: one group of people, with two names for two sides of their work.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Daniel in the hall area of the scene with his handheld instrument.","beats":[{"at":"Now the people in the field: the industrial radiographers, s","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"In industrial radiography their training is built in.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Every radiographer follows the training for radiation protec","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"So every radiographer is trained as an agent: one group of p","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"equipment":["EQ-HANDHELD-SURVEY","EQ-EPD-LEFT-CHEST","EQ-TLD-RIGHT-UPPER-CHEST"],"characters":["Daniel"],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P8"},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P9","speaker":"Emilia","text":"On a worksite, the company goes one step further. From the trained radiographers present who belong to our own staff, it designates one as the radiation protection agent for that worksite. For those tasks, the agent works under our service. His job is the frequent, systematic checking of everyday protection: that the protection rules and work procedures are being followed; that the protective equipment, the instruments and the dosimeters are available, working and used correctly; and that any abnormal situation reaches me and the recognised expert. He does those checks according to instructions and procedures that the recognised expert has approved, which is how the expert's judgement reaches the worksite without the expert standing there.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Planning sheet DOC-PLANNING close-up: the 'designated agent' line with Daniel's name for Thursday.","beats":[{"at":"On a worksite, the company goes one step further.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"From the trained radiographers present who belong to our own","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"His job is the frequent, systematic checking of everyday pro","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"He does those checks according to instructions and procedure","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"documents":["DOC-PLANNING","DOC-CHECK-SHEET","DOC-PROCEDURE-RECORD"],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P9"},{"cue":"B1.1-S03-P10","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now connect the roles, and notice that they form a circle rather than a ladder. FANC regulates and supervises from outside. Our company organises radiation protection and remains responsible for it. I coordinate our service. The recognised organisation provides the recognised expert, who evaluates our protection and performs the examinations and approvals reserved for her. And on every worksite a designated agent checks and reports, under procedures the expert approved. The company keeps its responsibility alongside the expert's contract, and every radiographer keeps his own duties alongside the designated agent.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Regulator supervises","beats":[{"at":"Now connect the roles, and notice that they form a circle ra","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Our company organises radiation protection and remains respo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The recognised organisation provides the recognised expert, ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The company keeps its responsibility alongside the expert's ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S03-P10","characters":["Emilia"],"documents":[]}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S03-P1","B1.1-S03-P2","B1.1-S03-P3","B1.1-S03-P4","B1.1-S03-P5","B1.1-S03-P6","B1.1-S03-P7","B1.1-S03-P8","B1.1-S03-P9","B1.1-S03-P10"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S04","title":"The expert's report lands on my desk","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S04-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The recognised expert visited us last week, and this morning her evaluation report is on my desk. One of her actions reads: the working procedure for setting up a worksite has to be revised, because it no longer matches the way our teams actually work. She has set a date by which she wants to see it done. Nothing dramatic: exactly the kind of finding a good visit produces.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Expert visit: assess protection in practice","beats":[{"at":"The recognised expert visited us last week, and this morning","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"One of her actions reads: the working procedure for setting ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"She has set a date by which she wants to see it done.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Nothing dramatic: exactly the kind of finding a good visit p","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S04-P1","characters":["Emilia"],"documents":[]},{"cue":"B1.1-S04-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Within an hour I have heard three opinions. Our managing director: \"We pay that organisation, let them write it.\" Luc, our most experienced radiographer: \"I know how it should read; I'll change it this afternoon and the teams can start using it.\" And Daniel, new to all of this, asking me which of the two is right. Think about who is responsible, who drafts, who approves, and when a procedure may be used.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Daniel considers the purpose of the visit","beats":[{"at":"Within an hour I have heard three opinions.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Our managing director: \"We pay that organisation, let them w","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Think about who is responsible, who drafts, who approves, an","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"}],"documents":[],"equipment":["EQ-FANC-LOGO"],"clip":"B1.1-S04-P2","characters":["Emilia"]}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S04-Q01","type":"single_choice","title_visible":"Who does what to close this action?","prompt_spoken_once":"Who does what to close this action properly?","situation_visible_text":"The expert's report asks us to revise the worksite set-up procedure by a set date. The director wants the organisation to write it. Luc wants to change it himself this afternoon.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The recognised organisation writes the new procedure and issues it to the teams; that is the service we pay for.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"We do pay the organisation, and its expert will have a real part in this, just not the one the director has in mind. The procedure describes how our company works, and the responsibility for our protection stays with the company; so the drafting is ours, with the people who do the work. What the expert brings is the examination and the approval: she checks whether our revised procedure gives enough protection, and only after her approval do our agents work on the basis of it.","screen":"The company drafts the procedure; the expert examines and approves it; the company stays responsible."},"clip":"B1.1-S04-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Our company revises the procedure, the recognised expert examines and approves it, and only then do the teams work with the new version.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. I organise the revision with Luc and the teams, because they know how the work is actually done; that is the company carrying its responsibility. The draft goes to the expert, who examines and approves it, the task the regulation reserves for her. Until she has, the current approved version stays in use, and I report back to her before the deadline so that she can close the action. Three roles, one procedure, and everyone can say which part was theirs.","screen":"The company revises, the expert approves, the teams use the approved version. Until then the current version applies."},"clip":"B1.1-S04-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Luc revises the procedure today and the teams start using it; the expert reviews it at her next visit.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Luc's experience is exactly what the revision needs, and his draft is where I would start. What the draft cannot do yet is govern the work: our agents carry out their checks on the basis of procedures the recognised expert has approved, and a revised text becomes such a procedure only when she has examined and approved it. So the teams keep using the current version, the draft goes to the expert now, and her approval, not her next visit, is what puts it into use.","screen":"A draft is not yet a procedure. The expert approves it first; then the teams use it."},"clip":"B1.1-S04-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S04-Q01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S04-P1","B1.1-S04-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S04-P2","interaction_id":"B1.1-S04-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S05","title":"From Bram's email to a prepared request","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Let me take you to Havenmeer Process Works. Bram is the maintenance manager here; his company runs this workshop, owns the equipment and knows the site. Havenmeer is our client: it asks our company to inspect some welds, and it will have to give us the information only a client can give. Our planning desk prepares the assignment with Bram before any of our radiographers goes to work, and that preparation is where radiation protection begins.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Bram at Havenmeer workshop","beats":[{"at":"Let me take you to Havenmeer Process Works.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Bram is the maintenance manager here; his company runs this ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Havenmeer is our client: it asks our company to inspect some","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Our planning desk prepares the assignment with Bram before a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia","Bram"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"This is the steel vessel Bram wants inspected. The two highlighted rings are welds: they join sections of the vessel wall, and each runs all the way around. On his drawing they are numbered seven and eight. The vessel is one point two metres across and its steel wall is twelve millimetres thick. It is fixed to its supports and connected to pipework, so it stays where it is, which already tells you something about where the radiography will have to happen. Bram will have to explain that later, when he justifies the location.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Both welds highlighted on the vessel","beats":[{"at":"This is the steel vessel Bram wants inspected.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"On his drawing they are numbered seven and eight.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The vessel is one point two metres across and its steel wall","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Bram will have to explain that later, when he justifies the ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia","Bram"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The job starts with an email. Bram writes: could you radiograph two welds on our vessel on Thursday? Please let me know whether this fits your planning. That is a familiar first enquiry, and it opens a conversation. Planning now knows what Bram wants; what it needs next is everything that lets us prepare the inspection properly.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Original short enquiry email","beats":[{"at":"The job starts with an email.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Bram writes: could you radiograph two welds on our vessel on","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"That is a familiar first enquiry, and it opens a conversatio","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Planning now knows what Bram wants; what it needs next is ev","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia","Bram"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"So our planner replies with specific questions. Which welds, and how much of each weld must be examined? Please send a marked drawing, the material, the diameter and the wall thickness, and the examination requirements. We also need the exact location in the workshop, the proposed time, who else works nearby, and a contact person. To make that easy, planning sends Bram an inspection request form that puts those details in one place. Each line on it serves a purpose: the welds and the drawing tell us what to image, the material and thickness tell us how, and the location and the people nearby tell us whom we have to protect.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Planner asks for marked drawing and scope","beats":[{"at":"So our planner replies with specific questions.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Please send a marked drawing, the material, the diameter and","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"We also need the exact location in the workshop, the propose","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Each line on it serves a purpose: the welds and the drawing ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P4"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P5","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bram completes the request and attaches his drawing. Now every row matches something real: weld seven and weld eight, both in carbon steel, with the same diameter and wall thickness. He asks for the full circumference of each weld to be examined. He names the workshop and puts himself down as the contact person, reachable throughout the work, so that there is always someone on his side who can answer, decide and reach his colleagues. The law asks the client for correct written job information at least twenty-four hours before the work. That day is for us: it is the time in which we plan the exposure, mark out the area we keep clear, and agree who watches it.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Bram returns request and marked drawing","beats":[{"at":"Bram completes the request and attaches his drawing.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"He asks for the full circumference of each weld to be examin","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"He names the workshop and puts himself down as the contact p","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"That day is for us: it is the time in which we plan the expo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia","Bram"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P5"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P6","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Planning also sends Bram a justification form. It asks for his reasons for requesting radiography, and for proposing this location, with the information that supports each reason. Bram gathers those answers with colleagues who have the technical knowledge, because the reasons have to hold up, in writing, for this type of job. We will read that justification in the next scenes; for now, notice who receives the form and why planning needs it back before we go further.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Planning sends justification form to client","beats":[{"at":"Planning also sends Bram a justification form.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"It asks for his reasons for requesting radiography, and for ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Bram gathers those answers with colleagues who have the tech","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"We will read that justification in the next scenes; for now,","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P6"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P7","speaker":"Emilia","text":"There is a separate sheet as well: the task risk analysis, often called the TRA. Look at one issue in this workshop: a forklift route passes the vessel, and people use the nearby workbenches. Bram supplies that site information so that his company and ours can coordinate the precautions, and our company assesses the radiation risks on top of it. This sheet is about the hazards while the work is done. The justification form answers a different question, why radiography at all and what a missed defect would mean, and the two stay separate for that reason.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Separate TRA worksheet","beats":[{"at":"There is a separate sheet as well: the task risk analysis, o","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Look at one issue in this workshop: a forklift route passes ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"This sheet is about the hazards while the work is done.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The justification form answers a different question, why rad","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P7"},{"cue":"B1.1-S05-P8","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bram returns the completed request, the marked drawing and the supporting documents. Planning brings the file together for the technical and safety review that follows. The first email has become a job we can assess, and the review is what turns it into a job we can do. Keep that sequence in mind: the client asks, planning clarifies, the client supplies the information, and our company reviews it. Next, we look at the reasoning behind using radiation.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Bram returns a coordinated file","beats":[{"at":"Bram returns the completed request, the marked drawing and t","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Planning brings the file together for the technical and safe","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Keep that sequence in mind: the client asks, planning clarif","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Next, we look at the reasoning behind using radiation.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia","Bram"],"clip":"B1.1-S05-P8"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S05-P1","B1.1-S05-P2","B1.1-S05-P3","B1.1-S05-P4","B1.1-S05-P5","B1.1-S05-P6","B1.1-S05-P7","B1.1-S05-P8"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S06","title":"Three principles working together","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S06-P1","clip":"B1.1-S06-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bram's request is now on our desk. Before we read his justification, let me show you how the three principles I named at the start work together, for ordinary, planned industrial work like this. Justification asks whether using radiation is warranted at all. Optimisation asks how we keep the exposure that remains as low as we reasonably can. Dose limitation sets the boundaries that may never be crossed. Each of the three has its own evidence, and a job is ready only when all three are answered.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Three linked responsibilities around the request","beats":[{"at":"Bram's request is now on our desk.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Justification asks whether using radiation is warranted at a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Optimisation asks how we keep the exposure that remains as l","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Each of the three has its own evidence, and a job is ready o","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S06-P2","clip":"B1.1-S06-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Start with justification. Bram needs reliable information about these welds, because a defect that goes unnoticed could matter for the safety of the vessel. That is the benefit. Using radiation also brings disadvantages, among them a health risk, even at doses that cause no immediate effect, and the benefit has to outweigh them. A competent assessment therefore looks at what information the inspection must deliver and whether another suitable testing technique could deliver it. That reasoning has to be written down, for this type of job, by the people who can judge it; in the next scene we read Bram's.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Benefit: useful weld information","beats":[{"at":"Start with justification.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"That is the benefit.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Using radiation also brings disadvantages, among them a heal","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"That reasoning has to be written down, for this type of job,","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S06-P3","clip":"B1.1-S06-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Suppose the use of radiography is justified. Then optimisation begins: keeping exposure as low as reasonably achievable, taking economic and social factors into account. For this vessel that means examining the practical arrangements before anyone starts. Can shielding be placed between the source and the people around? Can people work farther from the source, or spend less time near it? Can the forklift route and the workbenches be reorganised so that fewer people could be exposed at all? The inspection must still reach the quality the client needs, so the team chooses and verifies the measures under its procedures. And a reasonable improvement is worth making even when the dose would already stay well below a limit.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Shielding considered in the plan","beats":[{"at":"Suppose the use of radiography is justified.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"For this vessel that means examining the practical arrangeme","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Can the forklift route and the workbenches be reorganised so","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"And a reasonable improvement is worth making even when the d","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S06-P4","clip":"B1.1-S06-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Dose limitation answers a different question. For planned work, the applicable limits restrict the dose a person may receive over a specified period, for workers and for members of the public. A worker's record carries over from one assignment to the next: exposure from every job counts towards the same total. So a limit marks the boundary; below it, every exposure still counts and optimisation still applies. Planning and dose monitoring are how we keep that check alive during the work.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Dose limits apply over a defined period","beats":[{"at":"Dose limitation answers a different question.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"For planned work, the applicable limits restrict the dose a ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"So a limit marks the boundary; below it, every exposure stil","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Planning and dose monitoring are how we keep that check aliv","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S06-P5","clip":"B1.1-S06-P5","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now imagine someone answers our planner: \"The dose will be low, so we can go ahead.\" That sentence speaks to the third principle only, and even there it is an expectation, where the check asks for a documented comparison with the applicable limit. It says nothing yet about why radiography is needed for these welds, and nothing about which reasonable measures have been taken. The reverse is just as true: a sound justification still needs good protection. The three parts have to support one another.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Claim: low dose means proceed","beats":[{"at":"Now imagine someone answers our planner: \"The dose will be l","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"It says nothing yet about why radiography is needed for thes","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The reverse is just as true: a sound justification still nee","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The three parts have to support one another.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S06-P6","clip":"B1.1-S06-P6","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bring that back to Bram's vessel. We need a sound reason for using radiation, practical arrangements that reduce exposure, and respect for the applicable dose limits, and each of the three stands on its own evidence, so the file is finished only when all three are. That is the framework for the lessons that follow. First we examine justification and who has to provide it. Then we look more closely at optimisation in preparing the job.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Reason for using radiation","beats":[{"at":"Bring that back to Bram's vessel.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"We need a sound reason for using radiation, practical arrang","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"First we examine justification and who has to provide it.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Then we look more closely at optimisation in preparing the j","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S06-P1","B1.1-S06-P2","B1.1-S06-P3","B1.1-S06-P4","B1.1-S06-P5","B1.1-S06-P6"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S07","title":"Justification: from the request to the work location","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P1","clip":"B1.1-S07-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Let's review Bram's request properly, instead of putting it in the diary. The Belgian Royal Decree of the seventeenth of February, twenty twenty-three, on industrial radiography asks three justification questions for every assignment. Why this examination technique? Why this irradiation location? And why this equipment? The first two belong to the client: Havenmeer gives us its written justification of the technique and of the location, for each type of assignment. The third belongs to us: our company justifies the equipment, and decides whether it can accept the assignment at all. You can open the legal references below as we go.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Three written decisions","beats":[{"at":"Let's review Bram's request properly, instead of putting it ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Why this examination technique?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The first two belong to the client: Havenmeer gives us its w","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"You can open the legal references below as we go.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P2","clip":"B1.1-S07-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"First, why radiography for these welds? Article three gives two routes. The first: a specific industrial standard, issued by a recognised standardisation organisation, requires radiography for this type of assignment; then the client identifies that requirement, standard and clause. The second: where no industrial standard provides for radiography, or the client asks for more than the standard does, the client justifies radiography with a risk analysis of what it would mean if a fabrication defect went undetected. Two documents are easy to mistake for that analysis, so know them: a purchase order that says \"please do X-ray\" tells us what the client wants; a standard that explains how to take a radiograph tells us how to do it well. The justification is the reasoning behind the choice, and that is what we read.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Two routes under article 3","beats":[{"at":"First, why radiography for these welds?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The first: a specific industrial standard, issued by a recog","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The second: where no industrial standard provides for radiog","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The justification is the reasoning behind the choice, and th","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P3","clip":"B1.1-S07-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"In Bram's file, no industrial standard requiring radiography has been identified for these two welds. His project specification asks for radiography, so the second route applies: his reasoned risk analysis. Its subject is a weld that holds pressure: what a missed defect could lead to, and whether another examination technique could give the same assurance. Keep this apart from the task risk assessment about forklifts, access and other workshop hazards: both matter, and they answer different questions. We read the reasoning in the analysis; the label \"project requirement\" on the specification is where that reasoning starts, and the analysis is where it is made.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Bram: risk-analysis route","beats":[{"at":"In Bram's file, no industrial standard requiring radiography","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"His project specification asks for radiography, so the secon","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Keep this apart from the task risk assessment about forklift","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"We read the reasoning in the analysis; the label \"project re","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P4","clip":"B1.1-S07-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Next, where should the work take place? Article four gives a firm rule for small movable workpieces: if the complete workpiece fits within one cubic metre and weighs less than five hundred kilograms, its radiography takes place in a bunker: both conditions together, and the piece has to be movable. Look at this separate small pipe assembly: eighty by sixty by forty centimetres, one hundred and twenty kilograms. It meets the conditions, so it goes to a bunker. Note that we judge the complete workpiece, because the whole piece is what travels, and the short length of weld being examined is only the part we image. Our company also checks that the bunker holds a valid conformity certificate.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Movable complete workpiece","beats":[{"at":"Next, where should the work take place?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Look at this separate small pipe assembly: eighty by sixty b","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"It meets the conditions, so it goes to a bunker.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Our company also checks that the bunker holds a valid confor","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P5","clip":"B1.1-S07-P5","speaker":"Emilia","text":"For a larger or heavier workpiece, a bunker is still the preferred location. Where that is not reasonably feasible, the next option is an irradiation infrastructure at the client's site, after risk analyses by both the client and our company. An irradiation infrastructure is a real facility: fixed shielding built for radiation protection, with the required safety arrangements and supervised entrances; shielding and control, in other words, that stand between the radiation and everyone else. Only when neither a bunker nor such an infrastructure is reasonably feasible may another location be considered, again after both risk analyses. The client records the location justification in writing.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Bunker first","beats":[{"at":"For a larger or heavier workpiece, a bunker is still the pre","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Where that is not reasonably feasible, the next option is an","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Only when neither a bunker nor such an infrastructure is rea","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The client records the location justification in writing.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P6","clip":"B1.1-S07-P6","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now apply that order to Bram's vessel. It is one point two metres across and installed in the workshop; welds seven and eight are part of it, so the vessel as a whole is the workpiece. The file therefore examines dismantling and transporting the vessel to a bunker, and explains why that is not reasonably feasible here. It then examines whether fixed shielding could be provided at the vessel, and explains the outcome. Those two supported assessments are what carry the choice of the hall. Bram supplies the site information; our company reviews the proposed conditions and decides whether it can accept them.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Two welds remain part of the vessel","beats":[{"at":"Now apply that order to Bram's vessel.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The file therefore examines dismantling and transporting the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"It then examines whether fixed shielding could be provided a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Bram supplies the site information; our company reviews the ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P7","clip":"B1.1-S07-P7","speaker":"Emilia","text":"If the hall is justified, the radiation still needs a protected work area. Before the radiography, the team marks out a continuous protection perimeter, using at least barrier tape and ionising-radiation warning signs, with a warning lamp in darkness or poor visibility. Look beyond the vessel: workshop doors, nearby benches and every route into the area are part of the picture. Bram is told where the perimeter will run. The client and our company agree in advance who will supervise it, with extra people wherever the radiographers cannot watch the whole line themselves. The tape marks the boundary; the protection comes from the distance it creates, which is why the one thing that matters is that nobody crosses it. And work outside a bunker is always done by at least two industrial radiographers.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Continuous barrier around work","beats":[{"at":"If the hall is justified, the radiation still needs a protec","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Look beyond the vessel: workshop doors, nearby benches and e","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The client and our company agree in advance who will supervi","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"And work outside a bunker is always done by at least two ind","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P8","clip":"B1.1-S07-P8","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Where that boundary runs follows from a measurement, under article nineteen. The dose rate outside the perimeter is limited according to who is there: ten microsieverts per hour where people work permanently and in adjoining buildings, forty where workstations are only occasionally occupied, because someone who spends the whole day at a bench must be protected more than someone who passes by. Repeated work at the same place must also respect the three-hundred-microsievert yearly constraint for each person who is not occupationally exposed. The team measures at the perimeter during the first exposure or a test exposure and enlarges the area if the reading asks for it. These values are ceilings; optimisation, which we look at next, works below them.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Permanent workplaces and adjoining buildings","beats":[{"at":"Where that boundary runs follows from a measurement, under a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The dose rate outside the perimeter is limited according to ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The team measures at the perimeter during the first exposure","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"These values are ceilings; optimisation, which we look at ne","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P9","clip":"B1.1-S07-P9","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Finally, our company justifies the equipment. Article five prefers an X-ray generator when that is feasible without creating additional risk. Where gamma radiography is used, the isotope's penetrating power has to suit the examination. As head of our physical control service, I make sure that a person competent in the different NDT techniques has justified the technique, the isotope and the activity for each assignment, so the equipment is chosen for the job, with reasons. And if our company cannot accept the client's justification of the technique or of the location, it refuses the assignment.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"X-ray preference with conditions","beats":[{"at":"Finally, our company justifies the equipment.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Article five prefers an X-ray generator when that is feasibl","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"As head of our physical control service, I make sure that a ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"And if our company cannot accept the client's justification ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]},{"cue":"B1.1-S07-P10","clip":"B1.1-S07-P10","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bram's request can now be read as a connected file: a reason for radiography, a supported location choice, our equipment assessment, and agreed protection arrangements; four pieces of evidence, each standing on its own. In the workshop, the required measures and the last-minute risk assessment still have to be in place, and if safe working turns out to be impossible, the radiographers stop and report it immediately. Before we move on to optimisation, let me place three workpieces for you. The small pipe assembly, movable, within the size and under the weight: the bunker. A heavy frame that could be moved but would not fit a bunker: a bunker where reasonably feasible, otherwise an irradiation infrastructure after both risk analyses. Bram's installed vessel: the hall, on the strength of the two assessments we just read. Notice that wall thickness played no part in placing them: it helps us choose the examination technique, and it is not part of the bunker rule.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Connected evidence","beats":[{"at":"Bram's request can now be read as a connected file: a reason","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Before we move on to optimisation, let me place three workpi","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"A heavy frame that could be moved but would not fit a bunker","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Notice that wall thickness played no part in placing them: i","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Emilia"]}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S07-Q01","type":"case_sequence","title_visible":"Who justifies what?","prompt_spoken_once":"Bram calls you about his request. Three of his questions, three answers to choose. Each answer is explained.","cases":[{"id":"case1","title":"The technique","situation_visible_text":"Bram: \"You're the radiography specialists. Can't you simply confirm that these welds need radiography, so I don't have to write anything?\"","prompt_spoken_once":"Bram asks: you are the radiography specialists, can't you simply confirm that these welds need radiography, so he doesn't have to write anything? What do you tell him?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Yes: our head of service confirms the technique for every job, so his written justification is covered by ours.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Our head of service does check every job: she makes sure a competent person justified the technique, isotope and activity. That is our company's verification of a justification that already exists. The justification itself is the client's: for each type of assignment, Bram puts in writing why radiography is the right method, either because a standard from a recognised standardisation organisation requires it, or, as here, through his risk analysis of what an undetected defect would mean. We check his reasoning; we cannot write it for him.","screen":"Our head of service does check every job: she makes sure a competent person justified the technique, isotope and activity. That is our company's verification of a justification that already exists. The justification itself is the client's: for each type of assignment, Bram puts in writing why radiography is the right method, either because a standard from a recognised standardisation organisation requires it, or, as here, through his risk analysis of what an undetected defect would mean. We check his reasoning; we cannot write it for him."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case1-a"},{"id":"b","text":"No: the technique justification is the client's, in writing: a standard that requires radiography, or his risk analysis of undetected defects.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. The decree gives Bram two routes: a specific industrial standard from a recognised standardisation organisation that requires radiography for this type of assignment, or, where no such standard provides for it, a risk analysis of what it would mean if a fabrication defect went undetected in these pressure-holding welds. For his vessel no such standard has been identified, so it is the risk analysis, prepared with people who can judge it. Our part comes afterwards: we verify it, and we refuse the job if we cannot accept it.","screen":"Yes. The decree gives Bram two routes: a specific industrial standard from a recognised standardisation organisation that requires radiography for this type of assignment, or, where no such standard provides for it, a risk analysis of what it would mean if a fabrication defect went undetected in these pressure-holding welds. For his vessel no such standard has been identified, so it is the risk analysis, prepared with people who can judge it. Our part comes afterwards: we verify it, and we refuse the job if we cannot accept it."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case1-b"},{"id":"c","text":"No, but his project specification already says \"all shell welds shall be radiographed\", and that sentence is the justification.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"The specification is a real document and it matters: it tells us what Bram requires of his welds. What it does not contain is the reasoning the decree asks for. A requirement in his own project document is not a standard issued by a recognised standardisation organisation, so it does not open the first route; and it is not a risk analysis, so it does not complete the second. The specification is where Bram's reasoning starts; the risk analysis is where he makes it.","screen":"The specification is a real document and it matters: it tells us what Bram requires of his welds. What it does not contain is the reasoning the decree asks for. A requirement in his own project document is not a standard issued by a recognised standardisation organisation, so it does not open the first route; and it is not a risk analysis, so it does not complete the second. The specification is where Bram's reasoning starts; the risk analysis is where he makes it."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case1-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case1"},{"id":"case2","title":"The location","situation_visible_text":"Bram: \"The vessel is welded in place and we have no bunker, so the hall is the only option. Is that enough for the location?\"","prompt_spoken_once":"Bram says: the vessel is welded in place and we have no bunker, so the hall is the only option. Is that enough for the location? What do you tell him?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Yes: a fixed vessel cannot go to a bunker, so the firm bunker rule does not apply and the hall follows.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Right about the rule: the firm requirement is for small, movable workpieces, and this vessel is neither small nor movable. Outside that rule the decree sets an order, not a free choice: a bunker is still preferred, then an irradiation infrastructure at the site, and only when neither is reasonably feasible another place. Bram's justification has to walk that order with reasons, why dismantling and transport are unreasonable, why fixed shielding at the vessel is not feasible, before the hall is the answer.","screen":"Right about the rule: the firm requirement is for small, movable workpieces, and this vessel is neither small nor movable. Outside that rule the decree sets an order, not a free choice: a bunker is still preferred, then an irradiation infrastructure at the site, and only when neither is reasonably feasible another place. Bram's justification has to walk that order with reasons, why dismantling and transport are unreasonable, why fixed shielding at the vessel is not feasible, before the hall is the answer."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case2-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Yes, as long as our company adds its own risk analysis of the hall to his file.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Our risk analysis is required and we will make it. It answers how we work safely at a place, once that place is justified. Justifying the place is Bram's task, in writing, and the decree asks him for two assessments: whether taking the vessel to a bunker is reasonably feasible, and whether fixed shielding at the vessel is. Both risk analyses, his and ours, then support the hall. His sentence gives the facts; the assessments give the justification.","screen":"Our risk analysis is required and we will make it. It answers how we work safely at a place, once that place is justified. Justifying the place is Bram's task, in writing, and the decree asks him for two assessments: whether taking the vessel to a bunker is reasonably feasible, and whether fixed shielding at the vessel is. Both risk analyses, his and ours, then support the hall. His sentence gives the facts; the assessments give the justification."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case2-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Not yet: his written justification has to assess both the bunker and fixed shielding at the vessel, with reasons, before the hall is justified.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. \"Welded in place\" and \"no bunker on site\" are facts; the justification is the reasoning the decree asks for. Bram's file has to show why dismantling and transport to a bunker are not reasonably feasible, and why an irradiation infrastructure, fixed shielding at the vessel, is not either. With those two assessments in writing, and risk analyses from both companies, the hall is the justified location, and the perimeter and its supervision are planned there.","screen":"Exactly. \"Welded in place\" and \"no bunker on site\" are facts; the justification is the reasoning the decree asks for. Bram's file has to show why dismantling and transport to a bunker are not reasonably feasible, and why an irradiation infrastructure, fixed shielding at the vessel, is not either. With those two assessments in writing, and risk analyses from both companies, the hall is the justified location, and the perimeter and its supervision are planned there."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case2-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case2"},{"id":"case3","title":"The equipment","situation_visible_text":"Bram: \"Will you be using X-rays or a gamma source for my welds? And is that my decision or yours?\"","prompt_spoken_once":"Bram asks: X-rays or a gamma source for his welds, and is that his decision or ours? What do you tell him?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Ours: our company justifies the equipment, preferring an X-ray generator where that is feasible without extra risk, and matching the isotope to the examination where gamma is used.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. The third justification question belongs to our company. The decree prefers an X-ray generator when that is feasible without creating additional risk; where gamma radiography is used, the isotope's penetrating power has to suit the examination. Our head of service makes sure a person competent in the NDT techniques justified the technique, the isotope and the activity for this assignment. Bram hears what we chose and why; the choice and its reasons are ours.","screen":"Yes. The third justification question belongs to our company. The decree prefers an X-ray generator when that is feasible without creating additional risk; where gamma radiography is used, the isotope's penetrating power has to suit the examination. Our head of service makes sure a person competent in the NDT techniques justified the technique, the isotope and the activity for this assignment. Bram hears what we chose and why; the choice and its reasons are ours."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case3-a"},{"id":"b","text":"His: the client justifies technique and location, and the equipment is part of the technique.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Half right: Bram does justify the technique, why radiography, and the location. The equipment is the third, separate question, and the decree gives it to the company doing the work, because it depends on our generators, our sources and our competence. So Bram justifies that radiography is needed and where; we justify what we bring, with a preference for X-rays where feasible without extra risk.","screen":"Half right: Bram does justify the technique, why radiography, and the location. The equipment is the third, separate question, and the decree gives it to the company doing the work, because it depends on our generators, our sources and our competence. So Bram justifies that radiography is needed and where; we justify what we bring, with a preference for X-rays where feasible without extra risk."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case3-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Neither: FANC decides which equipment may be used on a client's site.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"FANC is in the picture, as the regulator that licensed our equipment and can prohibit a location it finds insufficiently justified. The choice of equipment for a given assignment, though, is made by our company, under the decree's rule: X-ray generator where feasible without extra risk, and a suitable isotope where gamma is used, justified by a competent person and checked by our head of service. We decide; FANC supervises.","screen":"FANC is in the picture, as the regulator that licensed our equipment and can prohibit a location it finds insufficiently justified. The choice of equipment for a given assignment, though, is made by our company, under the decree's rule: X-ray generator where feasible without extra risk, and a suitable isotope where gamma is used, justified by a competent person and checked by our head of service. We decide; FANC supervises."},"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case3-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01-case3"}],"clip":"B1.1-S07-Q01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S07-P1","B1.1-S07-P2","B1.1-S07-P3","B1.1-S07-P4","B1.1-S07-P5","B1.1-S07-P6","B1.1-S07-P7","B1.1-S07-P8","B1.1-S07-P9","B1.1-S07-P10"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S07-P10","interaction_id":"B1.1-S07-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S08","title":"Optimisation: protecting people in Bram's hall","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S08-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"We are back in Bram's workshop at Havenmeer. For this example, the reasons for examining the installed vessel here have been accepted. Now we improve the way the job will be done. Optimisation means keeping exposure as low as reasonably achievable, taking economic and social factors into account: looking, below the limits, for every reasonable improvement. Daniel and Sofia are our radiography team. With Bram, they prepare the positions, the shielding and the access arrangements before any exposure.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Optimisation hall: approved Daniel and Sofia miniatures, installed vessel, workbenches and legible horizontal route labels. Paragraph-specific physical arrangement.","beats":[{"at":"We are back in Bram's workshop at Havenmeer.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Now we improve the way the job will be done.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Optimisation means keeping exposure as low as reasonably ach","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"With Bram, they prepare the positions, the shielding and the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Daniel","Sofia"],"clip":"B1.1-S08-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S08-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Start with the radiation itself, before the barrier tape. The team chooses a beam direction that points away from where people are, and restricts the beam so that only the weld and its surroundings are irradiated. Here, a lead shielding screen is placed between the examination area and the proposed control position. Its material, thickness and position have to suit the equipment and the assessed radiation field, including scattered radiation, because radiation that hits the vessel and the floor bounces off in other directions and reaches places the direct beam never pointed at. The screen takes a large share of the exposure out of the control position; the perimeter around the whole set-up takes care of everyone else.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Optimisation hall: approved Daniel and Sofia miniatures, installed vessel, workbenches and legible horizontal route labels. Paragraph-specific physical arrangement.","beats":[{"at":"Start with the radiation itself, before the barrier tape.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The team chooses a beam direction that points away from wher","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Its material, thickness and position have to suit the equipm","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The screen takes a large share of the exposure out of the co","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Daniel","Sofia"],"clip":"B1.1-S08-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S08-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now look at Daniel's position. The controls are placed away from the vessel, outside the protection perimeter, with the shielding between him and the examination area. Increasing distance usually reduces exposure. For an unshielded point source in free space, twice the distance gives roughly a quarter of the dose rate; scattering and shielding in this hall change that simple relationship. The exact positions follow from the assessment and are confirmed by measurement on the day. Sofia watches the other approach from outside the perimeter. The two radiographers stay in visual or audible contact with each other throughout, and extra supervision is arranged wherever they cannot cover all the access routes themselves.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Optimisation hall: approved Daniel and Sofia miniatures, installed vessel, workbenches and legible horizontal route labels. Paragraph-specific physical arrangement.","beats":[{"at":"Now look at Daniel's position.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Increasing distance usually reduces exposure.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The exact positions follow from the assessment and are confi","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The two radiographers stay in visual or audible contact with","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Daniel","Sofia"],"clip":"B1.1-S08-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S08-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The pedestrian route is another part of the job. People normally use it to reach the workbenches. Bram arranges for those activities to stop and for the route to be closed during the exposures. The closure is agreed in advance, marked, and supervised, so that it holds even when someone is in a hurry. Daniel covers the control-side approach and Sofia the other entrance. The team starts only when both routes are controlled, and if someone crosses the boundary during an exposure, the exposure is stopped first and the conversation comes afterwards.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Optimisation hall: approved Daniel and Sofia miniatures, installed vessel, workbenches and legible horizontal route labels. Paragraph-specific physical arrangement.","beats":[{"at":"The pedestrian route is another part of the job.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Bram arranges for those activities to stop and for the route","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The closure is agreed in advance, marked, and supervised, so","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The team starts only when both routes are controlled, and if","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Daniel","Sofia"],"clip":"B1.1-S08-P4"},{"cue":"B1.1-S08-P5","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Good preparation also keeps exposure time down. Before any radiation is produced, the team checks the weld identification, the detector position, the equipment and the exposure plan, so that each image is taken once and taken right. During the exposure, everyone stays at their assessed position and nobody approaches the vessel. After it, the team confirms safe conditions with the required radiation checks before anyone goes near. Time is saved by preparation and discipline; the exposure itself lasts as long as the image quality needs, because an image that has to be repeated costs more dose than one done properly.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Optimisation hall: approved Daniel and Sofia miniatures, installed vessel, workbenches and legible horizontal route labels. Paragraph-specific physical arrangement.","beats":[{"at":"Good preparation also keeps exposure time down.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Before any radiation is produced, the team checks the weld i","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"After it, the team confirms safe conditions with the require","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Time is saved by preparation and discipline; the exposure it","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Daniel","Sofia"],"clip":"B1.1-S08-P5"},{"cue":"B1.1-S08-P6","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Finally, the drawing becomes real only in the workshop. The team checks the actual hall against the plan and carries out the last-minute risk assessment. During the first or a test exposure, they measure at the perimeter and adjust it where the reading asks for it; the shielding and the occupied positions are verified under the work procedure in the same way. And if the access route reopens or conditions change, the work stops and the assessment is made again. That is optimisation in practice: shielding, distance, preparation and supervision working together, with measurement confirming that the arrangements do what the drawing promised.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Optimisation hall: approved Daniel and Sofia miniatures, installed vessel, workbenches and legible horizontal route labels. Paragraph-specific physical arrangement.","beats":[{"at":"Finally, the drawing becomes real only in the workshop.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The team checks the actual hall against the plan and carries","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"And if the access route reopens or conditions change, the wo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"That is optimisation in practice: shielding, distance, prepa","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"characters":["Daniel","Sofia"],"clip":"B1.1-S08-P6"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S08-P1","B1.1-S08-P2","B1.1-S08-P3","B1.1-S08-P4","B1.1-S08-P5","B1.1-S08-P6"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S09","title":"Does the screen protect the whole team?","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S09-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Look at the two working positions in Bram's hall. The lead screen stands between the vessel and Daniel's controls. Sofia supervises the other entrance, on the opposite side of the examination area. She is outside the perimeter too, with her personal dosimeter on, and from where she stands she can see the door and the forklift route. What she does not have is the screen: it stands on Daniel's side, and nothing is between her and the vessel.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Same hall; Daniel-screen relationship highlighted, then Sofia on the opposite side. No measured result claimed.","beats":[{"at":"Look at the two working positions in Bram's hall.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The lead screen stands between the vessel and Daniel's contr","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"She is outside the perimeter too, with her personal dosimete","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"What she does not have is the screen: it stands on Daniel's ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S09-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S09-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"During the test exposure the team measures at both positions. At Daniel's controls the reading is low. At Sofia's position it meets the applicable dose-rate criterion for that position, and clearly higher than at Daniel's. Sofia says what many of us would say: \"The reading meets the criterion, so I'm fine where I am.\" Bram points to a spot by the door, five metres further back, from which the entrance is still in full view. Luc mentions that a second screen is in the depot and could be here tomorrow.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Same hall; Daniel-screen relationship highlighted, then Sofia on the opposite side. No measured result claimed.","beats":[{"at":"During the test exposure the team measures at both positions","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"At Daniel's controls the reading is low.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Sofia says what many of us would say: \"The reading meets the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Luc mentions that a second screen is in the depot and could ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S09-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S09-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"That is the whole of optimisation in one small decision: a position whose reading meets the applicable criterion, two ways to improve it, and a job that has been prepared for today. Keep three things in view: the dose at Sofia's position, the entrance she supervises, and what is reasonable to ask of the team and the client.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"Same hall; Daniel-screen relationship highlighted, then Sofia on the opposite side. No measured result claimed.","beats":[{"at":"That is the whole of optimisation in one small decision: a p","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Keep three things in view: the dose at Sofia's position, the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.1-S09-P3"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S09-Q01","type":"single_choice","title_visible":"Sofia's position","prompt_spoken_once":"What does the team do about Sofia's position?","situation_visible_text":"At Sofia's position the measured dose rate is within the applicable dose-rate criterion but well above Daniel's. Bram offers a spot five metres further back with the entrance still in view. A second screen could arrive tomorrow.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Keep her where she is: the reading at her position is within the applicable criterion, so the arrangement is acceptable.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"The reading does tell us something important: the applicable dose-rate criterion is met at this position, and the team was right to measure rather than assume. Respecting the limit is the third principle; optimisation is the second, and it keeps asking whether a reasonable improvement is available. Here one is, at no cost: a position further back that still gives her the entrance. Below the limit, the question is always: is there a better place she can stand?","screen":"The local criterion is met, and a free improvement is still available. Optimisation continues below the limit."},"clip":"B1.1-S09-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Move her to the position by the door, where the entrance is still in view, and measure again during a controlled test exposure before routine work.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. Distance is the cheapest protection there is: the farther position offers a practical improvement while the entrance stays supervised. The team verifies the new arrangement and measures there during a controlled test exposure. Routine work continues only if the results confirm adequate protection. Dose reduced, supervision kept, the client's day respected: that is what \"as low as reasonably achievable\" looks like in a hall.","screen":"Further back, entrance still covered, measured again: a reasonable improvement, verified."},"clip":"B1.1-S09-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Postpone the exposures until the second screen arrives tomorrow and put it on Sofia's side.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"A second screen would lower Sofia's dose further, and on a longer job it may well be worth bringing. Optimisation, though, weighs the improvement against what it costs, a day's delay for Bram's plant, a team that stands idle, and against what else is available. Today the team first assesses the available farther position and verifies it by measurement. If that does not provide adequate protection, it must add suitable measures or postpone the job. The screen remains an option to assess, not something cost alone allows us to dismiss.","screen":"A screen helps; a free improvement is available today. Reasonable means weighing the gain against the cost."},"clip":"B1.1-S09-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S09-Q01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S09-P1","B1.1-S09-P2","B1.1-S09-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S09-P3","interaction_id":"B1.1-S09-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S10","title":"Dose information: read the right evidence","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S10-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"We have improved the arrangements for Bram's job. Now look at what the instruments and the dose records can actually tell us, because they answer different questions. Daniel carries three devices. In his hand, the survey meter: it measures the radiation field at a place, right now, at the perimeter, at the control position, next to the vessel after an exposure. On the left of his chest, the electronic personal dosimeter: it follows the dose he himself receives, shows it live and sounds an alarm at a set level. On the right, the passive badge: it records his dose over the monitoring period and is read out afterwards by the dosimetry service, which makes it the official record of what he received. Three devices, three jobs, and all three sit behind the shielding and the perimeter that do the protecting.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S10 view 1; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"We have improved the arrangements for Bram's job.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Daniel carries three devices.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"On the left of his chest, the electronic personal dosimeter:","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Three devices, three jobs, and all three sit behind the shie","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S10-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S10-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"With those three in mind, keep two quantities apart. A dose rate, in microsieverts per hour, is what the survey meter reads: how fast dose is being delivered at one place at one moment. An accumulated dose, in millisieverts, is what the dosimeters build up: how much a person has received over a period. A rate at the tape and a dose on a badge are different things, so comparing one with a limit meant for the other tells you nothing. To check a personal dose limit, the quantity, the person and the period have to match, with every exposure of that period included, which is why one favourable reading at the perimeter says nothing about Daniel's dose for the year.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S10 view 2; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"With those three in mind, keep two quantities apart.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"A dose rate, in microsieverts per hour, is what the survey m","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"A rate at the tape and a dose on a badge are different thing","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"To check a personal dose limit, the quantity, the person and","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S10-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S10-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Three reference levels guide protection, and each serves a different purpose. The legal dose limit is the boundary that may never be crossed. A dose constraint sits below it: a planning level used in optimisation for a particular job or source, which the Agency can impose. The alarm setting on Daniel's electronic dosimeter is different again: an operational warning threshold, set for this task under our approved arrangements, so that he knows early when the work is not going as planned. Limit, constraint, alarm: boundary, planning level, early warning.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S10 view 3; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Three reference levels guide protection, and each serves a d","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The legal dose limit is the boundary that may never be cross","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The alarm setting on Daniel's electronic dosimeter is differ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Limit, constraint, alarm: boundary, planning level, early wa","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S10-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S10-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"So what happens when the alarm sounds in Bram's hall? Daniel acts under the procedure: the exposure is stopped, he moves away from the source, and he reports what happened before anything resumes. The alarm is a signal to act; its cause and the recorded dose still need to be checked. An alarm does not, by itself, establish how the dose compares with a limit. And when the alarm stays silent, the dosimeter has recorded what he received; the proof that the limits were respected comes from the records over the period, read against the right quantity and the right person. The instruments tell us where we are; the planning and the records tell us whether we did well.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S10 view 3; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"So what happens when the alarm sounds in Bram's hall?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The alarm is a signal to act; its cause and the recorded dos","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"An alarm does not, by itself, establish how the dose compare","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The instruments tell us where we are; the planning and the r","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S10-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S10-P1","B1.1-S10-P2","B1.1-S10-P3","B1.1-S10-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S11","title":"Can one reading answer for the week?","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S11-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"For this dose-planning example, look ahead to the end of the Havenmeer job. Back at the depot, Daniel reads his electronic dosimeter: a small dose for the day, well within what the plan expected. The survey meter has done its work at the perimeter and at the control position. His passive badge goes back in the rack; the dosimetry service will read it out at the end of the monitoring period, as it does every time.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S11 view 1; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"For this dose-planning example, look ahead to the end of the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Back at the depot, Daniel reads his electronic dosimeter: a ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The survey meter has done its work at the perimeter and at t","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"His passive badge goes back in the rack; the dosimetry servi","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S11-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S11-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Luc is planning the coming days. \"Daniel's reading is low,\" he says, \"so I'll put him on the gamma job tomorrow and the two bunker days after that. No need to look anything up.\" Sofia, listening, isn't so sure: the week's jobs add up, and Daniel had a heavy job last week too. Think about what Luc is holding in his hand, what that number covers, and what the limit is written for.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S11 view 1; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Luc is planning the coming days.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"\"Daniel's reading is low,\" he says, \"so I'll put him on the ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"No need to look anything up.\" Sofia, listening, isn't so sur","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Think about what Luc is holding in his hand, what that numbe","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S11-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S11-Q01","type":"single_choice","title_visible":"Planning Daniel's week","prompt_spoken_once":"What does Luc need before he schedules Daniel's week?","situation_visible_text":"Daniel's electronic dosimeter shows a small dose for today's job. Luc wants to schedule him for a gamma job tomorrow and two bunker days after that, without checking anything. His badge is read out at the end of the period.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Nothing more: today's electronic reading is low, so the limit leaves plenty of room for the week.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Today's reading is real and useful: it tells us this job went as planned. What it covers is one day. The limit is written for a person over a period, and every job in that period counts towards the same total, last week's heavy job included. So the number in Luc's hand is one entry in a running record, and the planning question is answered by that record, with the last entry as one part of it.","screen":"One day's reading is one entry. The limit applies to the period, with every job included."},"clip":"B1.1-S11-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"The readout of Daniel's passive badge for today's job, before anything else is scheduled.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"The badge is the official record, and it will confirm the period's dose when the service reads it out. That is exactly why it is read per monitoring period and not per job: it is the check behind the planning. Between readouts, our service keeps Daniel's running dose from the electronic dosimeters and the previous readouts, and that is what Luc looks at before he fills a week.","screen":"The badge confirms the period afterwards. Planning uses the running record kept by the service."},"clip":"B1.1-S11-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Daniel's running dose for the period so far, with the expected doses of the three planned jobs, set against his constraint and the limit.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. Three things, matching the way the limit is written: the right person, the right quantity, the right period. The service keeps Daniel's running dose: today's reading, last week's job, the earlier official results and the subsequent operational readings, without counting any exposure twice. Luc adds what the gamma job and the bunker days are expected to give, and reads the total against the planning level set for Daniel and the limit behind it. If the plan meets the applicable requirements, it can be scheduled. Otherwise the service revises the protective arrangements and work allocation. Moving a job to a later day does not reset a person's dose for the period. That is how one low reading becomes a planning decision instead of a guess.","screen":"Running dose for the period plus the expected doses of the planned jobs, against constraint and limit."},"clip":"B1.1-S11-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S11-Q01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S11-P1","B1.1-S11-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S11-P2","interaction_id":"B1.1-S11-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S12","title":"The regulation, our licence and our procedures","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S12-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now return to the preparation of Bram's job. Planning has accepted the request, and the team is preparing the agreed work. On the desk lie three kinds of document, and Daniel reaches for each of them for a different reason. The first is the regulation: it tells us what has to be done, for everyone who does this work. Article sixteen of the industrial radiography decree, for instance, requires that the safety measures identified in the risk analyses are in place and that the team performs a last-minute risk assessment before the first exposure. That is the requirement, written once, for every job.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S12 view 1; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Now return to the preparation of Bram's job.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"On the desk lie three kinds of document, and Daniel reaches ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The first is the regulation: it tells us what has to be done","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"That is the requirement, written once, for every job.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S12-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S12-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The second is our company's licence. It is the Agency's authorisation for our company: it names the installations and equipment we may use, the sources we may hold, the practices we may carry out, industrial radiography in our bunker and on clients' sites, and the conditions attached to all of that. When Daniel wants to know whether we may bring a particular X-ray set to Havenmeer, the licence is the document that answers. Its scope and its conditions are what our company works within, and every job is prepared inside that frame.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S12 view 2; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"The second is our company's licence.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"It is the Agency's authorisation for our company: it names t","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"When Daniel wants to know whether we may bring a particular ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Its scope and its conditions are what our company works with","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S12-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S12-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The third is the approved work procedure, and with it the worksite record. The procedure describes how our team performs the work and the checks: in which order, with which instruments, against which criteria. Its radiation-protection content has been examined and approved by the recognised expert, you saw in the earlier scenes how that approval comes about, so when Daniel follows it, the expert's judgement is at the vessel with him. The record is the other half: it shows what was actually checked at Havenmeer, by whom, when, and with what result. The procedure is the method; the record is the evidence that the method was applied today, in this hall, with these results.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S12 view 3; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"The third is the approved work procedure, and with it the wo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The procedure describes how our team performs the work and t","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The record is the other half: it shows what was actually che","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The procedure is the method; the record is the evidence that","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S12-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S12-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Three documents, three questions. What is required? The regulation. What may our company do, and under which conditions? The licence. How do we do it, and what did we actually check? The procedure and its record. Open the three parts of Bram's job file and read, in each one, the line that answers its question.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S12 view 3; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Three documents, three questions.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The regulation.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"How do we do it, and what did we actually check?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Open the three parts of Bram's job file and read, in each on","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S12-P4"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S12-X01","type":"guided_exploration","title_visible":"What does each part of the file establish?","prompt_spoken_once":"Open the three parts of the job file and read the line each one is there for.","items":[{"id":"regulation","label":"The regulation: what is required?","page":"Extract of the industrial radiography decree, article sixteen, with the two lines in focus: the identified safety measures are present; a last-minute risk assessment is performed before the first exposure.","spoken":"This is the requirement for Bram's job and for every job like it: the safety measures from the risk analyses are in place, and the team carries out its last-minute risk assessment before the first exposure. It is the same for every hall and every team. Which measures those are for Havenmeer, and whether they were checked today, you find in the next two parts.","screen":"Required: assessed safety measures present; last-minute risk assessment before the first exposure.","field_in_focus":"The regulation: what is required?","clip":"B1.1-S12-X01-regulation"},{"id":"licence","label":"Our licence: what may we do, under which conditions?","page":"Teaching excerpt of the company licence, with the fields in focus: authorised practices (radiography in the company bunker and on clients' sites); equipment scope; conditions.","spoken":"This is the Agency's authorisation for our company. It tells Daniel that radiography on a client's site is within our practices, that the X-ray set he plans to bring is within our equipment scope, and which conditions apply. The licence sets the frame for the job; the justification, the risk analyses and today's checks fill that frame in for Havenmeer.","screen":"Licence: authorised practices, equipment scope, conditions.","field_in_focus":"Our licence: what may we do, under which conditions?","clip":"B1.1-S12-X01-licence"},{"id":"procedure","label":"Procedure and record: how, and what was checked?","page":"The worksite set-up procedure with its approval line (recognised expert) in focus; below it, today's worksite record with one completed line: perimeter measured at the first exposure · result · time · Daniel.","spoken":"The procedure tells the team how: mark out the perimeter, measure at the line during the first exposure, enlarge it if the reading asks for it, approved by the recognised expert. The record shows that it happened at Havenmeer: the measurement, the result, the time, and Daniel's name. Together they answer \"how do we work\" and \"what did we do today\", and the record is what the expert and the Agency will read later.","screen":"Procedure: how to check. Record: who checked what, when, with which result.","field_in_focus":"Procedure and record: how, and what was checked?","clip":"B1.1-S12-X01-procedure"}],"clip":"B1.1-S12-X01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S12-P1","B1.1-S12-P2","B1.1-S12-P3","B1.1-S12-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S12-P4","interaction_id":"B1.1-S12-X01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S13","title":"The hall is no longer as planned","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S13-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Daniel and Sofia arrive at Havenmeer Process Works for the job that was planned last week. Bram meets them at the door of the hall. Everything was prepared on paper: the workpiece, the technique, the protection perimeter, the place for the shielding and the positions of the two radiographers. Daniel walks in and sees two things that were different on paper. Pallets are now stored exactly where the perimeter and the shielding were planned. And in the adjoining hall, behind the wall, a maintenance team is at work. In the plan, that hall was empty.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S13 view 1; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Daniel and Sofia arrive at Havenmeer Process Works for the j","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Everything was prepared on paper: the workpiece, the techniq","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Pallets are now stored exactly where the perimeter and the s","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"In the plan, that hall was empty.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S13-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S13-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"These two changes matter because the plan was calculated on the hall as it was described. The distance to the perimeter, the place of the shielding, the positions of Daniel and Sofia and the dose rate at the wall of the adjoining hall all follow from that description. Pallets in the way mean the perimeter can no longer run where it was calculated, and the shielding can no longer stand where it was meant to stand. People in the adjoining hall mean that the wall is now a boundary with someone on the other side. The assessment must include adjoining areas, even when people cannot be seen from the vessel. Article nineteen sets a maximum of ten microsieverts per hour for permanent workstations and adjoining buildings; an apparently empty adjoining area must not simply be ignored. One change moves the perimeter. The other changes what the perimeter has to protect.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S13 view 2; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"These two changes matter because the plan was calculated on ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Pallets in the way mean the perimeter can no longer run wher","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Article nineteen sets a maximum of ten microsieverts per hou","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The other changes what the perimeter has to protect.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S13-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S13-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The X-ray set stays switched off and the first exposure waits. Daniel reports to Luc and to our service, and tells Bram what he has found. Then each of them decides their own part. Bram decides what happens in his hall: whether the pallets are moved, and whether the maintenance team stays, pauses or leaves. Our company decides whether the plan still covers the new situation. That means a new look at the perimeter, at the shielding and at the dose rate on every side, including the side it cannot see. If the pallets are gone and the neighbouring work is paused, our team still checks that the agreed conditions really are present before proceeding under the procedure. If the pallets stay or the team keeps working, the plan is adapted, checked and confirmed first. In both cases the start signal comes from the company's own check, after Bram has done his part.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S13 view 2; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"The X-ray set stays switched off and the first exposure wait","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Bram decides what happens in his hall: whether the pallets a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"That means a new look at the perimeter, at the shielding and","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"In both cases the start signal comes from the company's own ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S13-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S13-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Changed conditions are normal on a site. Halls get used, pallets arrive, other teams are planned in. The skill is to see the change, stop, report it and reassess, instead of fitting the work around it. And the division is clear: the person who owns the hall decides about the hall, and the company that brings the radiation decides about the radiation. Bram can clear the space and move his people. Whether it is safe to expose is a decision our company takes, and it takes that decision with the plan in hand.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S13 view 2; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Changed conditions are normal on a site.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The skill is to see the change, stop, report it and reassess","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"And the division is clear: the person who owns the hall deci","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Whether it is safe to expose is a decision our company takes","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S13-P4"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S13-Q01","type":"single_choice","title_visible":"Who decides what?","prompt_spoken_once":"Daniel has found two changes. Who decides what, before the first exposure can start?","situation_visible_text":"Daniel and Sofia arrive at Havenmeer Process Works for the planned on-site job. Pallets are now stored where the protection perimeter and the shielding were planned. A maintenance team is working in the adjoining hall, which the plan assumed to be empty. No exposure has started yet.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Bram clears the pallets and confirms that the maintenance team will take a break during the exposures. With both settled, Daniel starts as planned, because the hall is now as it was described.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have Bram's part right: the pallets and the maintenance team are his to arrange. The piece that is missing is the company's own check. The plan was calculated on an empty adjoining hall and on a perimeter at a certain distance. A break during the exposures is an arrangement, and arrangements are verified and written into the plan before they protect anyone. The hall is only as described when the company has confirmed that itself.","screen":"Bram arranges the hall. The company confirms the plan before the start."},"clip":"B1.1-S13-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Bram clears the pallets and decides whether the maintenance team stays or leaves. Daniel takes his word on the adjoining hall and only re-measures the perimeter on his own side of the wall.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You are right that Bram decides about the pallets and about his own people. Where this goes wrong is the wall. The perimeter belongs to the radiography company on every side, also on the side it cannot see. A boundary that is measured on one side and taken on trust on the other is half a boundary. The company checks the dose rate where people can be, and the adjoining hall is now exactly such a place.","screen":"The perimeter is the company's on every side, including behind the wall."},"clip":"B1.1-S13-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Bram decides what happens to the pallets and the maintenance team, because the hall is his. The company decides whether the new situation is still covered by the plan and checks the setup before exposure and verifies the perimeter during the first or a test exposure.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. Two owners, two decisions. Bram owns the hall, so the pallets and the maintenance team are his to move, pause or keep. The company owns the radiation, so whether the plan still holds, where the perimeter now runs and what the dose rate is on every side are its decisions, with the setup checked beforehand and dose rates measured during the first or a test exposure. Daniel reports to Luc, to our service and to Bram, and the job starts when both parts are done.","screen":"Bram: the hall. The company: the plan, the perimeter and the start."},"clip":"B1.1-S13-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S13-Q01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S13-P1","B1.1-S13-P2","B1.1-S13-P3","B1.1-S13-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S13-P4","interaction_id":"B1.1-S13-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S14","title":"From hold to a verified arrangement","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S14-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"We stay at Havenmeer, because the hold is only the beginning. The first thing Daniel does is report in facts. The space where the shielding and the perimeter were planned is taken by stored pallets. People are at work in the adjoining hall. No exposure has been made. He reports it this way to Luc and to our service, and he writes it down the same way in the worksite file. Facts first, because everyone who now has to decide, Luc, the physical control service and Bram, works from this description and nothing else. A report of what has been seen, what is known and what still has to be established is the ground every next step stands on.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S14 view 1; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"We stay at Havenmeer, because the hold is only the beginning","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The space where the shielding and the perimeter were planned","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"He reports it this way to Luc and to our service, and he wri","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"A report of what has been seen, what is known and what still","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S14-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S14-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bram does his part: he has the pallets moved and he coordinates with the maintenance team about when they work and where. Meanwhile the company looks at the arrangement as a whole, and that is more than the two things Daniel noticed. Five elements belong together in a site arrangement: the space, the direction of the beam, the shielding, the areas where people can be, and who supervises the perimeter during the exposures. Change one and the others shift with it. A pallet that stays means the shielding moves, and shielding that moves means the beam direction and the perimeter distance are looked at again. The outcome can be that the stored material is moved, that the neighbouring work is rescheduled, or that a different arrangement is assessed and chosen. The outcome can also be that the job waits for another day, because safe conditions are a result that is reached, and sometimes the way to reach them is to come back.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S14 view 2; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"Bram does his part: he has the pallets moved and he coordina","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Five elements belong together in a site arrangement: the spa","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"A pallet that stays means the shielding moves, and shielding","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The outcome can also be that the job waits for another day, ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S14-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S14-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"When the arrangement is decided, the team walks it before anyone exposes. The shielding stands where it is drawn. The perimeter is marked where it is calculated. The agreed arrangements for the adjoining hall are confirmed, and the applicable boundary criterion is included in the checks. The worksite information is updated so the file describes the hall as it is today. Then Daniel and Sofia do their last-minute risk assessment at the spot: a short, deliberate look at the real situation, in the minutes before the first exposure, by the people who will do the work.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S14 view 3; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"When the arrangement is decided, the team walks it before an","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The perimeter is marked where it is calculated.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The agreed arrangements for the adjoining hall are confirmed","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Then Daniel and Sofia do their last-minute risk assessment a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S14-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S14-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The first exposure is a test. During it the team measures the dose rate at the perimeter and at the wall of the adjoining hall, and compares the readings with the limits in the plan. Where a reading is higher than planned, the arrangement is adjusted and measured again. The readings that go into the record are the ones from the meter, written at the time, with the place and the moment. That is what makes the arrangement verified: a plan that was calculated, a set-up that was checked, and measurements that confirm it. The permission to continue follows from those readings, and that is where this example ends.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup: S14 view 3; linked to Bram’s current assignment.","beats":[{"at":"The first exposure is a test.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Where a reading is higher than planned, the arrangement is a","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"The readings that go into the record are the ones from the m","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"The permission to continue follows from those readings, and ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S14-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S14-P1","B1.1-S14-P2","B1.1-S14-P3","B1.1-S14-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S15","title":"Bram's assignment: bring the reasoning together","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Bram's request is where this lesson started, so let us walk his request back from the beginning, this time in one line of reasoning. He asked for radiography on two welds. Before any exposure was made, the company asked three questions, in this order. Is radiography needed for these welds, and on what basis: a standard from a recognised standardisation organisation, or a risk analysis of what an undetected defect would mean? Where will the exposure take place, and does this piece belong in the bunker, or is there a supported reason for his hall? And with what equipment, with an X-ray generator preferred where that is feasible without extra risk? Three questions, three justified answers, and only then a job.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup S15 closing view 1.","beats":[{"at":"Bram's request is where this lesson started, so let us walk ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"Before any exposure was made, the company asked three questi","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Where will the exposure take place, and does this piece belo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Three questions, three justified answers, and only then a jo","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-P1"},{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"With the job justified, the company organised protection. It drew the perimeter around the work, put distance and shielding between the radiation and the people, and placed two radiographers where they can supervise the perimeter and remain in visual or audible contact. It gave each of them a survey meter for the dose rate at a place and dosimeters for the dose they themselves receive, and it read those numbers against the planning level set for them and the limit behind it. It planned Daniel's week on his running dose for the period, with every job counted. And it wrote all of that down in documents that each answer a different question: what is required, what the company may do, how it is done, and what was done.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup S15 closing view 2.","beats":[{"at":"With the job justified, the company organised protection.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"It drew the perimeter around the work, put distance and shie","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"It planned Daniel's week on his running dose for the period,","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"And it wrote all of that down in documents that each answer ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-P2"},{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Then the hall was different from the plan, and the reasoning showed its value. The team held. Daniel reported facts. Bram arranged his hall, the company reassessed its plan, and the start was made to depend on measurements at the first exposure. Every step you have seen in this lesson belongs to one of three things: justifying the work, protecting the people, and checking that the real situation matches the plan.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup S15 closing view 3.","beats":[{"at":"Then the hall was different from the plan, and the reasoning","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"The team held.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"Bram arranged his hall, the company reassessed its plan, and","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"Every step you have seen in this lesson belongs to one of th","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-P3"},{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now Bram calls again. A week later, he has another weld in the same hall. He says: you have the plan from last time, the pallets are gone, the hall is quiet, can you come tomorrow and do the same? It sounds simple, and that is exactly why it is a good test of what you have learned.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup S15 closing view 3.","beats":[{"at":"Now Bram calls again.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"A week later, he has another weld in the same hall.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"He says: you have the plan from last time, the pallets are g","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"It sounds simple, and that is exactly why it is a good test ","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-P4"},{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P5","speaker":"Emilia","text":"That closes the first lesson, and here is what you now carry with you. You know what a radiography company is and why it exists: it finds defects that eyes cannot see, with radiation that needs rules. You know who is who around that radiation: the Agency that licenses and supervises, the recognised organisation and its expert who examine and approve, the physical control service that watches from inside, the head of that service who makes sure every justification was made by someone competent, the company that refuses a job it cannot accept, and the radiographers who do the work and are trained as agents. You know the three questions that come before every job, technique, location and equipment, and that each has to be justified and written down. You know how the people are protected: with a perimeter, distance, shielding, two radiographers, a survey meter for the dose rate at a place, dosimeters for the dose a person receives, and a planning level below the limit. You know which document answers which question. And you know what to do when the real situation differs from the plan: hold, report facts, let each party decide its own part, and verify with measurements before the start.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup S15 closing view 3.","beats":[{"at":"That closes the first lesson, and here is what you now carry","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"You know who is who around that radiation: the Agency that l","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"You know how the people are protected: with a perimeter, dis","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"And you know what to do when the real situation differs from","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-P5"},{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P6","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Keep three questions with you for every lesson that follows. What is known? What still has to be checked? And who has to act? In B one point two we stay with the same people and make their responsibilities concrete: what the radiation protection agent checks on the day, what the recognised expert approves and how often, and who receives the report when something is found.","screen_text":[],"start_visual":"B1Followup S15 closing view 3.","beats":[{"at":"Keep three questions with you for every lesson that follows.","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 1"},{"at":"What is known?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 2"},{"at":"And who has to act?","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 3"},{"at":"In B one point two we stay with the same people and make the","show":"Reviewed explanation, focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-P6"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.1-S15-R01","type":"single_choice","title_visible":"Bram's second request","prompt_spoken_once":"What does Bram's second request start in the company?","situation_visible_text":"A week after the first job, Bram asks for radiography on another weld in the same hall. He offers last week's plan, says the pallets are gone and the hall is quiet, and asks whether the team can come tomorrow and do the same.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The same three questions as the first time, for this weld: whether radiography is justified, where it belongs, and with what equipment. Then a plan for the hall as it is on the day, verified at the first exposure.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. A second weld is a second request, and a request starts the reasoning, not the exposure. Justification is about this weld: the standard or the risk analysis that applies to it, and the question whether this piece can go to the bunker. Last week's plan is a useful starting point, and it becomes this week's plan when the hall has been checked as it is tomorrow and the first exposure has been measured. Bram's good news about the pallets is welcome. The company checks it itself.","screen":"A new weld starts the three questions again. Last week's plan is a starting point; tomorrow's hall and the first exposure decide."},"clip":"B1.1-S15-R01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Last week's plan, because the justification was done for this hall and these workpieces. The team arrives, confirms that the pallets are gone and the hall is quiet, and starts with the same perimeter and measurements.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have remembered that the plan was built with care, and much of it will carry over. The part to look at again is the justification, because we must check whether the existing written justification for the type of assignment covers this new weld and these conditions. The standard or risk analysis, the location and the equipment must remain applicable. And a perimeter is confirmed by measuring at the first exposure, at every job, also in a hall the team knows.","screen":"Check that the written justification covers this assignment type and its conditions; verify the perimeter during the first or a test exposure."},"clip":"B1.1-S15-R01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"A visit by the recognised expert, because a second job in the same hall makes it a regular site and the expert approves the arrangement. The team waits for that approval and then uses last week's plan.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You are right that the recognised expert has a role, and you will see in the next lesson what the expert approves and when. The decision to accept Bram's request, to justify this weld and to prepare the arrangement lies with the company itself: the head of the physical control service makes sure the justification was made by someone competent, and the team plans and verifies the hall. The expert checks that this system works. Tomorrow's job starts with the company's own three questions.","screen":"The client justifies technique and location; our company checks acceptance, justifies equipment and plans the work. The expert performs the reserved expert tasks."},"clip":"B1.1-S15-R01-c"}],"clip":"B1.1-S15-R01","reviewed_b11":true},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.1-S15-P1","B1.1-S15-P2","B1.1-S15-P3","B1.1-S15-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.1-S15-P4","interaction_id":"B1.1-S15-R01","post_interaction_cues":[{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P5","condition":"after activity completion"},{"cue":"B1.1-S15-P6","condition":"after activity completion"}]}}]},{"id":"B1.2","title":"The people behind radiation protection","scenes":[{"id":"S01","title":"Welcome back: who does what","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S01-P1","text":"Welcome back. In the first lesson you met the people around radiation protection and followed one job from Bram's email to a verified arrangement. Today we stay inside our own company, and we look at the same people from a different side: not who they are, but what each of them is allowed to decide, what they have to be able to show, and who has to hear from whom when something is wrong.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Welcome back.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"In the first lesson you met the people around radiation prot","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Today we stay inside our own company, and we look at the sam","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.2-S01-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S01-P2","text":"I'll do that with three messages that arrived on my desk this week, because that is how these questions actually come: not as definitions, but as a colleague who needs an answer before Thursday. One is from our planner, one from the team, and one from Daniel. Each of them looks simple, and each of them hides a decision that belongs to a particular person.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"I'll do that with three messages that arrived on my desk thi","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"One is from our planner, one from the team, and one from Dan","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Each of them looks simple, and each of them hides a decision","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.2-S01-P2"},{"cue":"B1.2-S01-P3","text":"By the end of this lesson you will be able to tell apart three things that people easily lump together: doing a check, coordinating it, and approving the procedure behind it. You will know what a training certificate proves and what still has to be shown next to it. You will know exactly who has to hear from a radiographer when a check fails. And you will recognise one role name that sounds like ours and belongs to a different decree. Let's start with the messages.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"By the end of this lesson you will be able to tell apart thr","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"You will know what a training certificate proves and what st","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"And you will recognise one role name that sounds like ours a","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Let's start with the messages.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S01-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S01-P1","B1.2-S01-P2","B1.2-S01-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S02","title":"Three questions on my desk","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S02-P1","text":"Here is the first message, from our planner: \"Who is the radiation protection agent on Thursday's worksite?\" The second comes from the team: \"Can we start using the revised version of the pre-use check form for the survey meters and the exposure devices?\" And the third is from Daniel, who joined us a few months ago: \"I passed the agent course. Does that mean I can be the agent on my own now?\"","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Here is the first message, from our planner: \"Who is the rad","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Does that mean I can be the agent on my own now?\"","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.2-S02-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S02-P2","text":"It would be easy to answer all three with \"ask the safety people\". A team works better when it can answer them itself, because behind each message stand three different responsibilities: who performs a task, who has approved the way it is done, and who has to be told when something does not fit. When those three are kept apart, a missed check or an unapproved form is noticed the same day. When they are blurred, it can sit unnoticed for months.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"It would be easy to answer all three with \"ask the safety pe","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"A team works better when it can answer them itself, because ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"When those three are kept apart, a missed check or an unappr","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"When they are blurred, it can sit unnoticed for months.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S02-P2"},{"cue":"B1.2-S02-P3","text":"Notice also that the three messages are about three different kinds of paper. A completed check form records what one person observed on one day. A procedure describes how a check has to be done, every day, by everyone. A certificate shows that a person passed a test. I keep all three in the same folder, because they belong to the same activity, and I read each of them for what it proves and nothing more. Hold on to that; we come back to it with every message.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Notice also that the three messages are about three differen","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"A procedure describes how a check has to be done, every day,","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"A certificate shows that a person passed a test.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Hold on to that; we come back to it with every message.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S02-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S02-P1","B1.2-S02-P2","B1.2-S02-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S03","title":"Who may lead the service, and what leading means","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S03-P1","text":"You know from the first lesson that our company, as the licence holder, is the operator, and that every operator organises a physical control service. Today I want to show you the conditions behind that, because they decide who may do what. The first condition is about the head of the service. If the operator has a recognised expert in physical control of class one or two on its own staff, it entrusts the leadership of the service to that expert. If it has no such expert, it entrusts the leadership to a member of staff who has followed the basic and the continuing training that the general regulation sets out. That is our situation, and I am that staff member. For a radiography company the industrial radiography decree adds one more condition: the head of the service has three years of relevant experience in radiation protection for industrial radiography.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"You know from the first lesson that our company, as the lice","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The first condition is about the head of the service.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"If it has no such expert, it entrusts the leadership to a me","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"For a radiography company the industrial radiography decree ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S03-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S03-P2","text":"What does leading the service mean in practice? The regulation gives two things. The head coordinates and organises the proper execution of the tasks given to the service, and the head has direct access to the head of the establishment and to the operator. Put those together and you have my job on a Monday: I make sure every task the service has to do is covered by someone who can actually do it, and when a task cannot be done with the arrangements we have, I take that straight to the people who can change the arrangements. Coordinating is a real power, and it is also a bounded one: I organise the checks, I keep the versions of our procedures apart, I make sure the right people are told. I do not approve the procedures myself, and that is the next condition.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"What does leading the service mean in practice?","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The head coordinates and organises the proper execution of t","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Put those together and you have my job on a Monday: I make s","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"I do not approve the procedures myself, and that is the next","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S03-P2"},{"cue":"B1.2-S03-P3","text":"The general regulation lists a group of tasks, examining and approving, measuring, evaluating, that are carried out by a recognised expert of class one or two. We have no such expert on our staff, so the regulation requires us to entrust those tasks to a physical control organisation recognised for the purpose, and the contract between our company and that organisation is concluded for exactly this. Notice the two words: the contract is with the organisation, and the organisation provides the expert. That is why an expert from the organisation appears in our files, approves our procedures and visits our installations, and it is also why, when that expert is unavailable, the organisation is still bound to us.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"The general regulation lists a group of tasks, examining and","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"We have no such expert on our staff, so the regulation requi","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Notice the two words: the contract is with the organisation,","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"That is why an expert from the organisation appears in our f","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S03-P3"},{"cue":"B1.2-S03-P4","text":"One more condition closes the picture. In class two and three establishments, the Agency is charged with supervising whether the physical control service carries out its mission properly. So the Agency looks at the service itself: whether it exists, whether it is led by someone who meets the conditions, whether its tasks are done. Keep the whole arrangement in mind as four decisions: the company stays responsible, the head coordinates, the expert from the contracted organisation approves and evaluates, and the Agency supervises the service. The three messages on my desk are each answered by one of those four.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"One more condition closes the picture.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"In class two and three establishments, the Agency is charged","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Keep the whole arrangement in mind as four decisions: the co","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The three messages on my desk are each answered by one of th","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S03-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S03-P1","B1.2-S03-P2","B1.2-S03-P3","B1.2-S03-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S04","title":"Who is the agent on Thursday?","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S04-P1","text":"Now the planner's message: who is the agent on Thursday's worksite? The general regulation says that the operator designates, in each of its establishments and among its own staff, radiation protection agents who carry out the physical control tasks listed for them. For those tasks the agents depend functionally on the service, and they have followed the training for agents. The industrial radiography decree makes that concrete for us: on every worksite the company designates an agent from the industrial radiographers present who belong to its staff and have followed that training.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Now the planner's message: who is the agent on Thursday's wo","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The general regulation says that the operator designates, in","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"For those tasks the agents depend functionally on the servic","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The industrial radiography decree makes that concrete for us","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S04-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S04-P2","text":"So the answer to the planner is a person, chosen for that day. All our radiographers are trained as agents, and for Thursday the company names one of the radiographers who will actually be there. That designation is a company decision about one worksite, and it is recorded in the planning. My part is to make sure the decision has been taken, that it is written down, and that the person named is prepared for that installation and that task. \"Ask the safety department\" is an answer that skips all of that, because the agent has to be someone standing in that hall on Thursday.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"So the answer to the planner is a person, chosen for that da","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"All our radiographers are trained as agents, and for Thursda","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"My part is to make sure the decision has been taken, that it","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"\"Ask the safety department\" is an answer that skips all of t","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S04-P2"},{"cue":"B1.2-S04-P3","text":"You heard in the first lesson what the agent checks: that the protection rules and work procedures are followed, that the protective means, the instruments and the dosimeters are available, working and used correctly, and that abnormal situations reach me and the recognised expert. The regulation calls those checks frequent and systematic, and that is the point of the function: a trained person on the spot, looking at everyday protection every time, rather than an occasional visit from outside.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"You heard in the first lesson what the agent checks: that th","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The regulation calls those checks frequent and systematic, a","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.2-S04-P3"},{"cue":"B1.2-S04-P4","text":"And the list closes with one sentence I want you to carry through this lesson: the agent carries out those tasks on the basis of instructions and procedures approved by a recognised expert in physical control. That sentence connects the agent and the expert without confusing them. The expert has approved how the checking is done. The agent does the checking. When Daniel checks a survey meter against our pre-use procedure and records the result, that record is his observation on that day. The expert's approval of the procedure tells us how a check is to be done; the record tells us whether a particular check was actually done. Each piece of evidence answers its own question, and neither replaces the other.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"And the list closes with one sentence I want you to carry th","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The expert has approved how the checking is done.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"When Daniel checks a survey meter against our pre-use proced","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Each piece of evidence answers its own question, and neither","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S04-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S04-P1","B1.2-S04-P2","B1.2-S04-P3","B1.2-S04-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S05","title":"The revised check form: who may do what with it?","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S05-P1","text":"Now the team's message: can they start using the revised pre-use check form? Here is how the revision came about. Daniel noticed that one sentence on the current form can be read two ways: whether the meter's response is checked before or after the device is positioned. He wrote a clearer sentence and suggested we use it. That is exactly the kind of contribution I want from a radiographer, and I told him so.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Now the team's message: can they start using the revised pre","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Here is how the revision came about.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"He wrote a clearer sentence and suggested we use it.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"That is exactly the kind of contribution I want from a radio","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S05-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S05-P2","text":"A good suggestion is still a proposal, and the reason is in the sentence from the last scene. The form belongs to a radiation-protection procedure, and the agents do their checks on the basis of procedures approved by the recognised expert. A clearer wording changes what the agents do, so it goes through the same approval as the rest of the procedure. So I ask Daniel to describe the ambiguity with an example, I bring the proposal to our recognised organisation for its expert to examine, and the team keeps using the current version until the revised one has been examined and approved. Nobody on a worksite should have to guess which form applies.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"A good suggestion is still a proposal, and the reason is in ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The form belongs to a radiation-protection procedure, and th","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"So I ask Daniel to describe the ambiguity with an example, I","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Nobody on a worksite should have to guess which form applies","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S05-P2"},{"cue":"B1.2-S05-P3","text":"Here is where it gets interesting, and where this week's message actually comes from. The expert who usually handles our files is away for three weeks. The team would like the clearer form now, and two colleagues have offered me a way out. Luc: \"You lead the service, you can sign off a wording change yourself and show it to her when she's back.\" Our director: \"She approved that check last year; a clearer sentence for the same check doesn't need her again.\"","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Here is where it gets interesting, and where this week's mes","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The expert who usually handles our files is away for three w","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The team would like the clearer form now, and two colleagues","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Luc: \"You lead the service, you can sign off a wording chang","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S05-P3"},{"cue":"B1.2-S05-P4","text":"Both are trying to help, and both are testing the lines we just drew: what coordinating allows me to do, what approval is and who gives it, and whom our contract is actually with. Think about those three before you answer.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Both are trying to help, and both are testing the lines we j","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Think about those three before you answer.","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.2-S05-P4"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.2-S05-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b12":true,"title_visible":"The expert is away for three weeks","prompt_spoken_once":"What may I do, as head of the service, so that the team gets a clear form as soon as possible?","situation_visible_text":"Daniel's clearer version of the pre-use check form is on the desk, marked PROPOSED. The expert who handles our files is away for three weeks. Luc suggests that Emilia signs off the wording herself. The director says last year's approval of the check covers it.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Approve the clearer sentence myself for the three weeks, as head of the service, and put it on the expert's desk for confirmation when she returns.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You are right that the head of the service has real powers, and keeping the teams working with clear instructions is part of my job. The power to approve a radiation-protection procedure is a different one: the regulation gives examining and approving to a recognised expert, and our contract places those tasks with the recognised organisation. Coordinating means I organise the route to approval and keep the versions apart. A sentence I sign for three weeks would be a form that no expert has approved, in use on a worksite.","screen":"The head coordinates. Approval of a procedure is the expert's task, by contract with the organisation."},"clip":"B1.2-S05-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Let the team use the clearer form now, because the check itself is unchanged and the expert approved that check last year.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have seen correctly that the content of the check has not changed, and that is why the revision will be examined for approval. What the expert approved last year is the procedure as written, including the sentence Daniel found ambiguous. A new wording changes what the agents do on the spot, so it is part of the procedure and goes through the same examination. Last year's approval covers last year's text; the clearer text gets its own.","screen":"Approval covers the procedure as written. A new wording is examined before it is used."},"clip":"B1.2-S05-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Keep the current form in use, and send the proposal to the recognised organisation, which has one of its experts examine it; the team uses the clearer form as soon as that approval is in.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. Our contract is with the organisation, and the organisation provides a recognised expert; one expert's holiday does not pause our contract. So I send the proposal to the organisation and ask it to have the examination done, and until the approval is in, the current form stays in use. That is coordinating in full: the proposal moves, the versions stay apart, and the team knows which form applies on every day in between.","screen":"Contract with the organisation; it provides the expert. Current form until the approval is in."},"clip":"B1.2-S05-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.2-S05-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S05-P1","B1.2-S05-P2","B1.2-S05-P3","B1.2-S05-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.2-S05-P4","interaction_id":"B1.2-S05-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S06","title":"Training has several different jobs to do","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S06-P1","text":"That brings us to Daniel's message: he passed the agent course, so can he be the agent on his own now? To answer that properly I have to separate several things that people lump together as \"training\". They have different purposes and different evidence, and each one has to be there on its own.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"That brings us to Daniel's message: he passed the agent cour","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"To answer that properly I have to separate several things th","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"They have different purposes and different evidence, and eac","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.2-S06-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S06-P2","text":"The first thing Daniel received, before he worked in radiography at all, was our own four-hour initial instruction: how we work, which safety equipment we use and how, dosimeters, survey meters, dose-rate meters, the bunker equipment here and at our clients. The industrial radiography decree wants that given by a radiographer with at least three years of professional experience who knows our installations. Then there is the general information every exposed worker receives before starting at the workstation: the health risks, the rules of good practice, what the signs mean, what to do in an emergency. It is written down, and we refresh it at least once a year. The full list is in the reference reader; what matters for you is to recognise it when it is missing.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"The first thing Daniel received, before he worked in radiogr","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The industrial radiography decree wants that given by a radi","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"It is written down, and we refresh it at least once a year.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The full list is in the reference reader; what matters for y","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S06-P2"},{"cue":"B1.2-S06-P3","text":"Next, training for the actual job. On top of that general information, the operator organises training aimed at the person's own workstation or function, and at the devices and substances he uses. It happens on recruitment, when someone changes function, when a work tool is changed or introduced, and when a new technology arrives, and it is repeated as needs require and documented. So when Daniel moves from our X-ray sets to a gamma projector he has not used before, that is a new device, and it asks for its own training. Experience with one device is evidence for that device.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Next, training for the actual job.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"On top of that general information, the operator organises t","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"So when Daniel moves from our X-ray sets to a gamma projecto","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Experience with one device is evidence for that device.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S06-P3"},{"cue":"B1.2-S06-P4","text":"Then the agent course, which is what Daniel's message is about. The general regulation sets the floor: a certificate based on a passed knowledge test, proving a theoretical basic training of at least eight hours, supplemented by at least eight hours for class two establishments, together with relevant practical experience in physical control for the type of installation, and continuing training afterwards. The Agency's training regulation fills that in for our kind of company. Because we work with both X-ray devices and sealed sources, our radiographers follow the combined route: twelve hours of basic training and twelve hours of supplementary training covering devices and sources together. The theory is supplemented by practical training or experience in the installation type, the programme is approved by a recognised expert, and class two agents follow at least four hours of continuing training a year. For radiographers the decree places the agent training within three months of entering service, and without it nobody manipulates gamma or X-ray equipment.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Then the agent course, which is what Daniel's message is abo","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The Agency's training regulation fills that in for our kind ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Because we work with both X-ray devices and sealed sources, ","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"For radiographers the decree places the agent training withi","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S06-P4"},{"cue":"B1.2-S06-P5","text":"And finally designation. Training makes someone eligible. The company's decision to name him as the agent for a worksite is a separate act, recorded in the planning, taken when the evidence for that person, that installation and that day is there. All of this happens during working time and at the operator's cost. For external workers who come from another company, the division between their employer and us needs its own attention; that is a later lesson, and I keep it out of Daniel's case.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"And finally designation.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Training makes someone eligible.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"All of this happens during working time and at the operator'","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"For external workers who come from another company, the divi","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S06-P5"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S06-P1","B1.2-S06-P2","B1.2-S06-P3","B1.2-S06-P4","B1.2-S06-P5"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S07","title":"What does Daniel's certificate establish?","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S07-P1","text":"Daniel's folder currently holds one document: the certificate from his agent course, based on a passed knowledge test, combined route, twelve plus twelve hours. It is a real achievement and I want him to feel that. Now read it for what it proves. It answers one of the requirements we just walked through: the theory. It says nothing yet about practical training or experience with our projectors, nothing about the workplace instruction for our installations, and nothing about a company decision to designate him. An empty line in the folder is not a failure; it is something I still have to establish.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Daniel's folder currently holds one document: the certificat","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Now read it for what it proves.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"It answers one of the requirements we just walked through: t","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"An empty line in the folder is not a failure; it is somethin","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S07-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S07-P2","text":"So my reply to Daniel is: well done, and here is what we establish next, and who decides. And then the planner's message and Daniel's message meet. Sofia, who was scheduled as the second radiographer on Thursday, is ill. Thursday is a gamma job at a client's site. Luc proposes a solution: \"Daniel has his certificate, he has done three X-ray jobs with me and he was good. Put him down as the agent for Thursday.\"","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"So my reply to Daniel is: well done, and here is what we est","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Sofia, who was scheduled as the second radiographer on Thurs","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Thursday is a gamma job at a client's site.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Put him down as the agent for Thursday.\"","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S07-P2"},{"cue":"B1.2-S07-P3","text":"Luc is not being careless; he is doing what an experienced colleague does, solving Thursday. Read his proposal against the layers of evidence from the last scene: the certificate, the training for the device Daniel will actually use, the workplace instruction, and the designation. Then decide what Thursday needs.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Luc is not being careless; he is doing what an experienced c","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Read his proposal against the layers of evidence from the la","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Then decide what Thursday needs.","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.2-S07-P3"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.2-S07-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b12":true,"title_visible":"Can Daniel be the agent on Thursday?","prompt_spoken_once":"Can Daniel be designated as the agent for Thursday, and what decides it?","situation_visible_text":"Thursday is a gamma job at a client's site. Sofia is ill. Daniel has his agent certificate and three X-ray jobs with Luc. Luc proposes to put Daniel down as the agent for Thursday.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Only if his file also shows the practical training or experience for the projector and the workplace instruction for that equipment; then the designation is a company decision, recorded in the planning.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. Luc has given us two true things: the theory is proven by the certificate, and Daniel has practical experience, with X-ray sets. Thursday is a gamma job. The training for the device a person actually uses is a separate layer, and so is the workplace instruction for that equipment; experience with one device is evidence for that device. When those two are in the file for the projector, the company can designate him, and that decision is written in the planning. If they are not, Thursday needs another agent, and Daniel's path continues on a job with Luc on the projector.","screen":"Certificate plus device training plus workplace instruction, then a recorded company decision."},"clip":"B1.2-S07-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Yes, provided a second experienced radiographer is present, because work outside the bunker is always done by two radiographers anyway.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You remembered the rule from the first lesson correctly: outside a bunker there are always at least two industrial radiographers. That rule is about the work. The designation of the agent is about one person: the company names someone who has followed the agent training and who is prepared for that installation. A second radiographer standing next to Daniel adds safety to the job; it does not add the projector training to Daniel's file. Two separate requirements, each shown on its own.","screen":"Two radiographers is a rule for the work. Designation is about the person's own evidence."},"clip":"B1.2-S07-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Yes: the certificate proves the theory and the three X-ray jobs prove the practice, so the company can designate him for Thursday.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have the two layers Luc named, and you have them right. The layer that is missing is the one Thursday is about. The three jobs were on X-ray sets; Thursday is a gamma projector. Training for the actual device and the workplace instruction for it are separate requirements, documented separately. For an X-ray job, his relevant experience is one part of the evidence; the other training requirements and the company designation still have to be established. For the projector, the file needs its own line first.","screen":"Practice counts for the device it was done on. A gamma job needs the projector evidence."},"clip":"B1.2-S07-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.2-S07-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S07-P1","B1.2-S07-P2","B1.2-S07-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.2-S07-P3","interaction_id":"B1.2-S07-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S08","title":"One person, more than one function","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S08-P1","text":"Suppose a few weeks have passed. Daniel's practical experience on the projector and his workplace instruction are documented, and the company has designated him as the agent on a worksite. He is now both: the radiographer doing the radiography, and the agent for that site. When he positions the device and makes the exposure, the operational duties of a radiographer apply. When he checks that the protection perimeter is set up as the procedure requires, he is exercising the agent function under the approved procedure. Same person, two functions, and at every decision we can say which one is at work.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Suppose a few weeks have passed.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"He is now both: the radiographer doing the radiography, and ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"When he positions the device and makes the exposure, the ope","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Same person, two functions, and at every decision we can say","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S08-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S08-P2","text":"The same is true higher up the chart. I am also the company's quality and safety manager, and I have been formally appointed to head the physical control service. The letters on my business card create neither function; the appointments do. In a small company one name appears in several places, and that is legitimate when the conditions for each function are met.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"The same is true higher up the chart.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"I am also the company's quality and safety manager, and I ha","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The letters on my business card create neither function; the","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"In a small company one name appears in several places, and t","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S08-P2"},{"cue":"B1.2-S08-P3","text":"What we avoid is the shortcut: assuming that a senior title brings every power on the chart with it. A head of service who is also quality manager still has the head's powers and the quality manager's, each within its own appointment. Hold on to that; at the end of this lesson you will meet an appointment with a name very close to ours that belongs to a different decree altogether.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"What we avoid is the shortcut: assuming that a senior title ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"A head of service who is also quality manager still has the ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Hold on to that; at the end of this lesson you will meet an ","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.2-S08-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S08-P1","B1.2-S08-P2","B1.2-S08-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S09","title":"When a check does not pass: who has to hear","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S09-P1","text":"Now a situation rather than a document. Daniel is the designated agent on a worksite. Before the first exposure he performs the pre-use check on the survey meter, and the meter fails its function check. The device has not been positioned and no exposure has been made. We know the observation. We do not know the cause, and we have no reason to think anyone has been exposed. That is enough to require action, and it is too little to invent a diagnosis.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Now a situation rather than a document.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Before the first exposure he performs the pre-use check on t","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"We know the observation.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"That is enough to require action, and it is too little to in","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S09-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S09-P2","text":"In the first lesson you saw the reflex: stop, report, reassess. Today the question is more precise: who exactly has to hear, and in which capacity. Three provisions come together, and each names different people. The general regulation puts a duty on every worker: follow the instructions, never expose yourself unnecessarily, never damage or remove protective means, and report immediately, at least to the physical control service, every irregularity or defect in the protective means. You do not need an agent title for that duty; it belongs to everyone.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"In the first lesson you saw the reflex: stop, report, reasse","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Today the question is more precise: who exactly has to hear,","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The general regulation puts a duty on every worker: follow t","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"You do not need an agent title for that duty; it belongs to ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S09-P2"},{"cue":"B1.2-S09-P3","text":"The agent's list adds a task on top: informing the head of the physical control service and the recognised expert of every abnormal situation. And the industrial radiography decree tells radiographers to stop the radiography when safe working is not possible and to report that immediately, with the reason, to their hierarchical superior, to the head of the physical control service and to the client's contact person. So Daniel, in one morning, is three things at once: a worker who reports a defect, an agent who informs the head and the expert, and a radiographer who tells his supervisor and the client. The service is the one address that appears in all three.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"The agent's list adds a task on top: informing the head of t","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"And the industrial radiography decree tells radiographers to","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"So Daniel, in one morning, is three things at once: a worker","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The service is the one address that appears in all three.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S09-P3"},{"cue":"B1.2-S09-P4","text":"That is why our procedure for this case routes everything through the service, and I tell you its condition so you never have to guess: a failed instrument is reported to the service before any exposure, the service makes sure the expert is informed, and the service decides whether the work continues with a checked replacement. Daniel takes the protective action his instruction assigns, he calls the service on the worksite line, and he keeps the boundary around technical work he is not authorised or competent to do. And he describes what he saw, not what he supposes.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"That is why our procedure for this case routes everything th","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Daniel takes the protective action his instruction assigns, ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"And he describes what he saw, not what he supposes.","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.2-S09-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S09-P1","B1.2-S09-P2","B1.2-S09-P3","B1.2-S09-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S10","title":"The spare meter in the van","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S10-P1","text":"Keep the facts in mind: Daniel is the designated, prepared agent; the survey meter failed its function check; no exposure has been made; the cause is unknown. Now one more fact. There is a second survey meter in the van, calibrated, and Daniel runs its pre-use check: it passes.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Keep the facts in mind: Daniel is the designated, prepared a","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Now one more fact.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"There is a second survey meter in the van, calibrated, and D","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.2-S10-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S10-P2","text":"Luc, on the phone: \"Then there's nothing to report, is there? You've got a working meter, start the job.\" Daniel is not sure. He has a passing meter in his hand and a failed one on the table, and three provisions in his head. What does he do?","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Luc, on the phone: \"Then there's nothing to report, is there","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"You've got a working meter, start the job.\" Daniel is not su","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"He has a passing meter in his hand and a failed one on the t","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"What does he do?","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S10-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.2-S10-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b12":true,"title_visible":"A working meter, a failed meter","prompt_spoken_once":"Daniel has a working meter and a failed one. What does he do before the first exposure?","situation_visible_text":"The first survey meter failed its function check. The spare meter from the van passes its pre-use check. No exposure has been made. Luc says there is nothing to report and the job can start.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Start with the spare meter, since its check passed, and note the failed meter in the van's logbook so the service can read it at the next review.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"The spare meter does solve the measuring problem, and Daniel was right to run its own pre-use check first; that is the agent's task done properly. What stays open is the failed meter. A defect in the protective means is reported immediately, at least to the service, and as agent Daniel also informs the head and the expert. A logbook entry is a record for later; the duty is to report now, so that the failed meter is taken out of use and the question whether the job continues is answered by the people the procedure names.","screen":"The spare solves the measurement. The failed meter is reported now, not at the next review."},"clip":"B1.2-S10-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Report the failed meter now to the service, Luc and the client's contact person, take it out of use, and start only when the service confirms that the job continues with the checked spare.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. Three duties, one phone call. The failed meter is an irregularity in the protective means, so it is reported immediately, at least to the service; as agent Daniel makes sure the head and the expert hear, which our procedure routes through the service; and as the radiographer who halted the work he tells Luc and the client's contact person. The failed meter is tagged out so nobody picks it up. Whether the job continues with the spare is the service's decision under our procedure, and when that confirmation comes, Daniel starts with a meter that passed its own check.","screen":"Report now, tag out the failed meter; the service decides on continuing with the spare."},"clip":"B1.2-S10-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Stop the job for today, because an irregularity in the protective means means no exposure until the recognised expert has looked at the failed meter.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have the reporting right, and you are right that the expert has to be informed. The step you have added is waiting for her. The expert is informed through the service, and she will look at the meter question; the decision whether today's work continues with a checked replacement is taken under our procedure by the service, not tied to the expert's visit. Stopping the day would be the correct outcome if the service decided it. Here Daniel reports, and lets the people the procedure names decide.","screen":"The expert is informed via the service. Continuing with the spare is the service's decision."},"clip":"B1.2-S10-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.2-S10-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S10-P1","B1.2-S10-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.2-S10-P2","interaction_id":"B1.2-S10-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S11","title":"A handover the next person can act on","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S11-P1","text":"Daniel has done the right things. Now he has to say them in a way the next person can act on, and that is a skill of its own. A handover in a situation like this has four parts: what was observed, what has been done, who has been contacted and who is still being contacted, and what is still unknown. Four parts, and nobody has claimed a cause or a dose.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Daniel has done the right things.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Now he has to say them in a way the next person can act on, ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"A handover in a situation like this has four parts: what was","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Four parts, and nobody has claimed a cause or a dose.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S11-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S11-P2","text":"Watch what each part does for the receiver. The observation tells me what I am dealing with: a meter that failed its function check. The actions tell me the state of the site: exposure held, device untouched. The contacts tell me who already knows and whom I still have to reach, so nobody is called twice and nobody is forgotten. And the unknown is the most important line of the four: it tells me what the expert has to decide, and it keeps the handover true whatever the cause turns out to be. Those four parts come back in the lesson on abnormal events and reporting, where time limits and the Agency's criteria get their own treatment. Today the point is organisational: a clear handover lets the person with the next responsibility act.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Watch what each part does for the receiver.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The actions tell me the state of the site: exposure held, de","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"And the unknown is the most important line of the four: it t","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Today the point is organisational: a clear handover lets the","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S11-P2"},{"cue":"B1.2-S11-P3","text":"Daniel has written three versions of his call to me on the worksite record. All three are polite, all three mention the failed check. Read them as the person who has to act on them, and pick the one you could act on without first calling him back.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Daniel has written three versions of his call to me on the w","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"All three are polite, all three mention the failed check.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Read them as the person who has to act on them, and pick the","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.2-S11-P3"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.2-S11-R01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b12":true,"title_visible":"Three versions of the same call","prompt_spoken_once":"Which of the three handovers can I act on as it stands?","situation_visible_text":"Daniel has written three versions of his handover to the head of the service after the failed meter check. The spare meter has passed its check. The service has not yet decided whether the job continues.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"\"Emilia, Daniel at the pipe-rack site. The survey meter failed its function check during the pre-use check; the device is not positioned, no exposure. I've told Luc and the client contact. I'm calling the expert now so she has it first-hand, and I'll call you back with what she says.\"","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"This handover has the observation, the state of the site and two of the contacts, and all of it is true. The one line to change is the route to the expert. The agent's duty is that the head and the expert are informed, and our procedure routes that through the service: Daniel reports to me, and the service makes sure the expert hears, with the facts in one place. A radiographer calling the expert directly leaves me waiting for a decision I am supposed to organise. Same facts, one call fewer, and the handover is complete.","screen":"Facts right; the expert is informed through the service, not by Daniel directly."},"clip":"B1.2-S11-R01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"\"Emilia, Daniel at the pipe-rack site. The first survey meter failed its check; the battery is faulty, so I've swapped to the spare, which passes. Luc and the client contact know. We're ready to start at ten unless you say otherwise.\"","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"This is the handover of someone who wants to solve the problem, and the spare meter's check is exactly right. Two lines go beyond what Daniel knows. \"The battery is faulty\" is a cause nobody has established; the honest line is that the cause is open. And \"we start at ten unless you say otherwise\" lifts the hold himself, where our procedure gives the decision to continue to the service. Keep the observation, label the suspicion as a suspicion, and ask for the decision instead of announcing it.","screen":"Cause stated as fact, hold lifted by the sender. Keep the cause open and ask for the decision."},"clip":"B1.2-S11-R01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"\"Emilia, Daniel at the pipe-rack site. The survey meter failed its function check during the pre-use check; the device is not positioned, no exposure. The failed meter is tagged out; the spare passed its own check. Luc and the client contact know. The cause is unknown. I'm waiting for the service's decision on continuing with the spare.\"","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. Observed, done, contacted, unknown, and then the question that is mine to answer. I know what happened, I know the site is held and the failed meter is out of circulation, I know who has been told and that the expert is still to be informed by me, and I know the one thing nobody knows yet. I can act on this as it stands: inform the expert, decide on the spare under the procedure, and call Daniel back. A handover like this stays true whether the cause turns out to be the battery, the meter or something else.","screen":"Observed, done, contacted, unknown. The receiver can act without calling back."},"clip":"B1.2-S11-R01-c"}],"layout":"handover_documents","clip":"B1.2-S11-R01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S11-P1","B1.2-S11-P2","B1.2-S11-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.2-S11-P3","interaction_id":"B1.2-S11-R01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S12","title":"A role with a similar name: the delegate for radiological security","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S12-P1","text":"One more message arrived this week, and it came through the planner from Bram. His company is preparing for a gamma job on its site, and his question was: \"Who is your delegate for radiological security for the sources you bring to us?\" It is a good question, and it is about a role that sounds like ours and belongs to a different decree. Belgium has a separate royal decree of the seventeenth of March, twenty twenty-four, on the security of radioactive substances and certain nuclear materials; colleagues call it RAMAS. Radiation protection is about controlling exposure. Security is about preventing unauthorised removal, malicious acts and misuse of radioactive substances. The two meet in our work, and their responsibilities are separate.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"One more message arrived this week, and it came through the ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Belgium has a separate royal decree of the seventeenth of Ma","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Radiation protection is about controlling exposure.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The two meet in our work, and their responsibilities are sep","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S12-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S12-P2","text":"Where does the security decree apply? To radioactive substances, whether or not placed in a device, above the exemption levels, in establishments of class one, two or three, and also to radioactive substances used in a mobile installation or in temporary work licensed under the general regulation. That second part is us: our gamma projectors contain sealed sources, and we take them to worksites. An X-ray set contains no radioactive substance, so an X-ray-only activity is outside this decree, even though it produces ionising radiation. What applies to a given source depends on its category under the decree, and that category follows from the licensed radioactive activity and the categorisation rules under the decree, not from a meter reading or from the words \"class two\". For the lowest categories, four and five, only a few of the decree's articles apply.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Where does the security decree apply?","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"That second part is us: our gamma projectors contain sealed ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"An X-ray set contains no radioactive substance, so an X-ray-","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"For the lowest categories, four and five, only a few of the ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S12-P2"},{"cue":"B1.2-S12-P3","text":"Now the role Bram asked about. Under the security decree the operator appoints, within its establishment or organisation, at least one delegate for radiological security, the ARB, who works for the operator in a durable way, whether or not as an employee. That appointment is subject to the Agency's approval: the Agency may approve it, with or without conditions, or refuse it, looking at the person's qualifications, experience, security training, and his status, position and means within the establishment. The ARB sets up and maintains the radiological security system on behalf of and under the responsibility of the operator, and where relevant does so in consultation with the head of the physical control service. So the ARB and I talk to each other, and we are two different appointments.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Now the role Bram asked about.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Under the security decree the operator appoints, within its ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The ARB sets up and maintains the radiological security syst","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"So the ARB and I talk to each other, and we are two differen","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S12-P3"},{"cue":"B1.2-S12-P4","text":"One duty from that decree you should know even now: anyone who observes a malicious act must immediately inform the operator or the ARB. That belongs to every person, whatever their title. The later lesson on abnormal events shows how security incidents are reported onward. For today, notice how to recognise a request for a separate role, rather than one more routine task for the people you already know.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"One duty from that decree you should know even now: anyone w","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"That belongs to every person, whatever their title.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The later lesson on abnormal events shows how security incid","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"For today, notice how to recognise a request for a separate ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S12-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S12-P1","B1.2-S12-P2","B1.2-S12-P3","B1.2-S12-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S13","title":"Who answers Bram's question?","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S13-P1","text":"Back to Bram's question: who is our delegate for radiological security for the sources we bring to his site? Our planner has drafted a reply, and the draft names Daniel, with the reasoning: he is the designated agent for that worksite and the source will be in his care that day. Luc, reading over the planner's shoulder, suggests my name instead: the ARB consults the head of the physical control service, so it must be me.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Back to Bram's question: who is our delegate for radiologica","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Our planner has drafted a reply, and the draft names Daniel,","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Luc, reading over the planner's shoulder, suggests my name i","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.2-S13-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S13-P2","text":"On my desk lie two appointment documents side by side: the planning line that records Daniel's designation as radiation protection agent, and the ARB appointment with its field for the Agency's approval. Same company, two decrees behind the two pieces of paper. Read them, and tell the planner what to answer.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"On my desk lie two appointment documents side by side: the p","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Same company, two decrees behind the two pieces of paper.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Read them, and tell the planner what to answer.","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.2-S13-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.2-S13-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b12":true,"title_visible":"Who is our delegate for radiological security?","prompt_spoken_once":"What does the planner answer Bram?","situation_visible_text":"Bram asks who our delegate for radiological security is for the sources we bring to his site. The planner's draft names Daniel, the designated agent. Luc suggests Emilia, the head of the service. Two appointment documents lie on the desk.","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The name of the person our company appointed as delegate for radiological security, an appointment the Agency has approved; Daniel's designation and my function are different appointments under a different decree.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. Bram asked for a role under the security decree, so the answer is the person who holds that appointment: appointed by the operator, approved by the Agency after looking at qualifications, experience, security training and position. Daniel's designation is a radiation-protection decision for one worksite; my appointment is the head of the service. The ARB consults me where relevant, and that contact is exactly what tells you the two are different people on the chart. The planner looks the name up and answers with that.","screen":"The ARB is a separate appointment, approved by the Agency. Agent and head of service are other appointments."},"clip":"B1.2-S13-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Daniel, because he is the designated agent for that worksite and the source is in his care on that day.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"The planner's reasoning starts from something true: on the day, the source is in Daniel's care, and as agent he checks that the protection rules are followed. His designation is a radiation-protection decision, recorded in our planning, for one worksite. The delegate for radiological security is an appointment under the security decree, made by the operator and approved by the Agency on security qualifications. Looking after a source well on Thursday is Daniel's job; being our ARB is somebody's appointment.","screen":"Agent designation is a planning decision for radiation protection. The ARB is an appointment under the security decree."},"clip":"B1.2-S13-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Emilia, because the delegate for radiological security works in consultation with the head of the physical control service, so the two functions meet in the same person.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Luc has spotted a real link: the ARB sets up the security system in consultation with the head of the physical control service, where relevant. Consultation is between two functions, and it works precisely because they are two. Heading the service is an appointment under the general regulation; the ARB is an appointment under the security decree, each with its own conditions and its own approval. The same person can hold both only when both sets of conditions are met and both appointments have been made. In our company they are two people, and the planner names the right one.","screen":"Consultation links two functions; it does not merge them."},"clip":"B1.2-S13-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.2-S13-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S13-P1","B1.2-S13-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.2-S13-P2","interaction_id":"B1.2-S13-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S14","title":"Bring the responsibilities together","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.2-S14-P1","text":"Let us return to the three messages, and now you can answer them yourself. Who is the agent on Thursday? A radiographer who will actually be there, trained as an agent, prepared for that installation, named by the company and written in the planning. Can the team use the revised check form? When the recognised expert, provided by the organisation we contract, has examined and approved it; until then the current version applies, whoever is on holiday. Can Daniel be the agent on his own? His certificate proves the theory; the training for the device he will use, the workplace instruction and the company's designation are established next to it, and then yes.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Let us return to the three messages, and now you can answer ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"A radiographer who will actually be there, trained as an age","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"When the recognised expert, provided by the organisation we ","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"His certificate proves the theory; the training for the devi","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S14-P1"},{"cue":"B1.2-S14-P2","text":"Underneath all three is the same habit: ask what a piece of evidence establishes and who holds the next decision. Today you have learned the conditions behind the names from the first lesson. Who may lead the service, and that leading means coordinating, with a direct line to the top. That approval of our procedures is the expert's task, placed by contract with an organisation that remains bound to us. That the Agency supervises the service itself. That the agent checks on the basis of approved procedures, and that a record and an approval answer different questions. That training comes in layers, each with its own evidence, and that designation is a separate decision. That when a check fails, three duties name three sets of people, and the service is the address they share. That a handover has four parts: observed, done, contacted, unknown. And that the delegate for radiological security is a different appointment, approved by the Agency, under a different decree.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Underneath all three is the same habit: ask what a piece of ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"That approval of our procedures is the expert's task, placed","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"That training comes in layers, each with its own evidence, a","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"And that the delegate for radiological security is a differe","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.2-S14-P2"},{"cue":"B1.2-S14-P3","text":"In the next lesson we leave the people for the paperwork that lets a company like ours exist at all: the licence, the bunker and its conformity, commissioning, and what happens when something about the installation changes. You will find the same people there, doing the things we have just taken apart. I'll see you then.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.2 scenario","beats":[{"at":"In the next lesson we leave the people for the paperwork tha","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"You will find the same people there, doing the things we hav","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"I'll see you then.","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.2-S14-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.2-S14-P1","B1.2-S14-P2","B1.2-S14-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}}]},{"id":"B1.3","title":"Licence, bunker and commissioning","scenes":[{"id":"S01","title":"Welcome back: from the people to the paperwork","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.3-S01-P1","text":"Welcome back. In the last lesson you took the people apart: who decides, who approves, who has to hear. Today we look at what lets a company like ours work with radiation at all: the licence, the walls, and the papers that turn a room and a machine into something we may actually use. And for each paper we ask the question you already know: what does it prove?","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Welcome back.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"In the last lesson you took the people apart: who decides, w","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Today we look at what lets a company like ours work with rad","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"And for each paper we ask the question you already know: wha","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S01-P1"},{"cue":"B1.3-S01-P2","text":"You will hear the phrase \"everything is approved\" on many worksites. By the end of this lesson you will be able to replace it with something precise: what our licence permits and under which conditions, what had to be favourable before an installation could be put into service, what makes a room a bunker in the sense of the law, what effective protection means in the regulation's own words, and what happens when somebody wants to change something. You will not learn here how to test or operate the equipment. You will learn to say what the evidence supports.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"You will hear the phrase \"everything is approved\" on many wo","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"By the end of this lesson you will be able to replace it wit","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"You will not learn here how to test or operate the equipment","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"You will learn to say what the evidence supports.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S01-P2"},{"cue":"B1.3-S01-P3","text":"I'll use two installations. The first is our own radiography bunker at the company's premises, which you have seen from the inside. The second is new: an X-ray cabinet at a client who inspects small castings in-house, in a foundry. The two sit in different classes under the regulation, and that difference is the easiest way into the licensing rules.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"I'll use two installations.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The first is our own radiography bunker at the company's pre","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The second is new: an X-ray cabinet at a client who inspects","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The two sit in different classes under the regulation, and t","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S01-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.3-S01-P1","B1.3-S01-P2","B1.3-S01-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S02","title":"Our licence: how we got it and what it covers","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.3-S02-P1","text":"Start with our own company. The general regulation sorts establishments into classes, and the class decides the route to a licence. Class two includes, among others, installations with X-ray devices whose nominal peak voltage exceeds two hundred kilovolts, and establishments that hold or use radioactive sources for industrial radiography without being exempt. Both apply to us, so we are a class two establishment, and a class two establishment holds an establishment and operating licence granted by the Agency.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Start with our own company.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The general regulation sorts establishments into classes, an","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Class two includes, among others, installations with X-ray d","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Both apply to us, so we are a class two establishment, and a","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S02-P1"},{"cue":"B1.3-S02-P2","text":"How did we get it? The application went to the Agency after it had been examined and approved by a recognised expert in physical control of class one or two, either an employee of the future operator or an expert from a recognised organisation. For us that was the organisation we still contract. The dossier describes the establishment, its installations, its sources and its practices in enough detail for the Agency to decide, and the Agency's decision is the licence.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"How did we get it?","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The application went to the Agency after it had been examine","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"For us that was the organisation we still contract.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The dossier describes the establishment, its installations, ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S02-P2"},{"cue":"B1.3-S02-P3","text":"In the first lesson Daniel opened our licence to see whether he could bring a particular X-ray set to a client. Today I want you to read it for two further things. First, for a type of practice, the licence granted counts as proof of justification: the question whether this kind of work is justified at all was answered when the Agency granted it, which is why Bram's file had to justify his specific assignment and not radiography as such. Second, the licence is exactly as wide as its own inventory and its own conditions, and nothing wider. An installation, a source or a practice that is not in it is, for the moment, not licensed. We come back to that at the end of the lesson, under changes.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"In the first lesson Daniel opened our licence to see whether","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"First, for a type of practice, the licence granted counts as","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Second, the licence is exactly as wide as its own inventory ","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"We come back to that at the end of the lesson, under changes","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S02-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.3-S02-P1","B1.3-S02-P2","B1.3-S02-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S03","title":"The foundry's cabinet: the class three route","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.3-S03-P1","text":"Now the client. The foundry wants to inspect small castings itself, so it has bought an enclosed X-ray cabinet. Its device does not exceed two hundred kilovolts, it is not one of the installations listed for class two, and it is not exempt from declaration and licensing. Installations with devices that can produce ionising radiation and fall outside the class two list, without being exempt, place the establishment in class three. I am giving you that classification as a fact of this example; in real life it is the expert's dossier, and not the look of the cabinet, that settles it.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Now the client.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The foundry wants to inspect small castings itself, so it ha","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Installations with devices that can produce ionising radiati","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"I am giving you that classification as a fact of this exampl","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S03-P1"},{"cue":"B1.3-S03-P2","text":"For class three the route is different. The operator submits a declaration to the Agency, in writing or in printable electronic form, after a recognised expert of class one or two has examined and approved it. The Agency grants the establishment and operating licence if the declaration meets the conditions set out in the regulation, and it rules within a set period: thirty calendar days after receiving the waste agency's reasoned opinion where that applies, or sixty calendar days after receiving the dossier, or a longer period that it has to justify. So for class three too, the licence is the Agency's decision; the declaration is the operator's request for it.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"For class three the route is different.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The operator submits a declaration to the Agency, in writing","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The Agency grants the establishment and operating licence if","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"So for class three too, the licence is the Agency's decision","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S03-P2"},{"cue":"B1.3-S03-P3","text":"That difference is where this week's email comes from. The foundry's office manager writes to me: \"The installer finishes on Monday. Our expert signed the declaration and we sent it to the Agency last week, so we're licensed. Can your people come on Monday and take the first test radiographs with us?\" Luc, who likes a Monday job, says the expert's signature is what counts. Our planner asks me what the foundry's situation actually is.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"That difference is where this week's email comes from.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The foundry's office manager writes to me: \"The installer fi","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Can your people come on Monday and take the first test radio","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Our planner asks me what the foundry's situation actually is","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S03-P3"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.3-S03-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b13":true,"title_visible":"Is the foundry licensed?","situation_visible_text":"The foundry's expert approved the declaration for the X-ray cabinet, and the foundry sent it to the Agency last week. The installer finishes on Monday. The office manager writes that they are licensed and asks us to come on Monday.","prompt_spoken_once":"What is the foundry's situation on Monday?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The declaration was sent and the expert approved it, so the cabinet is licensed and may be used as soon as the installer has finished.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have the first step right, and it is a real one: an expert-approved declaration is what the Agency needs in order to grant a class three licence. The step after it belongs to the Agency. It rules within thirty or sixty calendar days, or longer with reasons, and its decision is the licence. On Monday the foundry has a receipt for its declaration and no licence yet to read for scope and conditions. So Monday is the installer's day, and ours comes after the Agency's letter.","screen":"Declaration sent is step one. The licence is the Agency's decision, still to come."},"clip":"B1.3-S03-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"For class three the expert's approval of the declaration is the licence; the Agency registers it, so the foundry is right that it is licensed.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have spotted something true about class three: the expert's examination and approval come first, and without them the declaration goes nowhere. The licence itself is still granted by the Agency, which checks that the declaration meets the conditions and rules within its set period. The expert's signature opens the Agency's file; the Agency's decision closes it. Until that decision, the foundry has an approved declaration and a waiting period.","screen":"Expert approval opens the file. The Agency grants the licence."},"clip":"B1.3-S03-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"The declaration is with the Agency, which has thirty or sixty calendar days to rule; until its decision arrives there is no licence to read, and Monday is for the installer only.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. The declaration and the licence are two different pieces of paper, separated by a decision of the Agency. The foundry has done its part well: an expert-approved declaration, sent on time. What it is waiting for is the Agency's letter, with the scope and the conditions it will have to work under. I write back with that chronology, and I add one more thing the office manager has not asked about yet, because even the licence will not be the end of it. That is the next scene.","screen":"Declaration sent, decision pending, licence to come. Monday is the installer's day."},"clip":"B1.3-S03-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.3-S03-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.3-S03-P1","B1.3-S03-P2","B1.3-S03-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.3-S03-P3","interaction_id":"B1.3-S03-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S04","title":"From licence to use: commissioning","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.3-S04-P1","text":"Here is the second distinction the foundry has not met yet, and it applies to our bunker as much as to their cabinet. Once the licence is granted, for a class two establishment other than class two A, or for a class three establishment, the operator has the right, under its own responsibility, to build and fit out the installations in accordance with the licence. That is construction. Putting the installation into service is a separate step with its own conditions.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Here is the second distinction the foundry has not met yet, ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Once the licence is granted, for a class two establishment o","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"That is construction.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Putting the installation into service is a separate step wit","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S04-P1"},{"cue":"B1.3-S04-P2","text":"The regulation says commissioning may take place only if two things hold. First, where the security decree applies, the acceptance of the radiological security system by the delegate for radiological security is favourable. Second, the recognised expert's acceptance of the installation is fully favourable and expressly permits commissioning. And before commissioning, the operator of a class two establishment sends the Agency a document declaring that these conditions have been met.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"The regulation says commissioning may take place only if two","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"First, where the security decree applies, the acceptance of ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Second, the recognised expert's acceptance of the installati","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"And before commissioning, the operator of a class two establ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S04-P2"},{"cue":"B1.3-S04-P3","text":"What is an acceptance, an oplevering? The regulation defines it as the check that the installations or practices conform to the radiation regulations, to the establishment and operating licence, and, where there is one, to the safety report. Notice the three reference points. The expert is asking a precise question: does what was built match what was licensed and what the regulation requires? A supplier's delivery note, an installer's sign-off and a manager's enthusiasm answer a different question, whether the machine works, and that question is not the one commissioning is about.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"What is an acceptance, an oplevering?","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The regulation defines it as the check that the installation","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The expert is asking a precise question: does what was built","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"A supplier's delivery note, an installer's sign-off and a ma","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S04-P3"},{"cue":"B1.3-S04-P4","text":"So for the foundry's cabinet the order is: licence from the Agency, construction and installation, the recognised expert's fully favourable acceptance expressly permitting commissioning, and then use. For our bunker it was the same, with the security acceptance added because our projectors hold sealed sources. I keep the acceptance report with the licence, because together they answer the question \"may this installation be used at all?\", and because a client who asks us to come \"as soon as the installer leaves\" is asking us to skip exactly that step.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"So for the foundry's cabinet the order is: licence from the ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"For our bunker it was the same, with the security acceptance","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"I keep the acceptance report with the licence, because toget","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.3-S04-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.3-S04-P1","B1.3-S04-P2","B1.3-S04-P3","B1.3-S04-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S05","title":"What makes a room a bunker","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.3-S05-P1","text":"Now the walls. In the industrial radiography decree a bunker is more than a thick-walled room: it is a whole with four parts. An enclosure, with or without a roof, whose walls shield the ionising radiation. Various safety devices. Lockable doors or gates. And a control post outside the enclosure that holds the remote control of each radiography device. One more sentence completes the definition: a bunker has a valid conformity certificate drawn up by a recognised expert in physical control. Our company has to make sure that every bunker in which it carries out radiography holds such a certificate, our own and any client's.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Now the walls.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"An enclosure, with or without a roof, whose walls shield the","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"And a control post outside the enclosure that holds the remo","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Our company has to make sure that every bunker in which it c","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S05-P1"},{"cue":"B1.3-S05-P2","text":"\"Various safety devices\" is where the bells and buttons live. The Agency's technical regulation on safety means in industrial radiography sets the minimum a bunker has to have, and the safety logic of each bunker follows from its own risk analysis. Let me walk you through the hardware and the state each item is for. While a door or gate is closing, a signal sounds at the control post and inside the bunker; it begins with the closing, so that anyone inside or near the door is warned while there is still time. A visual signal comes on when, and only when, ionising radiation is present in the exposure room, visible from every point inside and at every entrance. While the set is emitting, access to the room is locked. A locked door must never trap a person, so at least one door or gate is a clearly marked evacuation exit that can always be opened by hand from the inside. At the entrance hangs a description of what the audible and visual alarms mean, and there is emergency lighting. And because our bunker is used with an X-ray set, two more things: a device that enforces a safety walk-round before an exposure, so that nobody is left behind, ending with the doors locked within a time the recognised expert set; and emergency stops inside the room, placed so that one can be reached from any position without crossing the direct beam, with one more at the control post.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"While a door or gate is closing","show":"Safety device 1"},{"at":"A visual signal comes on","show":"Safety device 2"},{"at":"While the set is emitting","show":"Safety device 3"},{"at":"A locked door must never trap","show":"Safety device 4"},{"at":"At the entrance hangs","show":"Safety device 5"},{"at":"there is emergency lighting","show":"Safety device 6"},{"at":"a device that enforces a safety walk-round","show":"Safety device 7"},{"at":"and emergency stops inside","show":"Safety device 8"}],"clip":"B1.3-S05-P2"},{"cue":"B1.3-S05-P3","text":"The certificate turns those parts into proof. The recognised expert checked that the safety requirements are met, and the certificate also says which isotopes and activities, which X-ray voltages and which working configurations are allowed in this bunker. It is valid for ten years at most, it is adapted when the bunker changes, and a copy goes to the Agency. Read those three conditions carefully, because each of them can make a certificate stop being valid while the paper still hangs on the wall: time passes, the bunker changes, or the work asked for falls outside what the certificate allows.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"The certificate turns those parts into proof.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The recognised expert checked that the safety requirements a","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"It is valid for ten years at most, it is adapted when the bu","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Read those three conditions carefully, because each of them ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S05-P3"},{"cue":"B1.3-S05-P4","text":"You met the location rules in the first lesson, with Bram's vessel: small movable workpieces go to a bunker, larger ones preferably, and the hall only after both risk analyses. Here is the companion to that rule from our side. When a client says \"use our bunker\", the first thing I want to see is the certificate, with its date and its scope. When a client says \"do it in the hall\", I want to see the written reasoning for why neither a bunker nor an irradiation infrastructure is reasonably feasible, and the information for our risk analysis. The location decision is the client's to justify; whether the room is a bunker is the certificate's to prove.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"You met the location rules in the first lesson, with Bram's ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Here is the companion to that rule from our side.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"When a client says \"do it in the hall\", I want to see the wr","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The location decision is the client's to justify; whether th","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S05-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.3-S05-P1","B1.3-S05-P2","B1.3-S05-P3","B1.3-S05-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S06","title":"Is it a bunker?","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.3-S06-P1","text":"At a new client's site everyone calls the concrete room at the back of the hall \"the bunker\". It has a heavy sliding door and a control desk outside. The site supervisor is proud of it: \"It was built for this, the walls are half a metre thick, and here is the certificate.\" The certificate is real, drawn up by a recognised expert, dated eight years ago, and it lists X-ray voltages that cover our set.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"At a new client's site everyone calls the concrete room at t","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"It has a heavy sliding door and a control desk outside.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The site supervisor is proud of it: \"It was built for this, ","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.3-S06-P1"},{"cue":"B1.3-S06-P2","text":"Then he adds, helpfully: \"Last year we replaced the old sliding door and its interlock with a new, faster one; the installer tested it and the test report is in the file.\" Daniel has small workpieces to plan for this room next week. Read the certificate against what you just learned, and tell him what has to be true before he plans.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Then he adds, helpfully: \"Last year we replaced the old slid","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Read the certificate against what you just learned, and tell","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.3-S06-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.3-S06-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b13":true,"title_visible":"Eight years old, one new door","situation_visible_text":"The client's room has a conformity certificate from a recognised expert, eight years old, with X-ray voltages that cover our set. Last year the client replaced the sliding door and its interlock. The installer's test report is in the file. Daniel wants to plan small workpieces there next week.","prompt_spoken_once":"What has to be true before Daniel plans small workpieces in that room?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The certificate is valid, because eight years is within the ten-year maximum and the voltages cover our set, so Daniel can plan the work.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have read the certificate for two of its three conditions, and read them correctly: the ten years have not passed, and the scope covers our set. The third condition is the one the supervisor handed us himself. A certificate is adapted when the bunker changes, and a new door with a new interlock is a change to the safety devices the certificate was drawn up for. So the question is whether the certificate was adapted after that change. If it was, Daniel plans. If it was not, the client asks its recognised expert first, and we wait for that.","screen":"Time and scope are fine. A changed door asks for an adapted certificate."},"clip":"B1.3-S06-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"The certificate has to have been adapted by a recognised expert after the door and interlock were replaced; until the client shows that, the room is a bunker with an open question, and Daniel waits.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. The certificate proves the bunker as the expert saw it, and the decree says it is adapted when the bunker changes. A new door and a new interlock are precisely the kind of change that matters, because the interlock is one of the safety devices the certificate stands for. So Daniel asks the client one question: was the certificate adapted after the door was replaced, and may we see it? With that paper, the room is a bunker and the small workpieces go in. Without it, the client's expert has work to do first.","screen":"Bunker changed, certificate adapted. Ask for the adapted certificate before planning."},"clip":"B1.3-S06-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"The door change is covered, because the installer tested the new interlock and the test report is in the file next to the certificate.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"The installer's test is useful, and it is right that it is in the file: it tells us the new interlock worked on the day it was fitted. What it cannot do is extend the certificate, because the certificate is drawn up and adapted by a recognised expert, who checks the whole set of safety requirements against the bunker as it now is. The test report is evidence for the expert's examination; it is the expert's adapted certificate that makes the room a bunker again.","screen":"An installer's test is input for the expert. The adapted certificate is the proof."},"clip":"B1.3-S06-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.3-S06-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.3-S06-P1","B1.3-S06-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.3-S06-P2","interaction_id":"B1.3-S06-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S07","title":"Effective protection: the regulation's own five factors","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.3-S07-P1","text":"Here is where the paperwork meets the physics. The general regulation says that undertakings put protective means in place that make it possible to ensure effective protection as the regulation defines it. And it adds a sentence I want you to keep for the next scene: devices and installations that do not, or no longer, meet the regulation's provisions are taken out of use until the identified deficiencies have been corrected.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Here is where the paperwork meets the physics.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The general regulation says that undertakings put protective","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"And it adds a sentence I want you to keep for the next scene","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.3-S07-P1"},{"cue":"B1.3-S07-P2","text":"The regulation then names five safety factors as fundamental, used alone or together. Protection by distance: the measures needed to prevent people from unintentionally approaching the sources; in our work that is the protection perimeter marked out around an exposure. Protection by shielding the sources: in our trade the projector's shielded container and the collimator are shielding at work, and the regulation adds a condition for the case where shielding is the only protective means relied on, which you will find in the reference reader. Protection of rooms by screens, with any openings in the screens themselves protected: the bunker's walls and door. Protection by preventing contamination: a list of principles for unsealed and sealed sources alike, sealed sources preferred, the smallest quantities, no spreading, no loss or theft, and an accurate inventory that lets every source be located at any moment. And protection by limiting exposure time: the speed of the source movement, the speed of the operation, or the limitation of working time and the rotation of staff.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Protection by distance","show":"Safety factor 1"},{"at":"Protection by shielding the sources","show":"Safety factor 2"},{"at":"Protection of rooms by screens","show":"Safety factor 3"},{"at":"Protection by preventing contamination","show":"Safety factor 4"},{"at":"protection by limiting exposure time","show":"Safety factor 5"}],"clip":"B1.3-S07-P2"},{"cue":"B1.3-S07-P3","text":"One more sentence from the same article, and it should shape how you think about your personal dosimeter. In the study and design of protective means, and in their use in existing installations, priority goes to collective protective means that limit the radiation and contamination level, rather than to individual protective means. The bunker, the interlocks and the perimeter protect everyone present; the dosimeter records what one person received. The dosimeter matters, and protection starts before it.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"One more sentence from the same article, and it should shape","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"In the study and design of protective means, and in their us","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The bunker, the interlocks and the perimeter protect everyon","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The dosimeter matters, and protection starts before it.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S07-P3"},{"cue":"B1.3-S07-P4","text":"So when I ask \"is the protection effective?\" about an installation, I am asking three precise things: which of these factors the design relies on, whether each of them still works as it was accepted, and whether the collective means come first. That is also how the recognised expert's risk analysis and acceptance are organised, and it is why the agent's checks look at protective means, instruments and dosimeters together.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"So when I ask \"is the protection effective?\" about an instal","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"That is also how the recognised expert's risk analysis and a","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.3-S07-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.3-S07-P1","B1.3-S07-P2","B1.3-S07-P3","B1.3-S07-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S08","title":"A failed function and a missing record are different facts","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.3-S08-P1","text":"Now apply that sentence about taking installations out of use. Our bunker's door interlock is one of its safety devices. During the periodic test under the approved procedure, the interlock fails to stop the exposure sequence when the door is opened. That is a protective function that no longer meets the requirements, so the installation goes out of use until the deficiency is corrected. The licence does not change that, and neither does the week's schedule. The failed test is reported immediately, through the route you learned in the last lesson, and the correction is confirmed through the procedure and the expert's involvement, with a satisfactory test on record.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Now apply that sentence about taking installations out of us","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"During the periodic test under the approved procedure, the i","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"That is a protective function that no longer meets the requi","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The failed test is reported immediately, through the route y","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S08-P1"},{"cue":"B1.3-S08-P2","text":"Here is a different fact that deserves the same care in language. This month's interlock test record cannot be found. We know that evidence is missing. We do not know whether the test was done and filed elsewhere, whether it was forgotten, or whether a fault was found and not written up. Two shortcuts offer themselves: fill in a pass because last month looked fine, or report a defective interlock because the folder is incomplete. Both replace an open question with an invented answer, in opposite directions.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Here is a different fact that deserves the same care in lang","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"We know that evidence is missing.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"We do not know whether the test was done and filed elsewhere","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Both replace an open question with an invented answer, in op","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S08-P2"},{"cue":"B1.3-S08-P3","text":"Our procedure says that the relevant satisfactory test has to be established before the bunker is used again. So in the second case use is held as well, for a different reason: the required evidence is not there. Naming the actual gap makes the handover useful: \"the result is not established; use is held under the procedure; please help locate or redo the test.\" That gives the service something specific to do and leaves room for the facts to change when the record turns up. Keep the two cases apart in your head: a function that failed, and a record that is missing. The next scene puts you in the second one.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Our procedure says that the relevant satisfactory test has t","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"So in the second case use is held as well, for a different r","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Keep the two cases apart in your head: a function that faile","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The next scene puts you in the second one.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S08-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.3-S08-P1","B1.3-S08-P2","B1.3-S08-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S09","title":"Sofia remembers the test","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.3-S09-P1","text":"The missing-record case, the same morning. The hold card is on the bunker door: use on hold, this month's interlock test result not established. Sofia, from the late shift, comes in and says: \"I ran that test on Friday, it passed, I just never wrote it up. Sorry.\" Luc, who needs the bunker at ten: \"Then enter Friday's result now, with Friday's date. Sofia's reliable, and the function is fine.\"","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"The missing-record case, the same morning.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The hold card is on the bunker door: use on hold, this month","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Sorry.\" Luc, who needs the bunker at ten: \"Then enter Friday","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Sofia's reliable, and the function is fine.\"","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S09-P1"},{"cue":"B1.3-S09-P2","text":"Sofia's memory is useful, and it is honest. Luc's solution is practical. The decision is mine, as head of the service, under the procedure. Think about what the procedure asks for before use, what a record is, and what we actually know about the interlock this morning.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Sofia's memory is useful, and it is honest.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Luc's solution is practical.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The decision is mine, as head of the service, under the proc","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Think about what the procedure asks for before use, what a r","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S09-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.3-S09-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b13":true,"title_visible":"Friday's test, written up on Monday?","situation_visible_text":"The bunker is on hold because this month's interlock test result is not established. Sofia says she ran the test on Friday and it passed, but never wrote it up. Luc proposes to enter Friday's result now, dated Friday, and use the bunker at ten.","prompt_spoken_once":"What do I decide, as head of the service, before the bunker is used?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"The test is repeated now under the procedure, witnessed by Luc, and the actual result is entered with today's date and both names; the hold comes off when I have reviewed that entry.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. What the procedure asks for before use is an established satisfactory test, and \"established\" means a record: result, date, names, written at the time. Sofia's memory tells me where to look and makes a pass likely; it is not a record, and a line written on Monday with Friday's date would be a record of something nobody can verify. So the test is repeated, witnessed, and entered as what it is: today's result. If it passes, I review the entry and lift the hold. If it fails, we are in the first case, with a defect to correct, and I am glad we repeated it.","screen":"Repeat, witness, record today's result. The record lifts the hold, after review."},"clip":"B1.3-S09-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Sofia enters Friday's result now, dated Friday, with a note that it was written up late; the test was done, so the evidence exists and the hold comes off.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You are right that honesty about the late entry matters, and a note like that is better than a silent backdate. The difficulty is what the line would prove. A record written on Monday about Friday proves that Sofia remembers a pass; nobody can check the function as it was on Friday. The procedure asks for an established result before use, and the only result I can establish this morning is one taken this morning. Repeating the test costs twenty minutes and gives us a record that stands.","screen":"A late entry records a memory. The procedure asks for an established result."},"clip":"B1.3-S09-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"The bunker stays out of use until the interlock has been examined by the recognised expert, because an unrecorded test has to be treated as a failed one.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have kept the hold, and that instinct is right: without an established result, use is held. The reason you have given goes one step too far. A missing record is an evidence gap, and the useful report names it as one; treating it as a failed function sends the expert after a defect nobody has observed. The procedure gives me a simpler route: repeat the test under it, record the actual result, and involve the expert if that result is a failure. Keep the hold, name the gap, redo the test.","screen":"Missing record is a gap, not a failure. Redo the test under the procedure."},"clip":"B1.3-S09-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.3-S09-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.3-S09-P1","B1.3-S09-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.3-S09-P2","interaction_id":"B1.3-S09-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S10","title":"When something changes","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.3-S10-P1","text":"Installations do not stay as they were licensed. A team wants a second projector of a different model, a client asks us to bring a higher-energy X-ray set, the recognised organisation we contract changes. The general regulation says that every change to the establishment which the Agency considers to have a potential impact on radiation protection or safety is declared to the Agency, and, for class two and three, every change with a potential impact on the security of radioactive substances as well. The Agency then decides whether the change requires a licence application under the relevant procedure, and for class two and three it may waive some formalities when the change does not move the establishment into a higher class.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Installations do not stay as they were licensed.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"A team wants a second projector of a different model, a clie","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The general regulation says that every change to the establi","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The Agency then decides whether the change requires a licenc","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S10-P1"},{"cue":"B1.3-S10-P2","text":"The Agency has set the criteria in a technical regulation on the declaration of changes, in force since the third of March, twenty twenty-two. For class two and three establishments other than class two A it does two things. First, our physical control service keeps a list of all changes with a potential impact on radiation protection or radiological safety: for each one a short description, the approvals already given and still needed, and the status of implementation. That list is mine to keep, and it is where every proposal goes first.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"The Agency has set the criteria in a technical regulation on","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"For class two and three establishments other than class two ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"First, our physical control service keeps a list of all chan","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"That list is mine to keep, and it is where every proposal go","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S10-P2"},{"cue":"B1.3-S10-P3","text":"Second, certain changes are declared to the Agency beforehand. Among them: using a radiation source, or holding a radioactive substance, in an installation not licensed for it; carrying out a practice that is not licensed; other changes that fall outside the inventory in the licence; the definitive cessation of a practice with sources; the departure of an internal recognised expert; and a change of the recognised organisation that provides our experts.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Second, certain changes are declared to the Agency beforehan","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Among them: using a radiation source, or holding a radioacti","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.3-S10-P3"},{"cue":"B1.3-S10-P4","text":"The declaration is approved and countersigned by a recognised expert in physical control, except for the purely organisational items such as the expert's departure, the change of organisation, an address change without moving, or a name change of the legal entity. It gives the establishment's unique number and a description of the change, together with the updated parts of the licence dossier that the change affects. And the Agency informs the operator and the head of the physical control service of its decision. So nobody in our company approves a change of this kind: not the team, not me, not the supplier. We recognise it, record it, bring in the expert and declare it. The Agency decides.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"The declaration is approved and countersigned by a recognise","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"And the Agency informs the operator and the head of the phys","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"So nobody in our company approves a change of this kind: not","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The Agency decides.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S10-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.3-S10-P1","B1.3-S10-P2","B1.3-S10-P3","B1.3-S10-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S11","title":"The new X-ray set is in the hall","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.3-S11-P1","text":"Our team proposed an additional X-ray set of a type that is not in our licence's equipment inventory, to use in the bunker for thicker sections. I did what the last scene describes. The set is on our change list as a proposal. The recognised expert examined and countersigned the declaration. The declaration went to the Agency ten days ago. And this morning the supplier delivered the set; it stands in the hall, crated.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Our team proposed an additional X-ray set of a type that is ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The set is on our change list as a proposal.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The recognised expert examined and countersigned the declara","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"And this morning the supplier delivered the set; it stands i","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S11-P1"},{"cue":"B1.3-S11-P2","text":"Luc, looking at the crate: \"The expert signed, the declaration is in, and the bunker certificate allows voltages well above this set. We can start using it in the bunker while the Agency does its paperwork.\" Daniel asks me whether that is right. Read Luc's sentence against the three things it mixes: the expert's countersignature, the bunker certificate, and the Agency's decision.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Luc, looking at the crate: \"The expert signed, the declarati","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"We can start using it in the bunker while the Agency does it","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Read Luc's sentence against the three things it mixes: the e","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.3-S11-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.3-S11-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b13":true,"title_visible":"Declared, delivered, usable?","situation_visible_text":"The new X-ray set is not in the licence inventory. It is on the change list, the expert countersigned the declaration, and the declaration has been with the Agency for ten days. The set has just been delivered. The bunker certificate allows higher voltages than this set. Luc wants to start using it in the bunker.","prompt_spoken_once":"May the team start using the new set in the bunker while the Agency processes the declaration?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Yes: the expert's countersignature is the approval the regulation asks for, and the Agency's letter confirms it afterwards.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have the expert's part exactly right: a declaration of this kind is approved and countersigned by a recognised expert before it goes anywhere. That signature is the condition for declaring, not the decision on the change. The Agency decides whether the change can go ahead as declared or needs a licence application, and it informs the operator and me of that decision. Until that letter, the set is \"declared, pending\" on our list, and it stays in its crate.","screen":"Countersignature makes the declaration complete. The Agency decides on the change."},"clip":"B1.3-S11-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Yes, in the bunker only: the bunker certificate lists the allowed X-ray voltages, and this set is within them, so the bunker is the place where it may be used.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have read the bunker certificate correctly, and it matters: a set with a voltage outside the certificate could never be used in that bunker, whatever the licence says. The certificate answers the question \"what may be used in this room\". The licence answers \"what may this company use at all\", and this set is not in its inventory yet. Two documents, two questions, and the set has to pass both. Today it passes one.","screen":"The certificate covers the room. The licence covers the company's equipment. Both are needed."},"clip":"B1.3-S11-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Not yet: the set stays \"declared, pending\" until the Agency's decision; if the Agency requires a licence application, it waits for that as well.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. Luc's three facts are all true, and none of them is the Agency's decision. The expert's countersignature completed our declaration. The bunker certificate shows the room could take the set. What is missing is the one thing the regulation reserves for the Agency: whether this change may go ahead as declared, or needs a licence application first. So the crate stays closed, the line on our change list reads \"declared, pending\", and the day the Agency's decision permits the change, we update the line and arrange any required acceptance before use. That is how a change outside the licence becomes part of it.","screen":"Declared, pending. Obtain the Agency decision and the required acceptance before use."},"clip":"B1.3-S11-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.3-S11-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.3-S11-P1","B1.3-S11-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.3-S11-P2","interaction_id":"B1.3-S11-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S12","title":"Useful knowledge from elsewhere, verified here","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.3-S12-P1","text":"One last kind of evidence, and it came up while we were unpacking the manual for that new set. The manufacturer's manual recommends testing the door interlock every six months. Our approved procedure says every month. Daniel, who did part of his training abroad, remembers a quarterly interval from there. Three numbers for the same test, and all three come from somewhere real.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"One last kind of evidence, and it came up while we were unpa","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The manufacturer's manual recommends testing the door interl","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Daniel, who did part of his training abroad, remembers a qua","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Three numbers for the same test, and all three come from som","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S12-P1"},{"cue":"B1.3-S12-P2","text":"Several of you learned radiation physics abroad, or from training material written for another country's rules. That knowledge keeps its value in Belgium: how radiation attenuates in steel does not change at the border, and a manufacturer knows its own machine. What changes at the border is the rule. A check interval, an alarm setting or a \"you may start when\" from another jurisdiction is not a Belgian requirement, and neither is a manufacturer's manual. What governs our installation is the Belgian regulation, our licence and its conditions, and the procedures approved by the recognised expert. For the interlock, that is the monthly test, because that is what the expert approved for this bunker.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"Several of you learned radiation physics abroad, or from tra","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"What changes at the border is the rule.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"A check interval, an alarm setting or a \"you may start when\"","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"For the interlock, that is the monthly test, because that is","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S12-P2"},{"cue":"B1.3-S12-P3","text":"So keep the physics, and treat every rule you bring from elsewhere as a question: \"this is what I was taught there; what applies here?\" When a manual and our procedure disagree, raise the difference with the service and the expert, who may well decide the manual has a point and adapt the procedure. What nobody does is pick the more convenient of the two on the day. That habit, the question rather than the memorised number, is worth more than any interval you could learn by heart.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"So keep the physics, and treat every rule you bring from els","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"What nobody does is pick the more convenient of the two on t","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"That habit, the question rather than the memorised number, i","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.3-S12-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.3-S12-P1","B1.3-S12-P2","B1.3-S12-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S13","title":"Bring the evidence back to the work","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.3-S13-P1","text":"We started with \"everything is approved\". Here is what you can say instead, and it is what you have learned today. Our licence is the Agency's decision on an expert-approved application; it counts as proof of justification for the type of practice, and it is exactly as wide as its inventory and conditions. The foundry's class three licence is the Agency's decision on a declaration, and the sending of the declaration is not that decision. Between the licence and the first use stands commissioning: a fully favourable acceptance by the recognised expert that expressly permits it, with the security acceptance where sealed sources are involved, and, for a class two establishment, a declaration to the Agency that those conditions are met.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"We started with \"everything is approved\".","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Here is what you can say instead, and it is what you have le","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The foundry's class three licence is the Agency's decision o","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Between the licence and the first use stands commissioning: ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S13-P1"},{"cue":"B1.3-S13-P2","text":"A room is a bunker when it has the four parts, the safety devices the technical regulation requires, and a valid conformity certificate from a recognised expert: at most ten years old, adapted when the bunker changes, and covering the work asked for. Effective protection is built on five factors the regulation names, with collective means before individual ones, and an installation that no longer meets the requirements goes out of use until it is corrected. A failed function and a missing record are two different facts, and each is reported as what it is. A change outside the licence is recorded on the service's list, declared with the expert's countersignature, and decided by the Agency. And a rule from elsewhere is a question to ask here, not an instruction to follow.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"A room is a bunker when it has the four parts, the safety de","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Effective protection is built on five factors the regulation","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"A change outside the licence is recorded on the service's li","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"And a rule from elsewhere is a question to ask here, not an ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S13-P2"},{"cue":"B1.3-S13-P3","text":"None of this needs you to be the licensing authority. It needs you to read the right document for the right question, to say plainly when a result is not established, and to route a proposal through the people who decide. In the next lesson we add a second company to the picture: what changes when the worker's employer and the operator of the workplace are not the same organisation, as happens every time one of our radiographers enters a client's controlled area, or a subcontractor enters ours. You will meet Clara there, with her file. I'll see you then.","speaker":"Emilia","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.3 installation and evidence","beats":[{"at":"None of this needs you to be the licensing authority.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"It needs you to read the right document for the right questi","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"You will meet Clara there, with her file.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"I'll see you then.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.3-S13-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.3-S13-P1","B1.3-S13-P2","B1.3-S13-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}}]},{"id":"B1.4","title":"External workers: protection across company lines","scenes":[{"id":"S01","title":"Welcome back: protection across company lines","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.4-S01-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Welcome back. So far we have looked at our own company from the inside: our service, our licence, our bunker, our agents, with clients at the edge of the picture, asking for radiography and justifying where it happens. Today the company line itself becomes the subject. Almost every week one of our radiographers walks into another operator's controlled area, and from time to time a radiographer employed by another company works in our bunker. Who makes sure the important information travels with the person?","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Welcome back.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"So far we have looked at our own company from the inside: ou","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Almost every week one of our radiographers walks into anothe","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Who makes sure the important information travels with the pe","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S01-P1"},{"cue":"B1.4-S01-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Belgian law has a short section for exactly this situation: the operational protection of external workers who are exposed to a risk of ionising radiation while working in a controlled area. By the end of this lesson you will be able to say what the worker's own employer has to do, what the operator of the workplace has to do, what a signed agreement between the two can and cannot move, and what the worker brings to the arrangement personally.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Belgian law has a short section for exactly this situation: ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"By the end of this lesson you will be able to say what the w","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.4-S01-P2"},{"cue":"B1.4-S01-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"We use both directions, with two people you know. Daniel goes out: he is sent to a power station during an outage, to radiograph welds inside the plant's controlled area. And Clara comes in: you met her name in the first lesson, arriving with her file. She is a radiographer employed by another inspection company, subcontracted to work in our bunker for two weeks. Same law, two directions, and by the end you will see that it is one structure seen from both sides.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"We use both directions, with two people you know.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Daniel goes out: he is sent to a power station during an out","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"She is a radiographer employed by another inspection company","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Same law, two directions, and by the end you will see that i","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S01-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.4-S01-P1","B1.4-S01-P2","B1.4-S01-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S02","title":"Two directions, the same words","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.4-S02-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"First the words, because the law uses the same terms whichever way the worker is travelling. The external undertaking is the company that employs the worker and sends him. The operator, or where there is no operator the head of the undertaking, is the party at whose premises the worker carries out an assignment involving an exposure risk. The external worker is the person in between. Three words, and the whole section is about what each of the three owes the others.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"First the words, because the law uses the same terms whichev","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The external undertaking is the company that employs the wor","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The external worker is the person in between.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Three words, and the whole section is about what each of the","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S02-P1"},{"cue":"B1.4-S02-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Direction one. Daniel at the power station: there, Daniel is the external worker, our company is the external undertaking, and the power station is the operator. Direction two. Clara in our bunker: she is the external worker, her employer is the external undertaking, and we are the operator. Same words, roles reversed. Whenever you are unsure who owes what in a situation like this, start by naming the three parties; most mistakes in this area come from skipping that step.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Direction one.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Direction two.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Clara in our bunker: she is the external worker, her employe","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Whenever you are unsure who owes what in a situation like th","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S02-P2"},{"cue":"B1.4-S02-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"One thing does not change when Daniel crosses the plant's line: he stays our designated agent for the radiography we perform there. The industrial radiography decree asks for our agent on every worksite, and the Agency's guidance accepts that contractors bring their own agents for specific operations, under the supervision of the operator's physical control service. So two roles run side by side in the plant: his, for our radiography; the plant's, for its controlled area. This lesson is about how those two are divided, and neither cancels the other.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"One thing does not change when Daniel crosses the plant's li","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The industrial radiography decree asks for our agent on ever","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"So two roles run side by side in the plant: his, for our rad","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"This lesson is about how those two are divided, and neither ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S02-P3"},{"cue":"B1.4-S02-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Two more definitions and one principle. A controlled area, in the regulation's words, is an area subject to special rules for protection against ionising radiation and against the spread of contamination, with controlled access; in licensed establishments, every area where three tenths of the annual dose limits for exposed workers could be exceeded is a controlled area or part of one. The protection perimeter we mark out around an exposure is our controlled area on a worksite; the plant's marked zones are its controlled areas. And the principle that governs the whole section is one sentence: the radiological control system for external workers provides protection equivalent to that enjoyed by the workers the operator employs permanently. Two weeks, or one shift, is never a reason for weaker arrangements. Keep that sentence in mind as we divide the duties.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Two more definitions and one principle.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The protection perimeter we mark out around an exposure is o","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"And the principle that governs the whole section is one sent","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Keep that sentence in mind as we divide the duties.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S02-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.4-S02-P1","B1.4-S02-P2","B1.4-S02-P3","B1.4-S02-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S03","title":"What the worker's own employer must do","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.4-S03-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Start with the employer, because its duties begin before anyone arrives. The external undertaking looks after the radiation protection and safety of its own workers under the general rules of the regulation. In particular it makes sure the general principles of radiation protection and the dose limits are respected, and it organises the general information every exposed worker receives, the information you met two lessons ago. So the employer's duty does not stop at the gate of someone else's plant; it travels with the worker.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Start with the employer, because its duties begin before any","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The external undertaking looks after the radiation protectio","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"In particular it makes sure the general principles of radiat","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"So the employer's duty does not stop at the gate of someone ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S03-P1"},{"cue":"B1.4-S03-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Then, before an assignment with an exposure risk, the employer informs the operator, or the head of the undertaking, or the foreign undertaking, about three things, and the purpose of each is easy to see. Who the sending company is, so the operator knows whom it is dealing with: the name, the establishment unit and the enterprise number. Who the worker is, unambiguously: his identity data down to the national register number, so that dose records can never be confused between two people with the same name. And what dose he has already received: the doses over the last five calendar years, shown per year, and the doses over the last twelve rolling months, shown with the monitoring period, so the operator can judge, before the task, whether a dose constraint is needed. Where exposure was not uniform or there was internal contamination, the file carries the corresponding equivalent and committed doses as well. The exact fields are in the reference reader.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Then, before an assignment with an exposure risk, the employ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Who the worker is, unambiguously: his identity data down to ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"And what dose he has already received: the doses over the la","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The exact fields are in the reference reader.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S03-P2"},{"cue":"B1.4-S03-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Two reporting periods, then: five calendar years and twelve rolling months. They answer different questions, and an unlabelled number does not tell you which one you have. If the assignment is abroad, the employer also states the legal dose limits that apply there, and the information is transmitted in the way the Agency prescribes, using the radiation passport. So when Daniel is sent to the power station, it is my service that sends the plant his file before he arrives; and when Clara is sent to us, it is her employer's service I expect to hear from first.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Two reporting periods, then: five calendar years and twelve ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"They answer different questions, and an unlabelled number do","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"If the assignment is abroad, the employer also states the le","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"So when Daniel is sent to the power station, it is my servic","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S03-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.4-S03-P1","B1.4-S03-P2","B1.4-S03-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S04","title":"Clara's file arrives incomplete","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.4-S04-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Clara's employer sent her file last week, and this morning Clara hands me the printed copy herself, with her agent-course certificate on top. Company details, her details, and her doses for the last five calendar years are there. The twelve-rolling-month section is blank. Our service has a dosimeter ready for her, and Luc has her down for the bunker at ten.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Clara's employer sent her file last week, and this morning C","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Company details, her details, and her doses for the last fiv","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The twelve-rolling-month section is blank.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Our service has a dosimeter ready for her, and Luc has her d","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S04-P1"},{"cue":"B1.4-S04-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Clara is helpful: \"I can log into our dosimetry portal on my phone, it shows my last twelve months, you can read it off the screen.\" Luc: \"Her five-year total is tiny anyway, and we measure her from today. Let her start.\" Two sensible people, two shortcuts. Think about who has to inform whom, what I have to take note of before she starts, and what a figure on a phone screen is.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Clara is helpful: \"I can log into our dosimetry portal on my","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Let her start.\" Two sensible people, two shortcuts.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Think about who has to inform whom, what I have to take note","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.4-S04-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.4-S04-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"The twelve months are missing","situation_visible_text":"Clara's file from her employer has her five calendar years but no twelve-rolling-month section. Clara offers to show her last twelve months on her phone. Luc says her five-year total is low and we measure her from today. Our dosimeter is ready.","prompt_spoken_once":"What do I do about the missing twelve months before Clara starts?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Read the twelve-month figure from Clara's phone, note it on the file, and let her start; the information is there, just not on paper.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Clara's offer is exactly the right attitude: a worker who contributes information about her own work, and we will see later today that the regulation asks that of her. The figure on her screen tells me what to expect, and it may well be accurate. What the regulation asks for before the assignment is the employer's information to the operator, and that is what I take note of. So I thank her, I use her screen to see that there is nothing alarming coming, and I ask her employer's service for the twelve-month section with its monitoring period this morning. The file is complete when the employer completes it.","screen":"Clara's screen tells us what to expect. The employer's file is what we take note of."},"clip":"B1.4-S04-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Treat the missing months as zero, because her five-year total is low and our dosimeter records her from today.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Luc has two true things: the five-year figures are low, and our dosimeter will record everything Clara receives with us. What neither can do is tell me what she received elsewhere in the last twelve months, and that is the number the regulation wants me to have before deciding whether a dose constraint applies to her task. Writing zero turns an unknown into a claim nobody can support. The useful step is a precise request to her employer: twelve rolling months, with the monitoring period.","screen":"Unknown is not zero. The dosimeter records from today only."},"clip":"B1.4-S04-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Name the gap to her employer's service and ask for the twelve-month section with its monitoring period; take note of it before she starts, and use the waiting time for her instruction on our bunker.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. The employer must inform the operator about both periods before the assignment, and I, as the operator, take note of her monitoring results before she starts. So I name the exact gap, twelve rolling months with the monitoring period, and I ask her employer's service for it this morning. Clara does not have to repeat anything, nobody guesses what the missing months would show, and her phone screen reassures me while we wait. Her instruction on our bunker and our procedures can begin meanwhile; it does not depend on that number.","screen":"Name the gap, ask the employer, take note before she starts. Instruction meanwhile."},"clip":"B1.4-S04-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.4-S04-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.4-S04-P1","B1.4-S04-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.4-S04-P2","interaction_id":"B1.4-S04-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S05","title":"What the operator of the workplace must do","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.4-S05-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Now the other side. The operator, or failing one the head of the undertaking, at whose premises external workers carry out an assignment with an exposure risk, is responsible for the operational aspects of their radiation protection in the controlled area and for the task to be performed. The regulation lists six things in particular, and I want you to hear them as a list, because the next scenes are about which of them can move and which cannot.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Now the other side.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The operator, or failing one the head of the undertaking, at","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The regulation lists six things in particular, and I want yo","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.4-S05-P1"},{"cue":"B1.4-S05-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"One: making sure the general principles and the dose limits are respected. Two: organising the individual dosimetric monitoring of the external workers. Three: organising the specific training for the external workers, the workstation training aimed at this area and this task. Four: making the necessary personal protective equipment available. Five: taking note, before the assignment, of the results of their individual dosimetric monitoring. Six: where necessary, determining and enforcing dose constraints, taking into account the doses already received, the nature of the controlled area and the task.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"One:","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Two:","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Three:","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Four:","show":"Focus 4"},{"at":"Five:","show":"Focus 5"},{"at":"Six:","show":"Focus 6"}],"clip":"B1.4-S05-P2"},{"cue":"B1.4-S05-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Apply it in both directions. When Daniel enters the power station, the plant organises his site-specific training, reads his dose history, and decides whether a dose constraint applies for the outage work. When Clara enters our bunker, that list is mine: I organise her monitoring with us, her instruction on our bunker and our procedures, her protective equipment, and I read her file before she starts, which is what you just did. Notice what the list asks for: the specific training is about this place and this task, so it is given by the party who knows the place, and a certificate from a classroom is evidence of something else.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Apply it in both directions.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"When Daniel enters the power station, the plant organises hi","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"When Clara enters our bunker, that list is mine: I organise ","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Notice what the list asks for: the specific training is abou","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S05-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.4-S05-P1","B1.4-S05-P2","B1.4-S05-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S06","title":"What a signed agreement can change","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.4-S06-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"You may be thinking: our own service already organises Daniel's dosimetry; surely the power station does not issue him a second dosimeter? The regulation foresees this. An external undertaking that intervenes continuously or repeatedly under a contract with an operator, or that has its own physical control service, or that is an external emergency service, may organise some or all of certain aspects of its workers' protection during assignments for that operator. Our company qualifies twice over: we work for the plant under a repeated contract, and we have our own physical control service.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"You may be thinking: our own service already organises Danie","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The regulation foresees this.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"An external undertaking that intervenes continuously or repe","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Our company qualifies twice over: we work for the plant unde","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S06-P1"},{"cue":"B1.4-S06-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Which aspects? The regulation names them, and the list is short: the specific training on the controlled area and the task; the individual dosimetric monitoring and the transfer of its results to the exposure register; and the provision of the necessary personal protective equipment. Three aspects out of the six, and no others. Then it adds the condition that matters most in practice: these arrangements are laid down in an agreement signed by both parties. A phone call, an email or a long habit of working together moves nothing.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"the specific training","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"the individual dosimetric monitoring","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"the provision","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.4-S06-P2"},{"cue":"B1.4-S06-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"So I read our agreement with the power station for what it actually allocates. Ours says: our company provides Daniel's individual dosimetry and transfers the results to the register, and provides his protective equipment; the plant provides the training specific to its controlled areas and the task. That is a sensible split: we know our dosimetry, they know their plant. Each aspect is allocated by name, and each still has to be carried out by somebody. Reading the agreement is the whole skill of the next scene.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"So I read our agreement with the power station for what it a","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Ours says: our company provides Daniel's individual dosimetr","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Each aspect is allocated by name, and each still has to be c","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Reading the agreement is the whole skill of the next scene.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S06-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.4-S06-P1","B1.4-S06-P2","B1.4-S06-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S07","title":"Can we take the briefing over?","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.4-S07-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The outage starts on Monday. On Friday afternoon the plant's contact person calls Luc: \"We're short of people for the site briefings. Your team has been here a dozen times and your service runs Daniel's dosimetry anyway; can your service do his site-specific briefing this time and sign the slip? We'll countersign later.\" Luc thinks it is a reasonable request between partners, and he is inclined to say yes.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"The outage starts on Monday.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"On Friday afternoon the plant's contact person calls Luc: \"W","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Your team has been here a dozen times and your service runs ","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"We'll countersign later.\" Luc thinks it is a reasonable requ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S07-P1"},{"cue":"B1.4-S07-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Read the request against the agreement on the desk: clause A, dosimetry, to us; clause B, protective equipment, to us; clause C, specific training, to the plant. And read it against what the regulation says about which aspects may move, and how. Then tell Luc what to answer.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Read the request against the agreement on the desk: clause A","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"And read it against what the regulation says about which asp","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Then tell Luc what to answer.","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.4-S07-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.4-S07-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"Who gives Monday's briefing?","situation_visible_text":"Our signed agreement with the plant allocates dosimetry and protective equipment to us and the site-specific training to the plant. On Friday the plant asks our service to do Daniel's site briefing for Monday and sign the slip, with the plant countersigning later.","prompt_spoken_once":"Can our service give Daniel's site-specific briefing for Monday?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Yes: our team knows the plant, our service runs Daniel's dosimetry already, and a briefing by us is at least as good as one by the plant.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You are right that our people know the plant, and right that the quality of the briefing is what protects Daniel on Monday. The regulation looks at one more thing: who is responsible for that aspect. Specific training is one of the aspects that may move to the external undertaking, and it moves in one way only, by an agreement signed by both parties. Our agreement allocates it to the plant. Until the agreement says otherwise, the briefing is the plant's to give, however well we could give it.","screen":"Specific training can move, by signed agreement only. Ours leaves it with the plant."},"clip":"B1.4-S07-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Only if both parties sign an amendment that allocates the specific training to us; until then the plant gives Monday's briefing, because clause C places it there.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. The regulation lets a qualifying external undertaking take over the specific training, and we qualify. It also says how: laid down in an agreement signed by both parties. Our agreement allocates that aspect to the plant, so a phone call on Friday does not move it. If the plant wants us to take it over, both sign an amendment, and from then on it is ours, with our service preparing a briefing that covers the plant's zones, rules and emergency instructions. If the amendment is not signed by Monday, the plant briefs Daniel, as clause C says.","screen":"Move it on paper, signed by both, or the plant briefs on Monday."},"clip":"B1.4-S07-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"No, never: the specific training is about the plant's own controlled area, so it can only be given by the operator.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have the reason the regulation places specific training with the operator by default: it is about this area and this task, and the operator knows them best. The regulation still allows that aspect to move to an external undertaking that qualifies, which we do, through an agreement signed by both parties. So the answer to the plant is a conditional one, with the amendment on the table, and the answer for Monday depends on whether it is signed.","screen":"Specific training can move to a qualifying external undertaking, by signed agreement."},"clip":"B1.4-S07-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.4-S07-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.4-S07-P1","B1.4-S07-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.4-S07-P2","interaction_id":"B1.4-S07-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S08","title":"When the task changes","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.4-S08-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Clara has been with us a week. She was instructed on the bunker and on the X-ray work she was brought in for; that is what her instruction record says. Then an assignment slip arrives: can she help with gamma exposures in hall two this afternoon? Clara says, sensibly: \"I've had the briefing, but it was for the bunker job.\" That is exactly the right thing to say. Workstation training is given for a workstation and a function, and the regulation repeats it when the function, the work tool or the technology changes.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Clara has been with us a week.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"She was instructed on the bunker and on the X-ray work she w","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Clara says, sensibly: \"I've had the briefing, but it was for","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Workstation training is given for a workstation and a functi","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S08-P1"},{"cue":"B1.4-S08-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Luc, who wrote the slip, points at her employer's file: \"She's done gamma work for years, it's all in there, and she's been in our building a week.\" Clara's experience is real, and so is her week with us. Think about what an instruction record covers, what experience elsewhere proves, and what a changed task asks for, before you decide what happens this afternoon.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Luc, who wrote the slip, points at her employer's file: \"She","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Think about what an instruction record covers, what experien","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.4-S08-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.4-S08-R01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"Bunker this week, hall two this afternoon","situation_visible_text":"Clara's instruction record covers the bunker and its X-ray set. The slip asks for gamma exposures in hall two this afternoon. Her employer's file shows years of gamma experience. Luc wants her to go.","prompt_spoken_once":"What happens before Clara does the gamma work in hall two?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"We name what has changed, area, equipment and procedure, arrange the specific instruction for that task and the review of her protection and monitoring that the change needs, and then she goes.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. Clara's own remark was the right start: her instruction covers the bunker and its X-ray set, and hall two with a gamma projector is a different area, a different tool and a different procedure. The regulation repeats workstation training when the tool or the technology changes, so we arrange the specific instruction for that task, with her employer under our agreement where it applies, and we look at whether her protection and monitoring need anything for gamma work. That takes an hour, and then she goes with an instruction record that actually covers what she is doing.","screen":"Name the change, instruct for it, review her protection, then go."},"clip":"B1.4-S08-R01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"She repeats the full induction, because a changed task means her instruction with us starts from the beginning.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have kept the right principle: a changed task asks for instruction before the work. The induction, though, was given for our site and our procedures in general, and that part is still true this afternoon. What the regulation repeats is the training aimed at the workstation and the task that changed. So we name the change and instruct for it, and we leave what still holds in place. A full repeat costs Clara and the team a day and adds nothing to the part that matters.","screen":"Instruct for what changed, keep what still holds."},"clip":"B1.4-S08-R01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"She goes: her employer's file shows years of gamma experience, and a week in our building covers the rest.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Luc's two facts are both true, and her experience is the reason she will be instructed quickly rather than trained from scratch. What the file proves is experience with gamma work elsewhere, on other equipment and under other procedures. What a week with us proves is instruction for the bunker and the X-ray set. Neither is the specific instruction for our projector in our hall two, which is what the regulation asks for when the tool and the technology change. Experience makes the instruction short; it does not replace it.","screen":"Experience elsewhere shortens the instruction. It does not replace it."},"clip":"B1.4-S08-R01-c"}],"clip":"B1.4-S08-R01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.4-S08-P1","B1.4-S08-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.4-S08-P2","interaction_id":"B1.4-S08-R01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S09","title":"Whose constraint is it?","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.4-S09-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Back to Daniel at the power station, Monday morning. The plant's physical control service has read his file, our five calendar years and twelve rolling months, and it has set a dose constraint for his outage work that is lower than the planning level we use for him in-house. Luc, on the phone with the plant: \"His dosimetry is ours under the agreement, so the constraint against those readings is ours to set.\"","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Back to Daniel at the power station, Monday morning.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The plant's physical control service has read his file, our ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Luc, on the phone with the plant: \"His dosimetry is ours und","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.4-S09-P1"},{"cue":"B1.4-S09-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Before you answer Luc, remember the three parties, the six duties of the operator, the three aspects that can move by signed agreement, and what you learned in the first lesson about who can impose a constraint. Then say whose constraint this is.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Before you answer Luc, remember the three parties, the six d","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Then say whose constraint this is.","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.4-S09-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.4-S09-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"A lower constraint from the plant","situation_visible_text":"The plant's service has set a dose constraint for Daniel's outage work, lower than our in-house planning level. Our agreement allocates Daniel's dosimetry and protective equipment to us. Luc says the constraint is ours to set.","prompt_spoken_once":"Who determines the dose constraint for Daniel's work in the plant's controlled area?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Our company: Daniel's dosimetry is ours under the agreement, and a constraint is read against those readings, so it is ours to set.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have read the agreement correctly: Daniel's dosimetry is ours, and our readings are what the constraint will be checked against. The constraint itself is a different duty. Determining and enforcing dose constraints, taking into account the doses already received, the area and the task, is one of the operator's six duties, and it is not one of the three aspects a signed agreement can move. So the plant sets it, using the dose history from our file, and our dosimetry feeds the check. Luc can discuss the level with the plant; the decision is the plant's.","screen":"Dosimetry moved to us. Constraints are the operator's duty and do not move."},"clip":"B1.4-S09-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Neither: a dose constraint can only be imposed by the Agency, so the plant's figure is a planning target, and Daniel works to our level.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have remembered the first lesson well: the Agency can impose dose constraints. That is one route. The regulation gives the operator of a workplace its own duty here: where necessary, it determines and enforces dose constraints for external workers in its controlled area, taking into account their dose history, the area and the task. The plant has done exactly that, with our file in hand. So its figure is binding for Daniel's work there, and our in-house level is what applies when he is back with us.","screen":"The Agency can impose constraints; the operator of the workplace sets them for its area too."},"clip":"B1.4-S09-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"The plant, as operator of the workplace, using the dose history from our file; our dosimetry under the agreement delivers the readings the constraint is checked against.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. Three parties: Daniel is the external worker, we are the external undertaking, the plant is the operator. Among the operator's duties is determining and enforcing dose constraints where necessary, taking into account the doses already received, the controlled area and the task, and the regulation does not list that among the aspects a signed agreement can move. So the plant sets the constraint, with the two reporting periods we sent it. What our agreement did move is the dosimetry: our dosimeter on Daniel's chest produces the readings that are checked against the plant's figure. Two companies, one worker, each doing the part the regulation gives it.","screen":"The plant sets the constraint. Our dosimetry feeds it. Both from the same file."},"clip":"B1.4-S09-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.4-S09-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.4-S09-P1","B1.4-S09-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.4-S09-P2","interaction_id":"B1.4-S09-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S10","title":"What the worker brings, and when the work is abroad","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.4-S10-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The information travels partly because the worker carries it. You know the duties every worker has, from the lesson on the failed meter check: follow the instructions, never expose yourself unnecessarily, never damage or remove protective means, report a defect at once. For external workers the regulation adds a duty that is easy to overlook: the worker contributes as far as possible to his own protection, and in particular he agrees to give the employer, the operator or the head of the undertaking information about his previous and current work that is relevant to effective and coherent protection, for himself and for others. Clara telling us that her briefing covered a different job was that duty in action; so was her offer to show her last twelve months. And the regulation stresses the need and the duty to declare a pregnancy as early as possible, for the same reason: protection can only be arranged around what is known.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"The information travels partly because the worker carries it","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"You know the duties every worker has, from the lesson on the","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Clara telling us that her briefing covered a different job w","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"And the regulation stresses the need and the duty to declare","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S10-P1"},{"cue":"B1.4-S10-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"One more direction: abroad. When we send a radiographer to an undertaking in another country, our company makes sure, through an agreement with the foreign undertaking, that the general principles, the dose limits and any agreed dose constraints are respected; that our worker is subject to individual dosimetric monitoring; that he receives the specific training before the assignment starts; and that he has the necessary protective equipment. We transmit the results of his monitoring to the exposure register ourselves, and the pre-assignment information goes with the radiation passport, in the way the Agency prescribes.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"One more direction: abroad.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"When we send a radiographer to an undertaking in another cou","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"We transmit the results of his monitoring to the exposure re","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.4-S10-P2"},{"cue":"B1.4-S10-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"I am not giving you a cross-border checklist today. I am showing you that the same three questions travel across any border: who has the information, who needs it, and who has agreed to do what. Answer those three and you can read any external-worker arrangement, in Belgium or abroad.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"I am not giving you a cross-border checklist today.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"I am showing you that the same three questions travel across","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Answer those three and you can read any external-worker arra","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.4-S10-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.4-S10-P1","B1.4-S10-P2","B1.4-S10-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S11","title":"One worker, connected responsibilities","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.4-S11-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Daniel going out and Clara coming in have shown you the same structure from both sides, and here is what you take with you. Three parties: the external undertaking, the operator of the workplace, the external worker. The employer brings the general information, the identity data and the dose history for two reporting periods, five calendar years and twelve rolling months, and it keeps its responsibility for principles and limits wherever its worker goes. The operator of the workplace organises the operational protection in its controlled area: monitoring, specific training, protective equipment, taking note of the dose history, and dose constraints where needed, with equivalent protection for the visitor as for its own staff.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Daniel going out and Clara coming in have shown you the same","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Three parties: the external undertaking, the operator of the","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The employer brings the general information, the identity da","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The operator of the workplace organises the operational prot","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S11-P1"},{"cue":"B1.4-S11-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"A signed agreement between a qualifying external undertaking and the operator can move three named aspects, and only those: specific training, dosimetry with its transfer to the register, and protective equipment. It moves them by signature, not by habit or by phone, and it never moves the constraint or the responsibility for the area. A changed task asks for instruction for that task, however experienced the worker. And the worker follows the instructions, reports defects at once, and shares what is relevant about his own work, including a pregnancy, as early as possible.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"A signed agreement between a qualifying external undertaking","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"It moves them by signature, not by habit or by phone, and it","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"A changed task asks for instruction for that task, however e","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"And the worker follows the instructions, reports defects at ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.4-S11-P2"},{"cue":"B1.4-S11-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"A missing twelve months, a briefing nobody has agreed to move, a slip for a different task, a constraint claimed by the wrong party: each of them is answered by naming the three parties and reading what the paper actually says. In the next lesson we look at what happens when something is actually wrong: the protective action, the internal information, and the statutory reporting to the Agency with its criteria and time limits, so that a message being passed on is never mistaken for every necessary action being done. I'll see you then.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.4 scenario","beats":[{"at":"A missing twelve months, a briefing nobody has agreed to mov","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"In the next lesson we look at what happens when something is","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"I'll see you then.","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.4-S11-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.4-S11-P1","B1.4-S11-P2","B1.4-S11-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}}]},{"id":"B1.5","title":"When something is wrong: action, information and reporting","scenes":[{"id":"S01","title":"Welcome back: when an observation becomes a responsibility","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S01-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Welcome back. In the last lesson you followed information across company lines, so that it reaches the right people before and after an assignment. Today we look at the moment when that connection becomes urgent: somebody notices that something is wrong. A defect, an unexpected event, a situation that could have hurt someone even though it did not.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Welcome back.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"In the last lesson you followed information across company l","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Today we look at the moment when that connection becomes urg","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"A defect, an unexpected event, a situation that could have h","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S01-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S01-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Those moments pull people in two directions. One is to wait until everything is understood before saying anything. The other is to treat a message passed on as the job done. Belgian law is precise about why both fall short, and it answers with three duties that run at the same time: the protective action, the information inside our own protection organisation, and the statutory notification to the Agency, with its criteria and time limits. I will call them three lanes, because they run side by side, and because a car in one lane does not clear the others.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Agency","show":"Focus 1"}],"clip":"B1.5-S01-P2"},{"cue":"B1.5-S01-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"By the end of this lesson you will be able to hold those three lanes apart and run them together. You will know who notifies the Agency, what counts as reaching it, and what the written notification contains when half the facts are still open. And you will be able to give a first account that is useful precisely because it says what is not yet known. We do all of that with one case, and we follow it from the first phone call to the final report.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"By the end of this lesson you will be able to hold those thr","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"You will know who notifies the Agency, what counts as reachi","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"And you will be able to give a first account that is useful ","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"We do all of that with one case, and we follow it from the f","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S01-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S01-P1","B1.5-S01-P2","B1.5-S01-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S02","title":"Tuesday, 10:12, in the bunker","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S02-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Here is the case. Tuesday morning, Daniel is radiographing a batch of castings in our bunker with the X-ray set. He is at the control post outside; the exposure is running and the warning light is on. At twelve minutes past ten a colleague from the workshop, Tom, a fitter, not one of our exposed workers, so he wears no dosimeter, opens the bunker door to fetch a tool he had left inside. The door interlock should have cut the exposure the instant the door opened. It did not. Daniel sees the door move on the camera, stops the exposure from the control post and calls Tom back out. Tom was in the doorway for a few seconds.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Here is the case.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"He is at the control post outside; the exposure is running a","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"It did not.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Tom was in the doorway for a few seconds.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S02-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S02-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Stop there and sort what we know from what we do not. We know the time, the place, the equipment, what Tom did, what the interlock did not do, and what Daniel did. We do not know why the interlock failed, and we do not know what dose Tom received. Seconds in the doorway of a bunker with an X-ray set running is something to have assessed by the people and the methods that can do it; it is neither something to wave away nor something to dramatise. And one thing we also cannot say: that the interlock worked yesterday, simply because nobody opened the door yesterday.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Stop there and sort what we know from what we do not.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"We know the time, the place, the equipment, what Tom did, wh","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Seconds in the doorway of a bunker with an X-ray set running","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"And one thing we also cannot say: that the interlock worked ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S02-P2"},{"cue":"B1.5-S02-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Daniel's first words to me on the phone were good ones: \"The interlock didn't cut the exposure when Tom opened the door. I've stopped the exposure and the bunker is out of use. Tom is out and says he feels nothing unusual, but I don't know his dose. I don't know why it failed.\" Observed, done, unknown: the handover you learned to give two lessons ago, under pressure, and it works. Notice what he has not said. He has not blamed Tom, he has not reassured anyone about a dose he cannot know, because feeling nothing says nothing about dose, and he has not diagnosed the interlock.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Daniel's first words to me on the phone were good ones: \"The","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Tom is out and says he feels nothing unusual, but I don't kn","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"I don't know why it failed.\" Observed, done, unknown: the ha","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"He has not blamed Tom, he has not reassured anyone about a d","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S02-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S02-P1","B1.5-S02-P2","B1.5-S02-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S03","title":"Lane one and lane two: protect, and inform the right people","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S03-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Lane one is the protective action, and most of it has already happened, because it was in Daniel's instructions. The exposure is stopped. The installation stays out of use: you know from the licensing lesson that a device or installation that no longer meets the requirements is taken out of use until the deficiency is corrected. Tom stays available, and the facts the expert will need to assess his dose are preserved under our response procedure: where he stood, for how long, the set's settings and the exposure log, nothing changed on the control panel. The agent's duties include taking the prescribed urgent measures in an incident and passing the information on immediately. None of that is an invitation to investigate the fault himself, and nobody tests an interlock by opening the door during an exposure.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Lane one is the protective action, and most of it has alread","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The installation stays out of use: you know from the licensi","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Tom stays available, and the facts the expert will need to a","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"None of that is an invitation to investigate the fault himse","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S03-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S03-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Lane two is information inside the protection organisation, and it runs at the same time as lane one. The agent informs the head of the physical control service and the recognised expert of every abnormal situation: so Daniel calls me and leaves the agreed message for the expert at the organisation we contract. As the radiographer who stopped the work, he also tells Luc, his supervisor. I do not assume the message landed: I call the expert myself, and I brief our head of establishment, because he is the one who will notify the Agency; you will see why in a moment.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Lane two is information inside the protection organisation, ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The agent informs the head of the physical control service a","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"As the radiographer who stopped the work, he also tells Luc,","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"I do not assume the message landed: I call the expert myself","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S03-P2"},{"cue":"B1.5-S03-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Then my own duties start, and the regulation names them. Whenever an event occurs that could endanger the safety or health of people, the head of the physical control service immediately takes all useful measures against the danger discovered, where appropriate in consultation with the recognised expert. And the head warns the recognised physician in charge of the workers' medical surveillance in three cases: whenever an exposed worker has to be subjected to an emergency exposure; whenever a person, exposed worker or not, has received an accidental exposure exceeding the dose limits; and whenever an accident occurs that involves a serious exposure hazard. We do not know Tom's dose yet, so I speak to the physician about Tom today, rather than waiting for a number to tell me whether I must.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Then my own duties start, and the regulation names them.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Whenever an event occurs that could endanger the safety or h","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"And the head warns the recognised physician in charge of the","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"We do not know Tom's dose yet, so I speak to the physician a","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S03-P3"},{"cue":"B1.5-S03-P4","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The regulation then gives the recognised expert a job: a thorough study of the circumstances and of the doses received, using the proper methods of individual dosimetry, ending in a report to the operator that recommends measures to correct the shortcoming and prevent a repeat. And it tells the operator, or failing one the head of the undertaking, to warn as soon as possible the Agency, according to the modalities and criteria the Agency has set, the government's coordination and crisis centre and the one-one-two emergency call system, and, where an accident involves a serious exposure hazard, the mayor and the emergency services as well. Which of those calls our event requires is written in our emergency procedure, drawn up with the expert; the Agency's modalities and criteria are the subject of the rest of this lesson. What matters now is that these duties run alongside each other. Protecting Tom does not wait for a written report, and telling me completes nobody's notification to the Agency.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"The regulation then gives the recognised expert a job: a tho","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"And it tells the operator, or failing one the head of the un","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"What matters now is that these duties run alongside each oth","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Protecting Tom does not wait for a written report, and telli","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S03-P4"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S03-P1","B1.5-S03-P2","B1.5-S03-P3","B1.5-S03-P4"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S04","title":"The minutes after the stop","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S04-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Put yourself beside Daniel at the control post, a minute after he stopped the exposure. The cause is unknown; his instruction says the bunker stays out of use and the service is called. Tom is standing next to him, a bit shaken, and says he feels fine and would like to get back to the workshop; the foreman is waiting for him.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Put yourself beside Daniel at the control post, a minute aft","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The cause is unknown; his instruction says the bunker stays ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Tom is standing next to him, a bit shaken, and says he feels","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.5-S04-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S04-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Luc, who has walked over: \"Tom isn't one of our exposed workers, he has no dosimeter, there's nothing to measure. Let him go, and we'll sort the door.\" Then, trying to be useful: \"Or put your survey meter in the doorway and run a short exposure, so the expert at least has a number for Tom.\" Two suggestions, both meant well. Think about lane one and lane two, and about who assesses a dose and how, before you decide what Daniel does.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Luc, who has walked over: \"Tom isn't one of our exposed work","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Let him go, and we'll sort the door.\" Then, trying to be use","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Think about lane one and lane two, and about who assesses a ","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.5-S04-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.5-S04-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"Tom wants to go back to work","situation_visible_text":"The exposure is stopped and the bunker is out of use. Tom, a fitter without a dosimeter, was in the doorway for seconds and feels fine; he wants to return to the workshop. Luc suggests letting him go, or measuring in the doorway with a short exposure so the expert has a number.","prompt_spoken_once":"What does Daniel do in the minutes after the stop?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Let Tom go back to the workshop, since he is not an exposed worker and feels fine; keep the bunker out of use and call the service about the interlock.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have lane one half right: the bunker stays out of use, and the service is called about the interlock. The part that goes missing is Tom. Whether he is one of our exposed workers changes nothing about what happened to him in that doorway, and feeling fine says nothing about dose. His dose is assessed by the recognised expert with the proper methods, and for that the expert needs Tom available and the facts preserved: where he stood, for how long, the set's settings. Tom goes back to the workshop when the service says so, with a note of where to find him.","screen":"Tom is part of the facts. He stays available until the service says otherwise."},"clip":"B1.5-S04-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Keep the bunker out of use, keep Tom available and the exposure facts untouched, and call the service now; the dose question goes to the expert, with the physician informed.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. That is lane one and lane two together. The protective action his instruction assigns: exposure stopped, bunker out of use, nothing changed on the panel, and Tom kept available, because he and the exposure facts are what the expert's dose assessment is built on. Then the call: the head of service and the expert informed at once, and Luc as his supervisor. Daniel reports what he saw and leaves the cause and the dose to the people and methods that can establish them. The expert studies the circumstances and the dose; I speak to the physician today.","screen":"Out of use, Tom and facts preserved, service called now. The expert assesses the dose."},"clip":"B1.5-S04-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Keep Tom there, put the survey meter in the doorway and run a short exposure, so the expert gets a measured number instead of a guess.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have understood that the expert will need facts rather than guesses, and that Tom's dose has to be assessed, not assumed. The way to get there is the one the regulation names: the expert's study of the circumstances, with the proper methods of individual dosimetry, using the settings, the position and the time that Daniel preserved. A new exposure with the door open repeats the event with the protection defeated, in an installation that is out of use. The number the expert needs comes from reconstruction, not from doing it again.","screen":"The expert reconstructs the dose from the preserved facts. No exposure with the door open."},"clip":"B1.5-S04-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.5-S04-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S04-P1","B1.5-S04-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.5-S04-P2","interaction_id":"B1.5-S04-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S05","title":"Give the facts their own place","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S05-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Before we reach the Agency, let us make Daniel's account useful to someone who was not there, because that person may be a duty officer who has never seen our bunker. \"Something went wrong this morning\" helps nobody. \"At ten twelve, bunker one, X-ray set in exposure, the door interlock did not cut the exposure when the door was opened; exposure stopped manually; bunker out of use\" gives the next person facts to work with. Two times matter: when the event happened and when it was discovered. Here they coincide. With a slow leak or a mislabelled source they might be weeks apart, and the reporting clock runs from the event or from its discovery.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Before we reach the Agency, let us make Daniel's account use","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"\"At ten twelve, bunker one, X-ray set in exposure, the door ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Two times matter: when the event happened and when it was di","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"With a slow leak or a mislabelled source they might be weeks","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S05-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S05-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"If Daniel suspects a cause, and he does, he thinks the door switch has been sticking, he may say so, labelled as a suspicion with his reason. A suspicion is not yet a finding, and the label is what keeps it honest. The same discipline applies to dose. \"Not yet established\" is a true description of Tom's dose this morning, and it stays true until the expert's assessment replaces it. When I take Daniel's account I ask him three things: what did you see yourself, what did Tom tell you, and what has already been done? Those three questions keep the record clean. Our teaching record is a handover aid; the statutory notification has its own prescribed contents, and we come to those.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"If Daniel suspects a cause, and he does, he thinks the door ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The same discipline applies to dose.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"When I take Daniel's account I ask him three things: what di","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Our teaching record is a handover aid; the statutory notific","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S05-P2"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S05-P1","B1.5-S05-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S06","title":"Lane three: who notifies the Agency, and for which establishments","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S06-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Lane three is the statutory notification, and its rules are in a technical regulation of the Agency: the regulation of the seventeenth of June, twenty twenty, setting the criteria for notifying significant events, as amended. What is a significant event? Any event, including a human error, a near-miss, an accident, an unauthorised act, that has consequences, even potential consequences, for safety, security, radiation protection or the environment. Tom's few seconds in the doorway are a significant event whatever his dose turns out to be, because the consequences could have been serious.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Lane three is the statutory notification, and its rules are ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"What is a significant event?","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Any event, including a human error, a near-miss, an accident","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Tom's few seconds in the doorway are a significant event wha","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S06-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S06-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Who is covered? All class two and three establishments, with one exception: establishments whose physical control is exercised by a shared service that also serves a class one establishment follow the class one route. Import, transit and export, and the transport of class seven dangerous goods, have their own criteria in the same regulation, and so do persons subject to the security decree. So a site event and a transport event are two different routes; today we stay with the establishment route.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Who is covered?","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"All class two and three establishments, with one exception: ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Import, transit and export, and the transport of class seven","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"So a site event and a transport event are two different rout","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S06-P2"},{"cue":"B1.5-S06-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Who notifies? The head of the establishment or the head of the undertaking. For the security rubrics, the delegate for radiological security may also notify on the operator's behalf. Notice who is not named: the head of the physical control service, and the agent. In our company the operator has designated our managing director as head of the establishment. I prepare the notification with him and make sure he has the facts; my title does not make me the notifier, and Daniel's call to me does not make the notification happen. For the exercises that follow, the applicable scope is given and the responsible assessment has identified the criteria; your job is to use the rules correctly, and classifying every event yourself is a task for the people who do that with the expert.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Who notifies?","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"For the security rubrics, the delegate for radiological secu","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"In our company the operator has designated our managing dire","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"For the exercises that follow, the applicable scope is given","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S06-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S06-P1","B1.5-S06-P2","B1.5-S06-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S07","title":"Use the criterion, not a remembered number","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S07-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The regulation's table lists the events to be notified, and for each one two things: whether successful direct contact with the Agency is required and by when, and whether an INES evaluation applies. Here is a small dated extract. Read the condition on the left as carefully as the deadline beside it; a remembered deadline without its condition is easy to apply to the wrong event.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"The regulation's table lists the events to be notified, and ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Here is a small dated extract.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Read the condition on the left as carefully as the deadline ","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.5-S07-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S07-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Criterion one point five: loss or failure of equipment that fulfils a safety function. Direct contact no later than the next working day; INES evaluation yes. Criterion one point four: non-compliance with the safety logic, or application of an unsuitable safety logic, that leads or may lead to unforeseen behaviour of the installation. Direct contact immediately; INES evaluation yes. Those are two different descriptions. An interlock that fails is equipment with a safety function; whether the way it was wired or bypassed also amounts to a safety-logic failure is a question for the responsible assessment with the expert, and Daniel at the control post is right to leave it there.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Criterion one point five: loss or failure of equipment that ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Criterion one point four: non-compliance with the safety log","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Direct contact immediately; INES evaluation yes.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"An interlock that fails is equipment with a safety function;","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S07-P2"},{"cue":"B1.5-S07-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Alongside the direct-contact column stands a separate duty. For every event that meets one or more criteria, a written notification is sent by the notifier within forty-eight hours of the event or its discovery, or sooner if the Agency asks, to the Agency's event address. Two duties, two columns in your head: the written notification does not replace an immediate call or a next-working-day contact, and a call does not replace the written notification. In real work, our procedure holds the current complete table and the Agency's contact details; if the regulation changes, the training and the procedure are checked against the new text. This extract is for learning the mechanism.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Alongside the direct-contact column stands a separate duty.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"For every event that meets one or more criteria, a written n","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"In real work, our procedure holds the current complete table","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"This extract is for learning the mechanism.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S07-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S07-P1","B1.5-S07-P2","B1.5-S07-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S08","title":"When two criteria apply","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S08-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Add one established fact to our case. By half past ten, the responsible assessment with the expert concludes that both criterion one point five and criterion one point four apply: a safety device failed, and the way it failed points to the safety logic. Established with the expert, not guessed from the first phone call. The regulation says what happens when an event meets several criteria: the strictest requirements for direct contact apply.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Add one established fact to our case.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"By half past ten, the responsible assessment with the expert","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Established with the expert, not guessed from the first phon","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The regulation says what happens when an event meets several","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S08-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S08-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Our head of establishment has the phone in his hand and two pieces of advice. Luc: \"One point five says next working day, and that's the criterion we found first. Let's get the whole picture straight and call tomorrow morning with facts instead of fragments.\" Our director's assistant: \"Just send the written form now with everything in it, that covers the contact and the notification in one go.\" Read both against the table and the two columns.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Our head of establishment has the phone in his hand and two ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Luc: \"One point five says next working day, and that's the c","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Let's get the whole picture straight and call tomorrow morni","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.5-S08-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.5-S08-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"Next working day, or now?","situation_visible_text":"The assessment with the expert establishes that both criterion one point five (direct contact next working day) and criterion one point four (direct contact immediately) apply. It is Tuesday, half past ten. Luc proposes to call tomorrow with the full picture; the assistant proposes to send the written form now instead of calling.","prompt_spoken_once":"What does our head of establishment do now?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Call the Agency tomorrow morning with the full picture, because criterion one point five was identified first and gives the next working day.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Luc's wish to call with facts instead of fragments is a good instinct, and one point five is genuinely met; on its own it would give the next working day. The order in which criteria were identified changes nothing. Once both apply, the regulation applies the strictest direct-contact requirement, and one point four says immediately. The picture does not have to be complete for the call; the duty officer expects to hear what is known and what is not. Tomorrow's call would be a day late.","screen":"Several criteria: the strictest contact rule governs. One point four means now."},"clip":"B1.5-S08-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Send the written notification now with everything in it; sent today, it covers both the direct contact and the forty-eight-hour notification.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Sending the written notification early is fine; it is due within forty-eight hours anyway, and today is well within that. It is one of the two columns, and only one. Direct contact is the other: a conversation with the person on duty, and criterion one point four wants it immediately. A document in the Agency's inbox is a document; the duty officer has not been spoken to. So the call is made now, and the written notification follows as its own step.","screen":"The written form is one column. Direct contact is the other, and it is immediate here."},"clip":"B1.5-S08-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Make successful direct contact with the Agency's duty officer now, because the stricter criterion governs, and send the written notification within forty-eight hours as a separate step.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. When an event meets more than one criterion, the strictest requirements for direct contact apply. Criterion one point four requires immediate contact, so that is the point on the timeline, whatever was identified first. And the written notification within forty-eight hours remains a separate duty that the call does not discharge, and that does not discharge the call. Our head of establishment calls now, with what is known and what is not, and the written notification is prepared for today or tomorrow. Two columns, both filled.","screen":"Call now, under the strictest criterion. Written notification within forty-eight hours, separately."},"clip":"B1.5-S08-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.5-S08-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S08-P1","B1.5-S08-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.5-S08-P2","interaction_id":"B1.5-S08-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S09","title":"A message left is not successful direct contact","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S09-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Our head of establishment calls the Agency's general duty roster at twenty past ten and reaches voicemail. He leaves a clear message with all the facts, and to be thorough he emails the same facts to the Agency's event address. At twenty to eleven the duty officer calls back, and the two of them speak for five minutes. Is the immediate direct contact made, and when? The regulation defines successful direct contact as contact with the person on duty in the Agency's general duty roster, with a view to a direct, oral and understandable notification of the event. And it says in so many words what does not count: a message on the Agency's answering machine or a mobile, a text, an email, a fax, or speaking to a person who is not on duty in that roster at the time.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Our head of establishment calls the Agency's general duty ro","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"At twenty to eleven the duty officer calls back, and the two","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Is the immediate direct contact made, and when?","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"And it says in so many words what does not count: a message ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S09-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S09-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The regulation adds that the notifier makes as many attempts as needed to actually obtain successful direct contact. There is no rule that two attempts are enough, and no rule that a written message closes the duty. Meanwhile lane one and lane two keep running: the expert's dose assessment for Tom is under way, the bunker stays out of use, the physician has been called. Daniel does not have to take over the notification. His handover, though, must say what actually happened, and the contact record on the desk is what you fill in now.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"The regulation adds that the notifier makes as many attempts","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"There is no rule that two attempts are enough, and no rule t","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Daniel does not have to take over the notification.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"His handover, though, must say what actually happened, and t","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S09-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.5-S09-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"Voicemail, email, and a call back","situation_visible_text":"Twenty past ten: voicemail left on the Agency's duty roster, and the facts emailed to the event address. Twenty to eleven: the duty officer calls back and they speak. The contact record has to be filled in.","prompt_spoken_once":"What does the contact record say?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Attempt at twenty past ten: voicemail, and the email, recorded as attempts; successful direct contact at twenty to eleven, when the duty officer called back and they spoke.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. The record says what happened, in order. The voicemail and the email are attempts, worth recording because they show the notifier tried without delay, and the regulation says in plain words that neither is successful direct contact. The call back at twenty to eleven is: the person on duty, orally, with an understandable account of the event. So the contact succeeded at twenty to eleven, twenty-eight minutes after the event. Had the duty officer not called back, the record would read \"not yet\" and the calls would have continued.","screen":"Voicemail and email: attempts. The call back: successful direct contact, at twenty to eleven."},"clip":"B1.5-S09-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Successful direct contact at twenty past ten, because the voicemail and the email carried all the facts and the duty officer's call back confirmed they arrived.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You are right that the facts reached the Agency at twenty past ten, and a complete voicemail with an email behind it is exactly the kind of attempt that helps the duty officer later. The regulation defines the contact by what it is, a direct, oral and understandable notification to the person on duty, and names the answering machine and email as what it is not. So the contact succeeded when the two of them spoke, at twenty to eleven. The earlier time is the attempt, and the record keeps both.","screen":"Facts arriving is not contact. Contact is the conversation, at twenty to eleven."},"clip":"B1.5-S09-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Successful direct contact at twenty past ten, and the email to the event address counts as the written notification, so lane three is closed.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have spotted that the email went to the right address, and if it contains what the written notification requires, it may well serve as that notification; that is a separate check. The contact itself is defined as oral and direct with the person on duty, and the regulation excludes email from it, so the contact succeeded at twenty to eleven, when they spoke. And lane three is closed only when both columns are filled: successful direct contact, and a written notification with the prescribed contents within forty-eight hours.","screen":"Email is not direct contact. Two columns: the call at twenty to eleven, and a complete written notification."},"clip":"B1.5-S09-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.5-S09-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S09-P1","B1.5-S09-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.5-S09-P2","interaction_id":"B1.5-S09-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S10","title":"Write what is known, without waiting for the final explanation","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S10-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Move the case forward: direct contact has succeeded and is recorded. Now the written notification, within forty-eight hours of the event or its discovery. The regulation says what it must contain at minimum, and the list has a logic you know from Daniel's first account: what happened, where and when, and when it was discovered; what equipment and sources were involved; what the actual consequences are, including doses where they are known; what the suspected causes are, suspected being the regulation's own word; what urgent measures were taken; who is managing the event; and, where it applies, the physician's follow-up proposal and the INES level the recognised expert proposes. It ends with the notifier's name and signature and with anything else the Agency asks for. The complete list is in the reference reader; what I want you to hear is that it is built from the facts known at that moment.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Move the case forward: direct contact has succeeded and is r","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Now the written notification, within forty-eight hours of th","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"It ends with the notifier's name and signature and with anyt","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The complete list is in the reference reader; what I want yo","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S10-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S10-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Two phrases carry the whole idea: \"suspected causes\" and \"on the basis of the facts known at that moment\". The initial notification is not the investigation report, and it has its own deadline. On Tuesday afternoon the form is on the desk. Tom's dose is under assessment by the expert; the cause is suspected, the door switch, and not established. Our assistant, who has to type it: \"Shall we wait for the expert's number, or send a short version with just the facts and leave causes and measures blank, so nobody can say we speculated?\"","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Two phrases carry the whole idea: \"suspected causes\" and \"on","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The initial notification is not the investigation report, an","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Tom's dose is under assessment by the expert; the cause is s","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Our assistant, who has to type it: \"Shall we wait for the ex","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S10-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.5-S10-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"The form with two open fields","situation_visible_text":"The written notification is due within forty-eight hours. Tom's dose is under assessment by the expert. The cause is suspected (door switch), not established. The assistant asks whether to wait for the expert's number, or to send a short version with causes and measures left blank.","prompt_spoken_once":"What does the notifier send, and when?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Wait for the expert's dose assessment, because the form has a dose field, and send the complete form as soon as the number is in.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"The expert's study is real and it will produce that number, in the final report, which has its own deadline of two calendar months. The written notification has a different one: forty-eight hours from the event or its discovery, and the regulation says it is based on the facts known at that moment. \"Dose: under assessment by the recognised expert\" is a true and complete entry on Tuesday. Waiting for the number confuses the initial notification with the final report, and misses the forty-eight hours.","screen":"Forty-eight-hour notification is not the final report. Send it with what is known."},"clip":"B1.5-S10-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Send it within forty-eight hours with the known facts, the suspected cause labelled as suspected, the dose marked as under assessment, and the urgent measures taken.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. The regulation asks for the facts known at that moment, for suspected causes, in its own word, and for the urgent measures taken. So the form says what happened, where and when; the X-ray set and the interlock; consequences: one person in the doorway for seconds, dose under assessment by the recognised expert; suspected cause: door switch, not established; measures: exposure stopped, bunker out of use, Tom available, physician informed; who manages the event. Every field true, on time. The dose and the cause follow in the investigation and the final report, which have their own requirements.","screen":"On time, every field true: knowns, suspected cause labelled, dose under assessment, measures taken."},"clip":"B1.5-S10-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Send a short version now with the facts only, leaving causes and measures blank to avoid speculation, and send the full form after the expert's report.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"The wish to keep speculation off a document sent to the regulator is the right wish. The regulation handles it differently: it asks for suspected causes, labelled as such, because a labelled suspicion is a fact about what the notifier thinks and helps the Agency judge the event. And the urgent measures taken are known facts, not speculation; leaving them blank hides exactly what the Agency wants to see first. So the form carries all three, and the final report later replaces \"suspected\" with \"established\".","screen":"Suspected causes, labelled, belong on the form. Measures taken are facts, not speculation."},"clip":"B1.5-S10-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.5-S10-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S10-P1","B1.5-S10-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.5-S10-P2","interaction_id":"B1.5-S10-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S11","title":"No INES rating does not mean no notification","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S11-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Two more things on the extract. First, a trap. Look at criterion one point twenty-two: repeated non-compliance with the deadlines for implementing actions proposed by the recognised expert. Keep all of that wording; it is a precise description and not a label for any late action. For that criterion the table says direct contact not required and INES evaluation no. The written notification within forty-eight hours still applies, because it applies to every event that meets a criterion. \"No\" in one column is always \"no\" for that column only, and the written notification is a column of its own.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Two more things on the extract.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Look at criterion one point twenty-two: repeated non-complia","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"For that criterion the table says direct contact not require","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"\"No\" in one column is always \"no\" for that column only, and ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S11-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S11-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Second, INES, the international scale of nuclear and radiological events. Where the table says yes, or where the Agency so judges, the recognised expert proposes an INES level in the written notification and the Agency approves it. For an event meeting several criteria the level follows the most penalising one. A confirmed level one or higher means the head of the establishment proposes a communication for publication on the Agency's website; level two or higher also means a press release. Daniel does not rate the event, and a low rating says nothing about whether the bunker may be used again; that question has its own answer, two scenes from now.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Second, INES, the international scale of nuclear and radiolo","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Where the table says yes, or where the Agency so judges, the","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"A confirmed level one or higher means the head of the establ","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Daniel does not rate the event, and a low rating says nothin","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S11-P2"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S11-P1","B1.5-S11-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S12","title":"A security event follows its own route","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S12-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"A failed interlock is a safety problem. A different kind of event needs a different route, and it must not get lost inside a technical-fault report. Suppose, in a separate example, that a gamma projector containing a sealed source is found to be missing from the locked storage at a client's site, or that someone has tried to take it. The source is a radioactive substance subject to the security decree you met in the lesson on roles, so three things happen that have nothing to do with interlocks.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"A failed interlock is a safety problem.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"A different kind of event needs a different route, and it mu","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Suppose, in a separate example, that a gamma projector conta","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The source is a radioactive substance subject to the securit","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S12-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S12-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"First, under the security decree, any person who observes a malicious act informs the operator or the delegate for radiological security immediately; that duty belongs to everyone on the site, whatever their title. Second, the operator, or the ARB on the operator's instruction, reports every malicious act and every unauthorised access or attempt at access to the competent police services, and any other security incident the operator judges should go to them. Third, every security incident the operator reports to the police is also reported to the Agency. And after the event, the operator draws up an evaluation report on causes, consequences and additional measures, available to the Agency at all times.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"First, under the security decree, any person who observes a ","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Second, the operator, or the ARB on the operator's instructi","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Third, every security incident the operator reports to the p","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"And after the event, the operator draws up an evaluation rep","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S12-P2"},{"cue":"B1.5-S12-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The Agency's table has rubrics for this. Criterion one bis point two has two branches: acts, threats or attempts of theft, unauthorised possession or malicious use of radioactive substances subject to the decree's security measures; and the loss of such substances if it has been reported to the police under the decree. Direct contact immediately; INES evaluation yes. Read the condition carefully: the police-report condition sits on the loss branch, and the theft-or-threat branch has no such condition. A credible threat is notified immediately; nobody waits for a police file before responding to it. For these security rubrics the ARB may make the notification on the operator's behalf, and a security incident may well also be a safety event, in which case both routes run.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"The Agency's table has rubrics for this.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Direct contact immediately; INES evaluation yes.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Read the condition carefully: the police-report condition si","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"For these security rubrics the ARB may make the notification","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S12-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S12-P1","B1.5-S12-P2","B1.5-S12-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S13","title":"From the first account to the final report, and back to work","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S13-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Back in our bunker, a few weeks on. The expert has studied the circumstances and assessed Tom's dose, and the interlock fault has been found. The work is not finished when the notification has gone. The regulation requires a final report within two calendar months of the event or its discovery, or another period the Agency sets, to the same address. Where the first notification said \"suspected\", this one says \"established\": the causes, the doses, a detailed description. And it adds what the first could not contain: the preventive measures decided to correct every shortcoming and prevent a repeat, the lessons learned and the action plan, and, where it applies, the approval of the recognised expert and of the class seven safety adviser. The full list is in the reference reader.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Back in our bunker, a few weeks on.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The work is not finished when the notification has gone.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Where the first notification said \"suspected\", this one says","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The full list is in the reference reader.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S13-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S13-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"That is a different document from the initial form sent again with a later date. \"Tom will be more careful\" is a sentence about a person; a cause analysis of a failed interlock is a sentence about the installation and why its protection did not work. And an acknowledgement from the Agency does not put the bunker back in service. Return to use follows the correction of the deficiency and the checks our procedure and the expert require: the same logic you met with the failed interlock test in the licensing lesson, with the expert's report now part of it.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"That is a different document from the initial form sent agai","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"\"Tom will be more careful\" is a sentence about a person; a c","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"And an acknowledgement from the Agency does not put the bunk","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Return to use follows the correction of the deficiency and t","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S13-P2"},{"cue":"B1.5-S13-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"One more route, specific to our trade. When radiographers stop a worksite because safe working is not possible and the situation cannot be resolved, our company contacts the Agency immediately under the industrial radiography decree. That is a different trigger from the event table, and it lives in the same procedure, so that whoever opens the procedure on a bad day finds both routes on the same page.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"One more route, specific to our trade.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"When radiographers stop a worksite because safe working is n","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"That is a different trigger from the event table, and it liv","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.5-S13-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S13-P1","B1.5-S13-P2","B1.5-S13-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S14","title":"Correct the draft before it is handed over","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S14-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Let us hand the case to a colleague who has just arrived. They need more than \"it's been dealt with\". Go back to Tuesday afternoon, before the expert's findings; that is the moment a handover is hardest and most useful. A draft handover record is on the desk. Most of its lines are genuine facts from the day: the interlock did not cut the exposure at ten twelve; the exposure was stopped manually and the bunker is out of use; Tom is available and the exposure facts are preserved; dose under assessment by the expert; the physician informed; the expert briefed and confirmed she had the facts; direct contact with the Agency succeeded at twenty to eleven, after a voicemail at twenty past ten; the written notification went this afternoon. And one line reads: \"Cause: sticking door switch.\" Three colleagues have each proposed a correction. Pick the one that makes the record true.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Let us hand the case to a colleague who has just arrived.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Go back to Tuesday afternoon, before the expert's findings; ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Most of its lines are genuine facts from the day: the interl","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Pick the one that makes the record true.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S14-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S14-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"\"Bunker one is out of use after the door interlock failed to cut an exposure at ten twelve; exposure stopped manually. Tom, a workshop fitter with no dosimeter, was in the doorway for seconds; his dose is under assessment by the recognised expert; the physician has been informed. The expert has been briefed and confirmed she has the facts. A voicemail was left on the Agency's duty roster at twenty past ten; direct contact succeeded at twenty to eleven; the written notification went this afternoon. Cause not established; Daniel suspects the door switch, reason noted. Open: cause, Tom's dose, and the checks before return to use.\"","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"\"Bunker one is out of use after the door interlock failed to","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The expert has been briefed and confirmed she has the facts.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"A voicemail was left on the Agency's duty roster at twenty p","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Open: cause, Tom's dose, and the checks before return to use","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S14-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.5-S14-R01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"One line to correct","situation_visible_text":"Draft handover, Tuesday afternoon. Lines: interlock did not cut the exposure at ten twelve; exposure stopped manually, bunker out of use; Tom available, facts preserved; dose under assessment by the expert; physician informed; expert briefed; direct contact with the Agency at twenty to eleven, after a voicemail at twenty past ten; written notification sent; cause: sticking door switch.","prompt_spoken_once":"Which proposed correction makes this handover true?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Replace \"dose under assessment by the expert\" with \"dose: none, Tom felt nothing unusual\", so the record gives a result instead of an open question.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You are right that a handover should be as definite as the facts allow, and every line that can be a result should be. This one cannot yet. Nobody has established Tom's dose; the expert's assessment is under way, and feeling nothing unusual says nothing about dose. \"Under assessment\" is the true and complete line on Tuesday afternoon. The line that actually needs correcting is the cause, which the draft states as a fact while it is still Daniel's suspicion.","screen":"Dose under assessment is the true line. The cause line is the one stated beyond the facts."},"clip":"B1.5-S14-R01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Replace \"direct contact at twenty to eleven\" with \"Agency notified at twenty past ten by voicemail and email\", because that is when the Agency first had the facts.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have remembered the timeline exactly, and the voicemail at twenty past ten belongs in the record, as an attempt. The regulation defines successful direct contact as the oral conversation with the person on duty, and that happened at twenty to eleven. So the draft line is already the true one, and it even keeps the earlier attempt. The line that goes beyond the facts is the cause: a suspicion written as a finding.","screen":"Contact at twenty to eleven is correct, with the attempt noted. The cause line is the error."},"clip":"B1.5-S14-R01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Replace \"cause: sticking door switch\" with \"cause: not established; Daniel suspects the door switch, reason noted\", so the suspicion is labelled as a suspicion.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. Every other line records something that actually happened or is truthfully open: the dose is under assessment, the contact succeeded at twenty to eleven with the earlier attempt noted. The cause line is the one that claims more than anyone knows. Daniel's suspicion is useful and belongs in the record, labelled, with his reason, because it tells the expert where to look first. Written as a finding, it would send the next person to the wrong conclusion and have to be withdrawn later. Here is the handover, read once in full.","screen":"Suspicion labelled as suspicion. Every other line stands."},"clip":"B1.5-S14-R01-c"}],"clip":"B1.5-S14-R01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S14-P1"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.5-S14-P1","interaction_id":"B1.5-S14-R01","post_interaction_cues":["B1.5-S14-P2"]}},{"id":"S15","title":"A clear response does not need to know everything","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.5-S15-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"When something is wrong, a clear response begins with an accurate observation, and here is what you now know about everything that follows it. Three lanes run at once. Lane one, the protective action in your instructions: stop, out of use, facts preserved, the person kept available. Lane two, the information inside our organisation: the agent to the head of service and the expert, the radiographer to his supervisor, the head of service taking the useful measures and warning the physician, the expert studying the circumstances and the dose. Lane three, the statutory notification by the head of the establishment, under the Agency's criteria.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"When something is wrong, a clear response begins with an acc","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Three lanes run at once.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Lane two, the information inside our organisation: the agent","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Lane three, the statutory notification by the head of the es","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S15-P1"},{"cue":"B1.5-S15-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"In that third lane you can now read the table: a criterion is a condition with a deadline beside it, the strictest contact rule governs when several apply, successful direct contact means an oral conversation with the person on duty and nothing less, and the written notification within forty-eight hours is a separate column that says what is known, with suspected causes labelled as such. A \"no\" for INES or for contact never cancels the written notification. Security events follow their own route through the operator or the ARB, the police and the Agency. And the case ends with a final report within two calendar months, with return to use decided by the correction and the checks, not by the Agency's acknowledgement.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"In that third lane you can now read the table: a criterion i","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"A \"no\" for INES or for contact never cancels the written not","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Security events follow their own route through the operator ","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"And the case ends with a final report within two calendar mo","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.5-S15-P2"},{"cue":"B1.5-S15-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Keep the three lanes with you, and keep the habit of writing \"not yet established\" when that is the truth; it is the sentence that kept every record in this lesson honest. In the final lesson of this module we bring the whole Belgian picture together around practical decisions: who is responsible, what evidence is needed, and what to do when the information in front of you is incomplete, with a visiting radiographer, a changed task and a client who would like you to hurry. I'll see you there.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.5 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Keep the three lanes with you, and keep the habit of writing","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"In the final lesson of this module we bring the whole Belgia","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"I'll see you there.","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.5-S15-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.5-S15-P1","B1.5-S15-P2","B1.5-S15-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}}]},{"id":"B1.6","title":"One Thursday: the Belgian framework in practice","scenes":[{"id":"S01","title":"Welcome to the last lesson of this module","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.6-S01-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Welcome back. Over five lessons we have looked at Belgian radiation protection from five directions: why a practice has to be justified, optimised and kept within limits; who does what in and around our company; what the licence, the bunker and the acceptance prove; how protection follows a worker across company lines; and what happens when something is wrong. Today nothing new arrives from the regulation. Instead I want to spend one ordinary Thursday with you, and watch the five lessons turn into decisions.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Welcome back.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Over five lessons we have looked at Belgian radiation protec","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Today nothing new arrives from the regulation.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Instead I want to spend one ordinary Thursday with you, and ","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.6-S01-P1"},{"cue":"B1.6-S01-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"This is practice, not an examination. The day has a job prepared earlier in the week, a client in a hurry to add to it, a visiting radiographer, a worksite that does not behave, and a planner who wants to make next time easier. In each case you will hear the situation and the opinions around it, and then you decide. A good answer explains the reason for a decision; it does not reach for the most reassuring document, and it does not ask for everything to be checked again.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"This is practice, not an examination.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The day has a job prepared earlier in the week, a client in ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"In each case you will hear the situation and the opinions ar","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"A good answer explains the reason for a decision; it does no","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.6-S01-P2"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.6-S01-P1","B1.6-S01-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S02","title":"08:10 - a prepared job, and a client in a hurry","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.6-S02-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Today's job was not born this morning. On Tuesday Bram asked us to radiograph two welds on a large pressure vessel at Havenmeer that had failed its visual inspection. The same afternoon we received, in writing, what the decree requires from him: his justification of the technique, his justification of the location, with the information from his own risk analysis, and the job details, numbers and dimensions included. The decree wants that information at least twenty-four hours before the work, so that we have time to prepare the worksite; we had it on Tuesday for a job on Thursday. As head of service I checked that the technique had been justified by someone competent in the different non-destructive methods, and on Wednesday we completed our own risk analysis.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Today's job was not born this morning.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"On Tuesday Bram asked us to radiograph two welds on a large ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The decree wants that information at least twenty-four hours","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"As head of service I checked that the technique had been jus","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.6-S02-P1"},{"cue":"B1.6-S02-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The location was not decided by habit either. You know the order from the first lesson, and Bram's written assessment walks it: dismantling and transport to a bunker assessed and judged unreasonable for two repair welds on an installed vessel; fixed shielding around the vessel assessed, access, crane traffic, duration, and judged not reasonably feasible. On that documented assessment, plus a risk analysis by the client and by us, the hall is the place, for these two welds, on this vessel. Everything today stands on paper that was written before today.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"The location was not decided by habit either.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"You know the order from the first lesson, and Bram's written","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"On that documented assessment, plus a risk analysis by the c","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Everything today stands on paper that was written before tod","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.6-S02-P2"},{"cue":"B1.6-S02-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Then, at ten past eight, Bram calls again. The visual inspection of the next vessel has thrown up a doubtful nozzle weld. \"You're here anyway. Can you add it today? I'll email you the justification for it within ten minutes, same reasoning as the other two, so you have it in writing.\" Luc, loading the van, likes the idea: same hall, same client, same set. Our planner asks whether a written justification this morning makes the nozzle weld part of today's job. Think about the three questions from the first lesson, and about what the twenty-four hours are for.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Then, at ten past eight, Bram calls again.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"\"You're here anyway.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"I'll email you the justification for it within ten minutes, ","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Think about the three questions from the first lesson, and a","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.6-S02-P3"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.6-S02-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"A third weld, in writing, this morning","situation_visible_text":"Two welds on one vessel were justified and prepared on Tuesday for today. At ten past eight Bram asks to add a nozzle weld on the next vessel and offers to email its written justification within ten minutes. Luc wants to add it; the planner asks whether that makes it today's job.","prompt_spoken_once":"Does Bram's email this morning make the nozzle weld part of today's job?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Yes: with his written justification in hand, the weld is justified, the hall is already justified, and the team is on site, so it can be added today.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have the first question right: once Bram's justification of the technique for the nozzle weld is in writing, the first of the three questions has an answer. The hall, though, was justified for two welds on one vessel, with a perimeter, positions and exposure times calculated for them; a weld on another vessel changes geometry, perimeter and time, and the location assessment and our risk analysis were written for the first vessel. And the decree wants the client's written information at least twenty-four hours before the work, precisely so that this preparation can happen. His email starts that clock; it does not stop it.","screen":"Justification in writing answers question one. Preparation and the twenty-four hours remain."},"clip":"B1.6-S02-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"No: his email today starts the clock; the written information comes at least twenty-four hours before the work, the weld needs its own risk analysis, and it goes to the next slot.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. The decree is specific about timing: the client's correct written information at least twenty-four hours before the work, so that the worksite can be prepared, and neither the client nor the site employer may impose time constraints that prevent us from working safely. A nozzle weld on another vessel is a new assignment: its own technique justification, which Bram is sending, its own location reasoning for that vessel, and our own risk analysis for that geometry. So my answer to Bram is a refusal of the timing, with warmth: send the papers now, and we plan the next slot. Today's two welds go ahead exactly as prepared.","screen":"New assignment: papers today, next slot. Not a refusal of the work, a refusal of the timing."},"clip":"B1.6-S02-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Yes, provided our dose estimate for the extra exposure stays within the perimeter limits we measure at the first exposure this morning.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have reached for the third question, dose limitation, and a forecast below the limit is worth having. It answers one question of the three. It does not justify the new weld's location on another vessel, it does not replace the client's written information in time for the worksite to be prepared, and it does not show how exposure for that weld will be kept as low as reasonably achievable. You met this in the opening lesson: a reassuring number stands in for nothing but itself. The nozzle weld gets its own preparation and its own slot.","screen":"A forecast below a limit answers the third question only. The weld still needs its own preparation."},"clip":"B1.6-S02-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.6-S02-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.6-S02-P1","B1.6-S02-P2","B1.6-S02-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.6-S02-P3","interaction_id":"B1.6-S02-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S03","title":"08:40 - who goes, and who is the agent","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.6-S03-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Planning for the two welds was finished on Wednesday, but one line is open again this morning: Sofia has called in sick, and radiography outside a bunker is done by at least two radiographers. Available are Daniel, and Clara, the subcontracted radiographer you met two lessons ago, who has now been working in our bunker for two weeks and whose instruction record covers the bunker and the bunker X-ray set. Clara has more worksite experience than Daniel, by years.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Planning for the two welds was finished on Wednesday, but on","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Available are Daniel, and Clara, the subcontracted radiograp","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Clara has more worksite experience than Daniel, by years.","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.6-S03-P1"},{"cue":"B1.6-S03-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"The planner proposes: \"Send both, and let Clara be the agent, she has done far more of this.\" Luc, more cautious: \"Daniel is the agent, but Clara can come as second straight away; she's agent-trained and she's been with us two weeks.\" Two proposals, both from people who know the work. Before you choose, think about three things you have learned: who the company may designate as agent on a worksite, what Clara's instruction record actually covers, and who settles the operational protection of an external worker on a job we run.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"The planner proposes: \"Send both, and let Clara be the agent","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Before you choose, think about three things you have learned","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.6-S03-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.6-S03-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"Daniel, Clara, or a colleague from another team","situation_visible_text":"Sofia is ill. Available: Daniel, our radiographer, agent-trained; and Clara, external worker, agent-trained, instructed with us on the bunker and the bunker X-ray set. Today is a client's hall with a portable X-ray set. The planner proposes Clara as agent; Luc proposes Daniel as agent with Clara as second right away.","prompt_spoken_once":"Who goes to Havenmeer, and in which role?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Clara as the agent, because she is agent-trained and far more experienced on worksites, with Daniel as the second radiographer.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Experience is real and it matters for how well the job goes, and Clara's training is real too. The decree still says the company designates the worksite agent from the industrial radiographers present who belong to its own staff and have followed the agent training. Clara is an external worker here, employed by another company; her own employer may designate her on its jobs, and we on ours cannot. So the agent is Daniel, and whether Clara can come at all is the next question.","screen":"The agent is designated from our own staff. Clara is an external worker here."},"clip":"B1.6-S03-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Daniel as the agent, recorded in the planning, and Clara as the second radiographer right away, since she is agent-trained and has been with us for two weeks.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have the agent right, and for the right reason: Daniel is our staff, trained and present, and the designation is recorded in the planning. The second radiographer is where this goes too fast. Clara's instruction with us covers the bunker and the bunker X-ray set; the client's hall with a portable set is a different place, different equipment and a different task, and you learned with her slip for hall two that a changed task asks for instruction for that task. Two weeks in our building does not supply it. So Clara comes as second only after that instruction is arranged, with her employer under our agreement.","screen":"Agent right. Clara's record covers the bunker; the hall needs its own instruction first."},"clip":"B1.6-S03-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Daniel as the agent, recorded in the planning; Clara as the second only after her employer and I arrange the instruction for this task this morning; otherwise a colleague from another team goes.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. Two different rules answer this. The company designates the agent from the industrial radiographers present who belong to its staff and have followed the training: Daniel. And an external worker's instruction covers the task it was given for: Clara's covers the bunker, so the client's hall with the portable set needs its own instruction, which her employer and I settle under our agreement rather than by assuming. Since the job is prepared and the procedure is written, that instruction can be done this morning; if it cannot, Clara stays on the bunker job she was prepared for and a colleague from another team goes. Experience makes a person eligible for things; it does not designate them.","screen":"Daniel: agent, recorded. Clara: second after instruction for this task, or a colleague goes."},"clip":"B1.6-S03-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.6-S03-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.6-S03-P1","B1.6-S03-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.6-S03-P2","interaction_id":"B1.6-S03-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S04","title":"10:30 - before the first exposure","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.6-S04-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"On site, Daniel and Clara set up as the approved procedure says: the perimeter marked out so it can be watched for the whole job, the warning signs placed, Bram named and present as the client's contact person, each radiographer's electronic dosimeter and the survey meter function-tested, and the last-minute risk assessment before the first exposure. Each of those is also one of the agent's frequent and systematic checks, carried out on the basis of a procedure the recognised expert approved, and the record Daniel keeps is his observation on that day.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"On site, Daniel and Clara set up as the approved procedure s","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Each of those is also one of the agent's frequent and system","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.6-S04-P1"},{"cue":"B1.6-S04-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Notice that nothing today has required anyone to approve anything new. The licence, the procedure, the designation, the client's justification and the two risk analyses were all in place before the first exposure. That is what a quiet morning looks like in this trade: the evidence was there before the pressure arrived. Keep that in mind, because the pressure is about to arrive.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Notice that nothing today has required anyone to approve any","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"The licence, the procedure, the designation, the client's ju","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"That is what a quiet morning looks like in this trade: the e","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Keep that in mind, because the pressure is about to arrive.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.6-S04-P2"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.6-S04-P1","B1.6-S04-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S05","title":"11:40 - the worksite does not behave","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.6-S05-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Then the morning stops being quiet. Twice in ten minutes, plant workers walk across the perimeter line to reach a store behind the hall, ignoring the signs and Clara at the boundary. Bram has gone to take a call. Daniel has not started the exposure. The dose rate at the line, measured at the test exposure, was low, well under the limit for the occupancy there.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Then the morning stops being quiet.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Twice in ten minutes, plant workers walk across the perimete","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Daniel has not started the exposure.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The dose rate at the line, measured at the test exposure, wa","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.6-S05-P1"},{"cue":"B1.6-S05-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"On the phone, Luc offers two ways out: \"Wait till Bram's back, then go; the contact person being there is the condition, and the crossings will stop when he's standing there.\" Or: \"Ask their safety officer to post someone at the line and get on with it, report to Emilia tonight.\" Clara, at the boundary, thinks the low reading at the line should settle it. Daniel has a decision that does not need a meeting, and you know the rules he has: what the decree tells a radiographer to do when safe working is not possible, whom he tells and when, and what the site employer owes him.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"On the phone, Luc offers two ways out: \"Wait till Bram's bac","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Daniel has a decision that does not need a meeting, and you ","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.6-S05-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.6-S05-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"Two crossings, the contact person away","situation_visible_text":"Plant workers have crossed the perimeter twice in ten minutes. Bram, the client's contact person, is away on a call. The exposure has not started. The dose rate at the line was low at the test exposure. Luc proposes waiting for Bram or asking the plant's safety officer to post someone; Clara points to the low reading.","prompt_spoken_once":"What does Daniel do now?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Hold the radiography and report at once, with the reason, to Luc, to me and to Bram; resume only after the client has restored control of the route and the team has verified the perimeter and the measures again.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. The decree gives it to him in one sentence: industrial radiographers stop the radiography when it cannot be carried out safely, and they report that immediately, with the reason, to their hierarchical superior, to the head of the physical control service and to the client's contact person. As agent he also informs the service, which informs the expert. The decree also places a duty on the site: the responsible employer makes sure his own staff and third parties respect the safety measures, and the contact person is reachable throughout. So Bram hears it too, and closes the route; then Daniel and Clara verify the perimeter and the measures under the procedure before anyone resumes. And if it cannot be resolved, the company contacts the Agency immediately.","screen":"Hold; report with the reason to Luc, Emilia, Bram; resume after the client restores control and the team verifies."},"clip":"B1.6-S05-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Hold until Bram is back and then start, because the contact person being present is the condition, and the crossings will stop while he stands there.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have kept the exposure held, and that is the first half of the decree's sentence. The second half is the report: immediately, with the reason, to Luc, to me and to Bram. Bram being back is welcome, and it is his job to make his staff respect the measures, with a closed route rather than a man standing there. What makes the restart possible is the verification: the team checks that the perimeter can be held along its whole length and the measures are in place, then resumes under the procedure. Waiting for Bram alone skips the report and the check.","screen":"Hold is right. Report now, let the client close the route, verify before resuming."},"clip":"B1.6-S05-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"Ask the plant's safety officer to post someone at the line, start the exposure, and report the crossings to me at the end of the day.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have reached for the site's own people, and that instinct is partly right: respect for the measures is the site employer's duty. The way to get it is through the client's contact person, whom the decree wants reachable throughout, and not through a start while the route is still open. Safe working was not possible twice in ten minutes, so the decree's answer is to stop and report immediately, with the reason, to the three people it names. The report at the end of the day is a day late, and the low reading at the line says nothing about someone walking inside it.","screen":"Not possible to work safely: stop and report now, to the three people named. No start with an open route."},"clip":"B1.6-S05-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.6-S05-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.6-S05-P1","B1.6-S05-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.6-S05-P2","interaction_id":"B1.6-S05-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S06","title":"12:00 - the handover, and what it is not","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.6-S06-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Daniel's call to me is the handover you have practised twice: \"Two plant workers crossed the perimeter twice; the contact person was away; I have not started the exposure and the radiography is on hold; I've told Luc, and Bram has just called back; I don't know yet whether the plant can keep the route closed.\" Observed, done, contacted, unknown. No exposure has occurred, nobody has been in a beam, and nothing has failed. My side of the call: I note the stop and its reason, I make sure the expert hears through our service, and I tell Daniel what has to be true before anyone resumes.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Daniel's call to me is the handover you have practised twice","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"No exposure has occurred, nobody has been in a beam, and not","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"My side of the call: I note the stop and its reason, I make ","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.6-S06-P1"},{"cue":"B1.6-S06-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Keep the lanes apart here too. This is a stopped worksite with a reason, the decree's route. Whether it is also a significant event under the Agency's criteria is for the responsible assessment with the expert; Daniel does not classify it, and nobody writes \"Agency notified\" because a phone call was made to me. By half past twelve Bram has closed the route with a locked gate and posted someone at it. That is the client's part. Ours is to verify rather than to take his word for it: Daniel and Clara check that the perimeter can be watched along its whole length and that the safety measures from the risk analyses are in place, they repeat the last-minute risk assessment, and Daniel confirms to me that safe working is possible again. Only then does the radiography resume under the procedure. The stop, its reason and the verification go into our records, and I note it for the expert's next visit.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Keep the lanes apart here too.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Whether it is also a significant event under the Agency's cr","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Ours is to verify rather than to take his word for it: Danie","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"The stop, its reason and the verification go into our record","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.6-S06-P2"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.6-S06-P1","B1.6-S06-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S07","title":"15:00 - the planner wants to make next time easier","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.6-S07-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Back in the office, the planner has an idea born of a stressful morning: \"That hall is fine now, the gate, the layout, the routes, we know it all. Can we put Havenmeer's hall on a list of approved locations, so next time we skip the justification?\" Luc adds: \"Or ask our expert to approve the hall once, and we're covered for the future.\" I understand the wish; the morning was long.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Back in the office, the planner has an idea born of a stress","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Can we put Havenmeer's hall on a list of approved locations,","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.6-S07-P1"},{"cue":"B1.6-S07-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Before you answer them, look at what you know about location justification: who gives it, for what, and what today's dossier actually contains. And remember that the next workpiece at Havenmeer may be a movable casting rather than an installed vessel.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Before you answer them, look at what you know about location","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"And remember that the next workpiece at Havenmeer may be a m","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.6-S07-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.6-S07-Q01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"A list of approved locations?","situation_visible_text":"The planner wants Havenmeer's hall on a list of approved locations so future jobs skip the justification. Luc suggests having our recognised expert approve the hall once. Today's dossier holds the location justification for this vessel, with both options assessed.","prompt_spoken_once":"What do I answer the planner and Luc?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Yes to the list: the hall was justified once with both options assessed, so the justification attaches to the hall and later jobs there can rely on it.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"You have read today's dossier correctly: both options were assessed, with reasons, and that is exactly what made the hall the place today. The justification, though, attaches to the type of assignment, by the client, in writing, and today's reasoning was about this installed vessel. A movable casting that fits within one cubic metre and weighs under five hundred kilograms goes to a bunker whatever the hall looks like, and for anything else the feasibility reasoning starts again. So no list; today's dossier is kept, because it makes the next review faster.","screen":"Justification attaches to the type of assignment, by the client. No standing list."},"clip":"B1.6-S07-Q01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"No list and no standing approval: the client justifies the location in writing for each type of assignment; we keep today's dossier so the next review is faster.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Exactly. The decree places the location justification on the client, in writing, for each type of assignment, with his risk-analysis information for our own analysis; our part is to assess it, do our risk analysis, and refuse if it does not hold. A vessel fixed in the hall today says nothing about a casting next month, which, if it is movable and within the size and weight, goes to a bunker. What we can do, and should, is keep today's dossier: the layout, the routes, the gate that solved our problem. That makes the next justification and risk analysis quicker to review. It is good practice, and it is not an approval.","screen":"Per type of assignment, by the client, in writing. Dossier helps; it does not replace."},"clip":"B1.6-S07-Q01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"A list is possible if our recognised expert approves the hall once; her approval of the location then covers future jobs there.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"The recognised expert does approve real things, and you have met them: procedures, risk analyses, acceptances. Justifying a client's location is not among them; that duty sits with the client, in writing, for each type of assignment, and moving it to our expert would misplace the responsibility and still not make it standing, because the next assignment may be a different workpiece with a different answer. So the expert approves our procedures, the client justifies his location, and the planner keeps the dossier.","screen":"The expert approves procedures and acceptances. The client justifies the location, each time."},"clip":"B1.6-S07-Q01-c"}],"clip":"B1.6-S07-Q01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.6-S07-P1","B1.6-S07-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.6-S07-P2","interaction_id":"B1.6-S07-Q01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S08","title":"The same reasoning with a sealed source","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.6-S08-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Today's job used a portable X-ray set. Most of the decisions would have been the same with a gamma projector: the client's justifications, the twenty-four-hour information, the designation of the agent, the specific instruction for a changed task, stopping when the perimeter cannot be held. Here is the transfer in one decision. Imagine the same client and the same vessel, but the welds need gamma radiography, and the projector will stay on Bram's site overnight in temporary storage.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Today's job used a portable X-ray set.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Most of the decisions would have been the same with a gamma ","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"Here is the transfer in one decision.","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Imagine the same client and the same vessel, but the welds n","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.6-S08-P1"},{"cue":"B1.6-S08-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"Three colleagues each raise what they think is the new question. Daniel: \"Does my designation as agent now also cover the security of the source, since I'm the agent on site?\" Luc: \"The projector's container is shielded, so can Bram skip the location justification this time?\" And the planner, who remembers a lesson: \"Which security responsibilities apply to that source on Bram's site overnight, and who has to be told if something looks wrong there?\" One of the three has found the question that is actually new with a sealed source.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"Three colleagues each raise what they think is the new quest","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Daniel: \"Does my designation as agent now also cover the sec","show":"Focus 2"}],"clip":"B1.6-S08-P2"}],"interaction":{"id":"B1.6-S08-R01","type":"single_choice","reviewed_b14_b16":true,"title_visible":"What is new with a sealed source?","situation_visible_text":"Same client, same vessel, now with a gamma projector that stays on the client's site overnight in temporary storage. Daniel asks whether his designation covers security; Luc asks whether the shielded container lets the client skip the location justification; the planner asks which security responsibilities apply overnight and who is informed.","prompt_spoken_once":"Which of the three has found the question that is new with a sealed source?","options":[{"id":"a","text":"Daniel's: whether his agent designation now also covers security, since he is the agent on site.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"Daniel's designation is real and it continues with a gamma projector: his checks on the equipment and the perimeter are the same. It is a radiation-protection designation by the company, and you saw in the lesson on roles that security responsibilities belong to the operator and its delegate for radiological security, an appointment the Agency approves. So Daniel's question has an answer you already know: no, and it was not new. The planner's question is the one that opens with the source.","screen":"Agent is radiation protection. The ARB is a separate appointment. Not the new question."},"clip":"B1.6-S08-R01-a"},{"id":"b","text":"Luc's: whether the client can skip the location justification, because the projector's container is shielded.","correct":false,"feedback":{"spoken":"The projector's shielded container is one of the protection means, and it matters for the dose outside it. It changes nothing about the decree's rule that the client justifies the location in writing for each type of assignment; that applied to the X-ray job this morning and applies here too. So Luc's question has the same answer as this afternoon's, and the sealed source did not change it. The question that is new is about security.","screen":"Shielding is a protection means. Location justification still applies. Not the new question."},"clip":"B1.6-S08-R01-b"},{"id":"c","text":"The planner's: which security responsibilities apply to this source on the client's site and overnight, and who is informed, the operator or its delegate for radiological security.","correct":true,"feedback":{"spoken":"Yes. A gamma projector holds a radioactive substance, so the security decree applies to it, including during temporary work on the client's site and overnight storage: the operator's delegate for radiological security, the duty of anyone who sees a malicious act to inform the operator or the ARB at once, and the police-and-Agency route for security incidents. All of today's radiation-protection decisions stay in force beside it, unchanged. What the arrangements are for this source on this site is for the ARB and the operator to settle; recognising that the question exists is what this lesson asks of you.","screen":"Security decree applies to the source. ARB and the reporting route. Protection reasoning unchanged."},"clip":"B1.6-S08-R01-c"}],"clip":"B1.6-S08-R01"},"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.6-S08-P1","B1.6-S08-P2"],"interaction_after_cue":"B1.6-S08-P2","interaction_id":"B1.6-S08-R01","post_interaction_cues":[]}},{"id":"S09","title":"What the module has given you","paragraphs":[{"cue":"B1.6-S09-P1","speaker":"Emilia","text":"That was one Thursday. Look back at what you used. From the opening lesson, the three questions, and the rule that the client justifies technique and location in writing while we check and refuse when a justification does not hold, with the decree's twenty-four hours for the written job information. From the lesson on people, the designation of the agent from our own trained staff, and the difference between a check record and an approval. From the licence lesson, what a bunker is and that a certificate has a date and a scope, and the location order that sends a movable casting to a bunker whatever the hall looks like.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"That was one Thursday.","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Look back at what you used.","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"From the lesson on people, the designation of the agent from","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"From the licence lesson, what a bunker is and that a certifi","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.6-S09-P1"},{"cue":"B1.6-S09-P2","speaker":"Emilia","text":"From the external-worker lesson, that Clara's experience does not make her our agent and that her instruction covers the task it was given for. From the lesson on things going wrong, the stop-and-report duty, the three people who hear about it, the verification before anyone resumes, the company's route to the Agency when a stop cannot be resolved, and the discipline of saying what is not yet known. And from the security decree, one question that arrives with every sealed source and with nothing else.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"From the external-worker lesson, that Clara's experience doe","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"From the lesson on things going wrong, the stop-and-report d","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"And from the security decree, one question that arrives with","show":"Focus 3"}],"clip":"B1.6-S09-P2"},{"cue":"B1.6-S09-P3","speaker":"Emilia","text":"A good decision is neither a permanent yes nor a permanent no. It connects a particular conclusion to particular evidence and to the people who hold the next responsibility. Finishing this module does not designate you as an agent, authorise an installation or replace the practical experience, the workplace instruction and the medical surveillance that real work requires; you know by now exactly which documents would show those things. The rest of the course turns to the science behind the decisions: what radiation is, how it interacts with matter and with people, and how we measure it. Keep one question with you into those lessons: what does this information actually allow me to conclude? Thank you for working through this module with me.","screen_text":[],"characters":[],"documents":[],"equipment":[],"start_visual":"Reviewed B1.6 scenario","beats":[{"at":"A good decision is neither a permanent yes nor a permanent n","show":"Focus 1"},{"at":"Finishing this module does not designate you as an agent, au","show":"Focus 2"},{"at":"The rest of the course turns to the science behind the decis","show":"Focus 3"},{"at":"Thank you for working through this module with me.","show":"Focus 4"}],"clip":"B1.6-S09-P3"}],"sequence":{"cues_before_interaction":["B1.6-S09-P1","B1.6-S09-P2","B1.6-S09-P3"],"interaction_after_cue":null,"interaction_id":null,"post_interaction_cues":[]}}]}]};
